{"parentUuid":"753eb417-3901-4b42-9dc8-17179bf6e604","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01G6UgXyrN6EUCo59CTpe916","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Locked. Single rule everywhere: no timeout unless user asks. This actually lets us drop one mechanism from #964 — the idle watchdog — since its only job was distinguishing \"stuck\" vs \"slow\" inside an automatic cap that no longer exists. We get the same diagnostic by inspecting captured streaming state at the (user-set) wall-clock cap.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- The idle watchdog and the wall-clock cap were two cancellation mechanisms in #964 to support a default deadline. With opt-in-only, you've collapsed that to one: the user's wall cap (or no cap). Diagnostic distinguishability still works because we have the *captured stream state*, not just a fired/didn't-fire boolean.\n- That means the goroutine + atomic.Int64 + `startIdleWatchdog` machinery from #964 doesn't need to come along. Simpler code path.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n## Section 2 — Streaming capability and Claude implementation\n\nPort from #964 with provider-neutral renaming:\n\n**`agent/agent.go`** — new interface alongside `TextGenerator`:\n\n```go\ntype ProgressPhase string\nconst (\n    PhaseConnecting   ProgressPhase = \"connecting\"\n    PhaseFirstToken   ProgressPhase = \"first-token\"\n    PhaseGenerating   ProgressPhase = \"generating\"\n    PhaseDone         ProgressPhase = \"done\"\n)\n\ntype GenerationProgress struct {\n    Phase             ProgressPhase\n    OutputTokens      int  // running estimate during Generating; final at Done\n    InputTokens       int  // populated at FirstToken\n    CachedInputTokens int  // populated at FirstToken\n    TTFTms            int  // populated at FirstToken\n    DurationMs        int  // populated at Done\n}\n\ntype ProgressFn func(GenerationProgress)\n\ntype StreamingTextGenerator interface {\n    Agent\n    GenerateTextStreaming(ctx context.Context, prompt, model string, progress ProgressFn) (string, error)\n}\n```\n\n**`agent/capabilities.go`** — capability detection: `AsStreamingTextGenerator(ag) (StreamingTextGenerator, bool)` that respects `DeclaredCaps.StreamingTextGenerator` for external agents.\n\n**`agent/claudecode/generate_streaming.go`** (new): invokes `claude --print --output-format stream-json --verbose --model <m>`, pipes stdout through NDJSON parser, dispatches progress callbacks per phase. If CLI stderr looks like \"unrecognized option\" + a streaming flag name → **falls back to non-streaming** `GenerateText` (no progress).\n\n**`agent/claudecode/response.go`** — `streamClaudeResponse(r, onEvent)` + event types from #964 (4MB line buffer, skip malformed lines, return final result event). Test fixtures `stream_success.jsonl` + `stream_error_404.jsonl`.\n\n**Other providers** (Codex, Gemini, OpenCode, Factory): not modified. They don't implement `StreamingTextGenerator`. The `AsStreamingTextGenerator` check returns false → call site falls back to `TextGenerator.GenerateText` as today. No regression. They simply don't get live progress, and on timeout we use their captured stderr for diagnostic instead.\n\n## Section 3 — Progress UI (provider-neutral)\n\nThree rendering modes, picked from one `summaryProgressWriter`:\n\n**TTY, non-accessible** (in-place line):\n```\nGenerating checkpoint summary... (transcript: 47.0 KB, provider: claude-code)\n→ Sending request to provider...\n→ Provider responded (TTFT 1.9s, 35.9k cached input tokens) -- generating...\n→ Writing summary... (~1.2k tokens)         ← updates in place\n✓ Summary generated (3.1s, 1.9k output tokens)\n```\n\n**Non-TTY (CI, piped):** same lines, no `\\r` updates, one line per event.\n\n**`ACCESSIBLE=1`:** no ANSI escape sequences at all; one line per event.\n\n**Provider-neutral wording**: the phase strings don't name \"Anthropic\" or \"Claude\". They say \"Sending request to provider…\" / \"Provider responded…\". On non-streaming providers, only the initial \"Generating checkpoint summary...\" line prints, then silence until done/fail. That's honest — we have no events to display.\n\n## Section 4 — Diagnostic on timeout (this is the key fix you flagged)\n\nWhen the user-set wall-clock cap fires, the error message is built from observable state:\n\n| State captured before kill | Error message |\n|---|---|\n| Stream-capable provider, never reached `PhaseConnecting` | `\"timed out after Xs: provider never produced output (CLI may be stalled, network unreachable, or wrong binary on PATH)\"` |\n| Stream-capable, reached `PhaseConnecting` only | `\"timed out after Xs: provider sent request but did not get a response (network/firewall/provider API issue)\"` |\n| Stream-capable, reached `PhaseFirstToken` but not `PhaseDone` | `\"timed out after Xs: model started responding but did not finish (transcript may be too large for the cap; raise --summary-timeout-seconds or pick a faster model)\"` |\n| Non-streaming provider, no stdout bytes captured | `\"timed out after Xs: <provider> produced no output (CLI may be stalled, network unreachable, or wrong binary on PATH)\"` |\n| Non-streaming provider, stdout bytes captured | `\"timed out after Xs: <provider> was generating output when killed. Captured stderr: <verbatim>\"` |\n\nAny non-empty stderr from the subprocess is **always surfaced verbatim** in the structured rows — even on success-but-malformed-response and even when the cap fires. Today it gets swallowed by `cmd.Run()` error wrapping; we explicitly preserve and render it.\n\nCancel (Ctrl+C) is treated separately and stays minimal: `\"summary generation canceled\"`.\n\nThe current 3-cause shrug message goes away.\n\n## Section 5 — Threading the callback\n\n`summarize.GenerateFromTranscript` grows one param: `ProgressFn` (may be `nil`).\n- `explain.go` (`generateCheckpointAISummary`) passes the `summaryProgressWriter.handle`.\n- `strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go` (the post-commit auto-summary path) passes `nil` — no live UI in hot path.\n\n`summarize/claude.go` (`ClaudeGenerator.Generate`) checks `AsStreamingTextGenerator(claudeAgent)`. If yes, calls `GenerateTextStreaming`. If no (old CLI or fell back), calls existing `GenerateText`.\n\n## Section 6 — Backward compat\n\n- `--summary-timeout-seconds` flag (added by #1204) — kept.\n- `summary_timeout_seconds` setting — kept.\n- `entire configure --summarize-timeout-seconds N` — kept.\n- `defaultCheckpointSummaryTimeout = 5min` constant → **removed**. No automatic default anymore. Lock-in test `TestDefaultCheckpointSummaryTimeout_IsFiveMinutes` from #1204 → replaced with `TestNoAutomaticTimeoutDefault`.\n- `resolveSummaryTimeout(...)` from #1204 — kept, but its \"fall through to package default\" branch now returns `0` (no deadline) instead of `5*time.Minute`.\n- Callers of `generateCheckpointAISummary` interpret `timeout == 0` as \"no `context.WithTimeout`; pass parent context through unchanged.\"\n\n## Section 7 — Testing\n\n- Unit: `streamClaudeResponse` against `stream_success.jsonl` and `stream_error_404.jsonl`. Malformed-line skipping. Result-only events. Empty stream.\n- Unit: `ClaudeCodeAgent.GenerateTextStreaming` with mocked `CommandRunner` — stub stdin/stdout/stderr fixtures.\n- Unit: `summaryProgressWriter` rendering tests for TTY/non-TTY/accessible modes against fixed event sequences.\n- Unit: `resolveSummaryTimeout` returns 0 when both flag and setting are unset (new behavior).\n- Unit: error message tests for each of the 5 diagnostic states in Section 4.\n- Integration: existing `TestGenerateCheckpointAISummary_*` updated for the new no-default-timeout semantics.\n- Vogon canary: no changes needed (doesn't exercise summary streaming).\n\n---\n\nBefore I write the spec, please flag anything in sections 2–7 you want different. In particular:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input