{"parentUuid":"a17fa805-28dd-4da3-8313-31fb2f226b15","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JDaU7HZh51dXLP5sFMQ1S8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MKzouP1Ck8QZYFx3UuMXPw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-13-explain-summary-streaming-design.md","content":"# `entire explain --generate` — streaming progress and meaningful timeout diagnostics\n\n**Date:** 2026-05-13\n**Status:** Spec — implementation plan to follow via `superpowers:writing-plans`\n**Builds on:** PR #1204 (merged on `main` at `cc178b537`)\n**Replaces:** PR #964 (draft) — this spec ports its mechanics on top of #1204's surface, drops the idle watchdog, and fixes the multi-provider regressions in its progress UI\n\n## Problem\n\nAfter PR #1204 landed:\n\n- The hardcoded 30s `--generate` timeout is gone. Default is 5min, overridable per-run with `--summary-timeout-seconds N` and per-project with `summary_timeout_seconds` setting.\n- Two issues remain.\n\n**Issue A — Meaningful failures.** When a timeout fires today, the user gets a single `context.DeadlineExceeded` and a three-cause shrug message (\"model slow / can't reach API / API degraded\"). The code can't tell which it is because it observes only \"wall clock elapsed\", not subprocess behavior. Origin: PR #876 (Apr 8 2026) added a wall-clock cap as a Claude-CLI stall-guard back when Claude was the only summary provider. Multi-provider summary generation (PR #1044, Apr 27 2026) expanded the surface under the cap without revisiting the diagnostic story. Users today debug network problems when the real issue is a legitimately slow generation, and vice versa.\n\n**Issue B — Silent wait.** Between \"Generating checkpoint summary...\" and \"✓ done\", the user sees nothing. On a 90-second summary with a real provider, that looks indistinguishable from a hang.\n\n## Goals\n\n1. Eliminate the automatic deadline default. Make timeouts opt-in only via #1204's existing surface.\n2. When a user-set timeout fires, classify the failure from observable subprocess state, not a generic sentinel. Surface any captured stderr verbatim.\n3. Show live progress on TTY when the provider supports streaming. Stay quiet (but correct) when it doesn't.\n4. Preserve PR #1204's contract: `--summary-timeout-seconds` and `summary_timeout_seconds` continue to work, on both TTY and non-TTY, with the same precedence (flag > setting > default).\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Streaming for non-Claude providers (Codex, Gemini, OpenCode, Factory). They keep their existing non-streaming path; only the diagnostic on their timeouts improves.\n- New configuration knobs. No `summary_idle_seconds`, no `summary_max_wall_seconds`. One number, opt-in.\n- TUI components. Progress is a single line that updates in place on TTY; otherwise one line per phase event.\n- Changes to the auto-summary path (`strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`). It passes `nil` progress and keeps its current deadline policy.\n\n## Deadline policy\n\nOne rule applies on TTY and CI alike:\n\n| User setting / flag | Effective deadline |\n|---|---|\n| Unset (default) | None — provider call inherits parent context unmodified |\n| `summary_timeout_seconds: N` or `--summary-timeout-seconds N` | Wall-clock cap = N seconds |\n\nPR #1204's `resolveSummaryTimeout(ctx, flagSeconds)` is preserved with one change: the package-default fallback returns `0` (no deadline) instead of `5*time.Minute`. The constant `defaultCheckpointSummaryTimeout = 5 * time.Minute` is removed; `checkpointSummaryTimeout` test-injection var is retired in favor of dependency-injection of `resolveSummaryTimeout` itself.\n\nThe idle watchdog from #964 (`startIdleWatchdog`, atomic.Int64 activity tracking, separate cancellation goroutine) is **not** ported. Its sole job was distinguishing \"stuck\" from \"slow\" inside an automatic default; with no automatic default that distinction is recovered from captured stream state at the wall-clock cap, without a second cancellation mechanism.\n\n## Streaming capability\n\nNew optional capability interface alongside `agent.TextGenerator`, declared in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go`:\n\n```go\ntype ProgressPhase string\nconst (\n    PhaseConnecting ProgressPhase = \"connecting\"\n    PhaseFirstToken ProgressPhase = \"first-token\"\n    PhaseGenerating ProgressPhase = \"generating\"\n    PhaseDone       ProgressPhase = \"done\"\n)\n\ntype GenerationProgress struct {\n    Phase             ProgressPhase\n    OutputTokens      int  // running estimate during Generating; final at Done\n    InputTokens       int  // populated at FirstToken\n    CachedInputTokens int  // populated at FirstToken\n    TTFTms            int  // populated at FirstToken\n    DurationMs        int  // populated at Done\n}\n\ntype ProgressFn func(GenerationProgress)\n\ntype StreamingTextGenerator interface {\n    Agent\n    GenerateTextStreaming(ctx context.Context, prompt, model string, progress ProgressFn) (string, error)\n}\n```\n\n`agent/capabilities.go` adds:\n\n- `DeclaredCaps.StreamingTextGenerator bool`\n- `AsStreamingTextGenerator(ag Agent) (StreamingTextGenerator, bool)` — type-asserts and respects declared capabilities for external agents.\n\nTests in `agent/capabilities_test.go` cover the four cases (not implemented / built-in implementer / declarer true / declarer false), mirroring the pattern already used for `AsTextGenerator`.\n\n## Claude streaming implementation\n\nNew file `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/generate_streaming.go`:\n\n```go\nfunc (c *ClaudeCodeAgent) GenerateTextStreaming(\n    ctx context.Context, prompt, model string, progress agent.ProgressFn,\n) (string, error)\n```\n\nInvokes:\n\n```\nclaude --print --output-format stream-json --verbose --model <model> --setting-sources \"\"\n```\n\nstdin is the prompt. stdout is piped through `streamClaudeResponse` (NDJSON decoder, 4 MiB line buffer, skip malformed lines, return final `result` event). stderr is buffered.\n\nPer-event dispatch:\n\n- `system.subtype=status, status=requesting` → `PhaseConnecting`\n- `stream_event.event.type=message_start` → `PhaseFirstToken` (carrying TTFT and cache token counts)\n- `stream_event.event.type=content_block_delta` → `PhaseGenerating` with a running ~4-char-per-token output estimate\n- `result` event with `is_error=false` → `PhaseDone` (with `duration_ms` and final `output_tokens`)\n- `result` event with `is_error=true` → returned as a `*claudecode.ClaudeError` so PR #963's classifier still maps it to actionable kinds (auth/rate-limit/config/etc.)\n\nIf the CLI rejects the streaming flags (older Claude install), stderr contains a rejection phrase (`unrecognized option` / `unknown flag` / `invalid option`) combined with a streaming flag name (`stream-json` / `verbose`). On that signal, `GenerateTextStreaming` falls back to `GenerateText` and logs the fallback at WARN. No progress events fire; the rest of the path is unaffected.\n\nStdout is drained with `io.Copy(io.Discard, ...)` after the scanner stops, so a blocked pipe can't deadlock `cmd.Wait()`. Drain errors are logged at DEBUG (stdout is closing anyway).\n\nStream parsing types (`streamEvent`, `streamInnerEvent`, `streamDelta`, `streamMessage`) live in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/response.go`. Fixtures `testdata/stream_success.jsonl` and `testdata/stream_error_404.jsonl`.\n\nThe ClaudeCodeAgent struct gains `DeclaredCapabilities().StreamingTextGenerator = true`.\n\n## Wiring through `summarize`\n\n`summarize.GenerateFromTranscript` adds one parameter:\n\n```go\nfunc GenerateFromTranscript(\n    ctx context.Context,\n    transcriptBytes redact.RedactedBytes,\n    filesTouched []string,\n    agentType types.AgentType,\n    generator Generator,\n    progress agent.ProgressFn,  // new; may be nil\n) (*checkpoint.Summary, error)\n```\n\n`summarize.Generator.Generate` is not changed. The progress threading lives at one level up:\n\n`summarize.ClaudeGenerator.Generate(ctx, input)` is changed: it accesses its underlying agent via `AsStreamingTextGenerator`. If available, it calls `GenerateTextStreaming` and forwards the `ProgressFn` it received from `GenerateFromTranscript` (carried on a new field of `ClaudeGenerator` or via a closure — implementation plan picks the cleaner shape). If not available, falls back to current `GenerateText`.\n\nNon-Claude generators (`CodexGenerator`, `GeminiGenerator`, etc.) keep their current `Generate` body. They never produce progress events; the `summaryProgressWriter` simply renders the initial \"Generating checkpoint summary...\" line and waits.\n\nExisting call sites:\n\n- `explain.go:generateCheckpointAISummary` → passes `progressWriter.handle` as `progress`.\n- `strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go:generateSummary` → passes `nil`.\n\n## Progress UI\n\nNew `summaryProgressWriter` in `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go`:\n\n- Constructor `newSummaryProgressWriter(w io.Writer)` detects TTY via `isTerminalWriter(w)` and `IsAccessibleMode()`.\n- Renders three modes:\n  - **TTY, non-accessible:** `\\r` + ANSI clear-line to update the in-progress \"Writing summary…\" line; final lines append normally.\n  - **Non-TTY:** plain `Fprintln`, one line per event, no deduplication of `PhaseGenerating` updates beyond the existing throttling (which the implementation plan will spec — likely \"emit one update per 500ms or per 25% output-token jump, whichever first\").\n  - **Accessible mode:** as non-TTY, but additionally strips ANSI styling from glyphs (uses ASCII `->` and `*` instead of `→` and `✓`).\n- Provider-neutral phrasing — no \"Anthropic\" or \"Claude\" hardcoded:\n  - Connecting: `\"→ Sending request to provider...\"`\n  - First-token: `\"→ Provider responded (TTFT 1.9s, 35.9k cached input tokens) -- generating...\"`\n  - Generating: `\"→ Writing summary... (~1.2k tokens)\"`\n  - Done: `\"✓ Summary generated (3.1s, 1.9k output tokens)\"`\n- The initial pre-stream line widens slightly to include the provider name resolved from settings: `\"Generating checkpoint summary... (transcript: 47.0 KB, provider: claude-code)\"`. Provider name comes from the `SummaryProvider` already resolved in `generateCheckpointSummary`.\n\nHelpers `formatMs`, `formatTokenCount`, `humanizeBytes` come from #964 verbatim.\n\n## Diagnostic on timeout\n\nThe most important change. Today's `formatCheckpointSummaryError` has a `case errors.Is(err, context.DeadlineExceeded):` branch that emits a hardcoded three-cause list. That branch is rewritten to consume **captured state** from the failed run.\n\nA new struct `summaryAttempt` accumulates state during the call:\n\n```go\ntype summaryAttempt struct {\n    streaming        bool          // did we use GenerateTextStreaming?\n    phasesReached    map[agent.ProgressPhase]bool\n    lastPhase        agent.ProgressPhase\n    stderrCaptured   string        // bytes captured from subprocess stderr\n    stdoutByteCount  int           // total bytes seen on stdout (for non-streaming providers)\n    deadline         time.Duration // the user-set cap that fired\n    provider         types.AgentName\n}\n```\n\n`summaryProgressWriter.handle` updates `phasesReached`. Non-streaming providers don't fire callbacks, so `phasesReached` stays empty and `streaming` stays false; `stderrCaptured` and `stdoutByteCount` come from the generator. (This requires the non-streaming `Generate` paths to expose stderr — many already capture it; PR #963 normalized stderr access on Claude. For Codex/Gemini/OpenCode/Factory, the `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI` shared helper already captures stderr; we surface it through the error chain.)\n\nAt `DeadlineExceeded`, message resolution:\n\n| State at timeout | Error label | Detail rows |\n|---|---|---|\n| `streaming && !phasesReached[Connecting]` | `\"Timed out after Xs: provider never sent its request\"` | `cause: CLI may be stalled before subprocess startup` ; `try: run \\`<provider