hrough the error chain.)\n\nAt `DeadlineExceeded`, message resolution:\n\n| State at timeout | Error label | Detail rows |\n|---|---|---|\n| `streaming && !phasesReached[Connecting]` | `\"Timed out after Xs: provider never sent its request\"` | `cause: CLI may be stalled before subprocess startup` ; `try: run \\`<provider-cli>\\` directly to confirm it works` |\n| `streaming && phasesReached[Connecting] && !phasesReached[FirstToken]` | `\"Timed out after Xs: provider sent request but received no response\"` | `cause: network/firewall, provider API degraded, or auth check stuck` ; `try: \\`<provider-cli> --version\\` and a small manual call` |\n| `streaming && phasesReached[FirstToken] && !phasesReached[Done]` | `\"Timed out after Xs: model responded but did not finish\"` | `transcript: <size>` ; `cap: <duration>` ; `try: raise --summary-timeout-seconds or pick a faster model` |\n| `!streaming && stdoutByteCount == 0` | `\"Timed out after Xs: <provider> produced no output\"` | `stderr: <verbatim trimmed stderr or \"(none)\">` ; `try: run \\`<provider-cli>\\` directly to confirm it works` |\n| `!streaming && stdoutByteCount > 0` | `\"Timed out after Xs: <provider> was generating output when killed\"` | `transcript: <size>` ; `stderr: <verbatim trimmed stderr>` ; `try: raise --summary-timeout-seconds` |\n\nCancellation (Ctrl+C / `context.Canceled`) bypasses this entirely and renders `\"Summary generation canceled\"` with no rows.\n\nNon-timeout failures (typed `*ClaudeError` from PR #963, `errEmptyTranscript`, parse errors, etc.) are unaffected — they have their own branches in `formatCheckpointSummaryError` and continue working as today.\n\n## Test coverage\n\nPer project convention (`t.Parallel()`, `testutil` helpers, no global state writes).\n\n**New unit tests:**\n\n- `agent/capabilities_test.go::TestAsStreamingTextGenerator` — 4 cases mirroring `TestAsTextGenerator`.\n- `agent/claudecode/response_test.go::TestStreamClaudeResponse_Success` — parses `stream_success.jsonl`, verifies event count, final result text, malformed-line count = 0.\n- `agent/claudecode/response_test.go::TestStreamClaudeResponse_ErrorEnvelope` — parses `stream_error_404.jsonl`, verifies `IsError=true`, `APIErrorStatus=404`.\n- `agent/claudecode/response_test.go::TestStreamClaudeResponse_MalformedLineSkipped` — synthetic stream with one bad line, asserts non-zero malformed count + final still returned.\n- `agent/claudecode/generate_streaming_test.go::TestGenerateTextStreaming_Success` — `CommandRunner` stub returning success fixture, asserts progress callback sequence: `Connecting → FirstToken → Generating (×N) → Done`.\n- `agent/claudecode/generate_streaming_test.go::TestGenerateTextStreaming_FallbackOnUnrecognizedFlag` — stub stderr returns \"unknown flag: --output-format=stream-json\", asserts fallback to `GenerateText`.\n- `agent/claudecode/generate_streaming_test.go::TestGenerateTextStreaming_EnvelopeErrorOverrideCancel` — stub returns is_error envelope, then ctx is cancelled — asserts envelope error wins (not \"canceled\").\n- `cli/explain_test.go::TestSummaryProgressWriter_TTY` — pipe to a fake terminal writer, render fixed event sequence, assert in-place updates present.\n- `cli/explain_test.go::TestSummaryProgressWriter_NonTTY` — render to `bytes.Buffer`, assert one line per event, no `\\r`.\n- `cli/explain_test.go::TestSummaryProgressWriter_Accessible` — `t.Setenv(\"ACCESSIBLE\", \"1\")`, assert ASCII glyphs only.\n- `cli/explain_test.go::TestFormatCheckpointSummaryError_TimeoutDiagnostic_*` — five tests, one per row of the table above.\n- `cli/explain_test.go::TestResolveSummaryTimeout_DefaultZero` — replaces `TestDefaultCheckpointSummaryTimeout_IsFiveMinutes`; asserts unset returns `0`.\n\n**Updated unit tests:**\n\n- `cli/explain_test.go::TestGenerateCheckpointAISummary_*` — accept the new `ProgressFn` parameter (passing `nil` or a recording function as appropriate).\n\n**Integration:** none new. Existing integration tests don't exercise `--generate`.\n\n**Vogon canary:** untouched. Vogon doesn't generate summaries.\n\n**Manual verification before merge:**\n\n- Real `claude` CLI, large transcript, no flag set → progress phases render on TTY, no timeout.\n- Real `claude` CLI, `--summary-timeout-seconds 5`, large transcript → row 3 diagnostic (\"model responded but did not finish\") fires.\n- Real `claude` CLI, network down → row 2 diagnostic (\"sent request but received no response\") fires.\n- `entire configure --summarize-provider codex`, `--summary-timeout-seconds 5` on large transcript → row 5 diagnostic (\"was generating output when killed\") fires, stderr surfaces.\n- `entire configure --summarize-provider codex`, fake `codex` binary that sleeps without producing output, `--summary-timeout-seconds 5` → row 4 diagnostic (\"produced no output\") fires.\n- Old `claude` CLI build (mocked via `CommandRunner` stub returning \"unknown flag\" stderr) → falls back to non-streaming, no progress events, but summary completes.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Idle-based cancellation. Discussed, dropped. Can be revisited if real-world reports show CI jobs hanging despite explicit caps.\n- Streaming for non-Claude providers. Requires per-provider work in each agent package; future PRs.\n- Progress rendering for the auto-summary path (`strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`). Hot path, no human watching, stays silent.\n- Restructuring `formatCheckpointSummaryError` beyond the `DeadlineExceeded` branch.\n\n## Risk\n\n- **Behavior change for users relying on the 5-minute default cap from #1204.** They now get no timeout unless they set one. Mitigation: release note explicitly calls this out and includes the one-line `entire configure --summarize-timeout-seconds 300` to restore the old default.\n- **Streaming path is a new code path.** Mitigated by the unrecognized-flag fallback, the malformed-line tolerance in the parser, and the stdout drain.\n- **Provider-neutral progress strings might surprise Claude users who expected \"Anthropic\" wording.** Acceptable trade — the alternative is per-provider rewrites of the UI strings, which is more code for marginal value.\n\n## Migration\n\n- One existing test (`TestDefaultCheckpointSummaryTimeout_IsFiveMinutes`) is replaced. No external code depends on the removed constant.\n- The `--summary-timeout-seconds 0` value already means \"no override\" in #1204; that semantic continues to work and now matches the absence of a deadline at the package level.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6407addc-c79d-4954-93eb-4360d391d090","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact-2","sessionId":"4944fa51-d7dd-4310-b62f-7802a196cd45","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"redact-2"}
