{"parentUuid":"87c630c8-46a3-475e-b8d3-8de98a809c93","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_018pBDaQ3G2PeRW9mf6fZ3Yc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013yW4vrW3V14DYmhmQ8zRN2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-13-explain-summary-streaming.md","content":"# `entire explain --generate` streaming + diagnostic — Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Make `entire explain --generate` show live progress on TTY, emit observable-state-based timeout diagnostics, and have **no automatic deadline** unless the user opts in via `summary_timeout_seconds` / `--summary-timeout-seconds`.\n\n**Architecture:** Port PR #964's `StreamingTextGenerator` capability interface, Claude `stream-json` parser, and per-phase progress events on top of #1204's existing flag/setting/configure surface. Drop #964's idle watchdog: with deadline now opt-in only, captured stream state alone suffices to write a meaningful timeout error. Provider-neutral progress UI (no \"Anthropic\"/\"Claude\" hardcoded — multi-provider summary work in #1044 already shipped).\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26.x, github.com/spf13/cobra, github.com/charmbracelet/lipgloss (existing style helpers), `bufio.Scanner` for NDJSON, `exec.CommandContext` for subprocess.\n\n**Worktree:** Execute in a dedicated worktree via @superpowers:using-git-worktrees, branched off `origin/main` (`cc178b537` is the head as of writing).\n\n**Reference:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-13-explain-summary-streaming-design.md`\n\n---\n\n## File Structure\n\n**Create:**\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/generate_streaming.go` — `(*ClaudeCodeAgent).GenerateTextStreaming` invoking `claude --print --output-format stream-json --verbose`, NDJSON event dispatch, fallback to `GenerateText` on unrecognized-flag stderr.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/generate_streaming_test.go` — success path, fallback path, envelope-error-outranks-cancel path, drain-on-early-abort.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/testdata/stream_success.jsonl` — golden multi-event stream ending in `result.is_error=false`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/testdata/stream_error_404.jsonl` — minimal stream ending in `result.is_error=true, api_error_status=404`.\n\n**Modify:**\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go` — add `ProgressPhase` constants, `GenerationProgress` struct, `ProgressFn` type, `StreamingTextGenerator` interface.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/capabilities.go` — add `DeclaredCaps.StreamingTextGenerator` field, `AsStreamingTextGenerator` detector.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/capabilities_test.go` — add `TestAsStreamingTextGenerator`, mirror `TestAsTextGenerator` pattern.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/response.go` — add `streamEvent`, `streamInnerEvent`, `streamDelta`, `streamMessage` types and `streamClaudeResponse` NDJSON scanner.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/response_test.go` — parser tests against fixtures.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/summarize/summarize.go` — add `progress agent.ProgressFn` parameter to `GenerateFromTranscript`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/summarize/claude.go` — try `AsStreamingTextGenerator` first, fall back to `TextGenerator`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/summarize/summarize_test.go` — update existing call sites with `nil` progress.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go` — remove `defaultCheckpointSummaryTimeout` constant, change `resolveSummaryTimeout` to return `0` on unset, skip `context.WithTimeout` when timeout is `0`, add `summaryProgressWriter`, add `summaryAttempt` state, rewrite the `DeadlineExceeded` branch of `formatCheckpointSummaryError`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/explain_test.go` — replace `TestDefaultCheckpointSummaryTimeout_IsFiveMinutes` with `TestResolveSummaryTimeout_DefaultZero`, add diagnostic-message tests, add progress-writer tests, update existing `TestGenerateCheckpointAISummary_*` tests.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go` — pass `nil` for new `ProgressFn` parameter.\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 1: Capability interface and detection\n\n**Outcome:** Build-only change — adds the `StreamingTextGenerator` interface and capability detector. No agent implements it yet. Test coverage mirrors existing `AsTextGenerator` pattern. One commit at the end.\n\n### Task 1.1: Add streaming types and interface to `agent.go`\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go` — insert immediately after `TextGenerator` interface (currently around line 198 on `origin/main`).\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Open `cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go` and locate the existing `TextGenerator` interface (search for `type TextGenerator interface`).\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Insert after the closing brace of `TextGenerator`:\n\n```go\n// ProgressPhase identifies a coarse stage in streaming text generation.\ntype ProgressPhase string\n\nconst (\n\t// PhaseConnecting is emitted once when the CLI signals it is making the upstream request.\n\tPhaseConnecting ProgressPhase = \"connecting\"\n\t// PhaseFirstToken is emitted once when the upstream responds with the first event,\n\t// carrying TTFT and input/cache token counts.\n\tPhaseFirstToken ProgressPhase = \"first-token\"\n\t// PhaseGenerating is emitted repeatedly as text or thinking deltas arrive.\n\t// OutputTokens carries a running estimate based on delta sizes.\n\tPhaseGenerating ProgressPhase = \"generating\"\n\t// PhaseDone is emitted once when the final result event is received without error.\n\tPhaseDone ProgressPhase = \"done\"\n)\n\n// GenerationProgress reports a snapshot of streaming text generation progress.\n// Fields not relevant to the current Phase may be zero-valued.\ntype GenerationProgress struct {\n\tPhase             ProgressPhase\n\tOutputTokens      int // running estimate during PhaseGenerating; final at PhaseDone\n\tInputTokens       int // populated at PhaseFirstToken\n\tCachedInputTokens int // populated at PhaseFirstToken\n\tTTFTms            int // time-to-first-token, populated at PhaseFirstToken\n\tDurationMs        int // populated at PhaseDone (final result event)\n}\n\n// ProgressFn receives streaming progress updates. It must not block — invoke it\n// from the same goroutine that reads the stream and keep handlers fast.\ntype ProgressFn func(GenerationProgress)\n\n// StreamingTextGenerator is an optional interface for text generators whose\n// underlying CLI exposes a streaming output mode. Callers can use AsStreamingTextGenerator\n// to detect support and fall back to plain GenerateText when unavailable.\ntype StreamingTextGenerator interface {\n\tAgent\n\n\t// GenerateTextStreaming invokes the agent's streaming text generation and\n\t// calls progress for each phase update. progress may be nil to suppress\n\t// reporting. The returned string is the final response text.\n\tGenerateTextStreaming(ctx context.Context, prompt, model string, progress ProgressFn) (string, error)\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Run `mise run fmt && mise run lint` from the repo root. Expected: clean, no diagnostics.\n\n### Task 1.2: Add capability field and detector\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/capabilities.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** In `DeclaredCaps`, add the new field. Keep the existing field order (`TextGenerator` is on line 26 on `origin/main`); insert directly after it:\n\n```go\nTextGenerator          bool `json:\"text_generator\"`\nStreamingTextGenerator bool `json:\"streaming_text_generator\"`\nHookResponseWriter     bool `json:\"hook_response_writer\"`\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Add the detector function. The existing `AsTextGenerator` sits around line 106 on `origin/main` — insert directly after it:\n\n```go\n// AsStreamingTextGenerator returns the agent as StreamingTextGenerator if it both\n// implements the interface and (for CapabilityDeclarer agents) has declared the capability.\nfunc AsStreamingTextGenerator(ag Agent) (StreamingTextGenerator, bool) { //nolint:ireturn // type-assertion helper must return interface\n\tif ag == nil {\n\t\treturn nil, false\n\t}\n\tstg, ok := ag.(StreamingTextGenerator)\n\tif !ok {\n\t\treturn nil, false\n\t}\n\tif cd, ok := ag.(CapabilityDeclarer); ok {\n\t\treturn stg, cd.DeclaredCapabilities().StreamingTextGenerator\n\t}\n\treturn stg, true\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Run `mise run fmt && mise run lint`. Expected: clean.\n\n### Task 1.3: Add capability detector tests\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/capabilities_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Locate `mockFullAgent` (around line 90 on `origin/main`). It already implements every capability. Add the streaming method:\n\n```go\n// StreamingTextGenerator\nfunc (m *mockFullAgent) GenerateTextStreaming(context.Context, string, string, ProgressFn) (string, error) {\n\treturn \"\", nil\n}\n```\n\nPlace it next to the other `mockFullAgent` method implementations (e.g., right after `GenerateText` or `CalculateTokenUsage`).\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Add a built-in mock (mirrors `mockBuiltinPromptAgent`):\n\n```go\n// mockBuiltinStreamingAgent is a built-in agent that implements StreamingTextGenerator but NOT CapabilityDeclarer.\ntype mockBuiltinStreamingAgent struct {\n\tmockBaseAgent\n}\n\nfunc (m *mockBuiltinStreamingAgent) GenerateTextStreaming(context.Context, string, string, ProgressFn) (string, error) {\n\treturn \"\", nil\n}\n```\n\nPlace it next to the other `mockBuiltin*Agent` declarations.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Add the test function. Mirror `TestAsTextGenerator` exactly — append at the end of the file:\n\n```go\nfunc TestAsStreamingTextGenerator(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tt.Run(\"not implemented\", func(t *testing.T) {\n\t\tt.Parallel()\n\t\tag := &mockBaseAgent{}\n\t\t_, ok := AsStreamingTextGenerator(ag)\n\t\tif ok {\n\t\t\tt.Error(\"expected false for agent not implementing StreamingTextGen