olated, no hardcoded vendor strings. One commit.\n\n### Task 6.1: Add the progress writer\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Add helpers `formatMs`, `formatTokenCount` (if not already present from elsewhere), and `humanizeBytes`. Search first: `grep -n \"func formatMs\\|func humanizeBytes\\|func formatTokenCount\" cmd/entire/cli/`. If none, insert near the existing `formatSummaryTimeout` helper:\n\n```go\n// formatMs formats a millisecond count as \"1.5s\" / \"120ms\".\nfunc formatMs(ms int) string {\n\tif ms < 1000 {\n\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%dms\", ms)\n\t}\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%.1fs\", float64(ms)/1000.0)\n}\n\n// humanizeBytes formats a byte count as a short human-readable string\n// (e.g., 0 B, 500 B, 1.5 KB, 47 KB, 1.2 MB). Uses 1024-based units.\nfunc humanizeBytes(n int) string {\n\tconst unit = 1024\n\tif n < unit {\n\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%d B\", n)\n\t}\n\tdiv, exp := int64(unit), 0\n\tfor x := int64(n) / unit; x >= unit; x /= unit {\n\t\tdiv *= unit\n\t\texp++\n\t}\n\tsuffix := []string{\"KB\", \"MB\", \"GB\", \"TB\"}[exp]\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%.1f %s\", float64(n)/float64(div), suffix)\n}\n\n// formatTokenCount formats a token count compactly: 1234 -> \"1.2k\", 35892 -> \"35.9k\".\nfunc formatTokenCount(n int) string {\n\tif n < 1000 {\n\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%d\", n)\n\t}\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%.1fk\", float64(n)/1000.0)\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Add the `summaryProgressWriter` struct. Place it near the existing `summaryDeadline*` / style helpers in `explain.go`:\n\n```go\n// summaryProgressWriter renders agent.GenerationProgress events to the\n// configured writer using existing statusStyles. On a TTY (and outside\n// ACCESSIBLE mode) it rewrites the current line for the running token\n// count; otherwise it appends one line per event.\n//\n// Provider-neutral phrasing — \"provider\" stands in for the configured\n// summary provider. The provider name is interpolated into the initial\n// \"Generating checkpoint summary...\" line by generateCheckpointSummary.\ntype summaryProgressWriter struct {\n\tw        io.Writer\n\tinplace  bool\n\tlastLine string\n\tarrow    string // precomputed styled glyph\n\tcheck    string // precomputed styled glyph\n\n\t// State captured for diagnostic use at timeout.\n\tphasesReached map[agent.ProgressPhase]bool\n\tstreamed      bool\n}\n\nfunc newSummaryProgressWriter(w io.Writer) *summaryProgressWriter {\n\tstyles := newStatusStyles(w)\n\tinplace := isTerminalWriter(w) && !IsAccessibleMode()\n\tarrow := \"->\"\n\tcheck := \"*\"\n\tif !IsAccessibleMode() {\n\t\tarrow = styles.render(styles.cyan, \"→\")\n\t\tcheck = styles.render(styles.green, \"✓\")\n\t}\n\treturn &summaryProgressWriter{\n\t\tw:             w,\n\t\tinplace:       inplace,\n\t\tarrow:         arrow,\n\t\tcheck:         check,\n\t\tphasesReached: make(map[agent.ProgressPhase]bool),\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (s *summaryProgressWriter) handle(p agent.GenerationProgress) {\n\ts.streamed = true\n\ts.phasesReached[p.Phase] = true\n\n\tswitch p.Phase {\n\tcase agent.PhaseConnecting:\n\t\ts.printLine(s.arrow + \" Sending request to provider...\")\n\tcase agent.PhaseFirstToken:\n\t\ts.printLine(fmt.Sprintf(\n\t\t\t\"%s Provider responded (TTFT %s, %s cached input tokens) -- generating...\",\n\t\t\ts.arrow, formatMs(p.TTFTms), formatTokenCount(p.CachedInputTokens)))\n\tcase agent.PhaseGenerating:\n\t\ts.updateLine(fmt.Sprintf(\n\t\t\t\"%s Writing summary... (~%s tokens)\",\n\t\t\ts.arrow, formatTokenCount(p.OutputTokens)))\n\tcase agent.PhaseDone:\n\t\ts.printLine(fmt.Sprintf(\n\t\t\t\"%s Summary generated (%s, %s output tokens)\",\n\t\t\ts.check, formatMs(p.DurationMs), formatTokenCount(p.OutputTokens)))\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (s *summaryProgressWriter) printLine(line string) {\n\tif s.inplace && s.lastLine != \"\" {\n\t\tfmt.Fprint(s.w, \"\\r\\033[2K\")\n\t}\n\tfmt.Fprintln(s.w, line)\n\ts.lastLine = \"\"\n}\n\nfunc (s *summaryProgressWriter) updateLine(line string) {\n\tif s.lastLine == line {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tif s.inplace {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(s.w, \"\\r\\033[2K%s\", line)\n\t} else {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(s.w, line)\n\t}\n\ts.lastLine = line\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Run `mise run fmt && mise run lint`. The unused struct fields `streamed` / `phasesReached` are intentional — they're consumed by chunk 7. If lint complains about unused fields, add a `//nolint:unused // consumed in chunk 7` line above the struct OR temporarily reference them in `handle`.\n\n### Task 6.2: Wire writer into `generateCheckpointSummary`\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Locate `generateCheckpointSummary` (search for `func generateCheckpointSummary`). Find the existing line:\n\n```go\nfmt.Fprintln(errW, \"Generating checkpoint summary...\")\n```\n\nReplace it with a provider-aware version (the provider name is already resolved upstream as `provider.Generator` / `provider.Name` — confirm the exact symbol by reading the surrounding code):\n\n```go\nfmt.Fprintf(errW, \"Generating checkpoint summary... (transcript: %s, provider: %s)\\n\",\n    humanizeBytes(len(scopedTranscript)), provider.Name)\n```\n\n(If the provider variable doesn't expose a `.Name` field directly, use whatever is already used for the existing \"Using <provider> for summary generation.\" line in the same function.)\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Add the progress writer just below that line, and pass `handle` into `generateCheckpointAISummary`. The relevant call becomes:\n\n```go\nprogressWriter := newSummaryProgressWriter(errW)\nsummary, err := generateCheckpointAISummary(\n    ctx, scopedTranscript, cpSummary.FilesTouched,\n    content.Metadata.Agent, provider.Generator,\n    timeout, // resolved earlier via resolveSummaryTimeout\n    progressWriter, // chunk 7 reads .phasesReached and .streamed on timeout\n)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Update the `generateCheckpointAISummary` signature to accept the progress writer (rather than a bare `ProgressFn`) so its diagnostic branch ca