s stderr from a\n// non-streaming text generator so callers can surface it in user-facing\n// errors. It wraps the original error (which may be a typed *ClaudeError\n// from PR #963 or a generic exec failure).\ntype TextGenerationFailure struct {\n\tErr          error\n\tStderr       string\n\tStdoutBytes  int  // total bytes seen on stdout before failure\n}\n\nfunc (e *TextGenerationFailure) Error() string { return e.Err.Error() }\nfunc (e *TextGenerationFailure) Unwrap() error { return e.Err }\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** For each non-streaming provider's generator (the ones that return `(*checkpoint.Summary, error)` via `agent.RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI`), wrap their error returns with a `*TextGenerationFailure` carrying captured stderr. Avoid changing the shared `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI` signature if possible — wrap at the per-provider site.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4:** Update `summarize.Generator` callers to recognize and preserve `*TextGenerationFailure` (don't double-wrap with `fmt.Errorf`).\n\n- [ ] **Step 5:** Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/summarize ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/...`. Expected: PASS.\n\n### Task 7.2: Rewrite the `DeadlineExceeded` branch\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Locate `formatCheckpointSummaryError`. Find the `case errors.Is(err, context.DeadlineExceeded):` branch — the one with the three \"causes\" rows.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Replace it with state-aware classification. The signature already takes `deadline time.Duration`; add a new parameter `attempt *summaryProgressWriter` (or pass the writer through). The branch becomes:\n\n```go\ncase errors.Is(err, context.DeadlineExceeded):\n    label, rows := timeoutDiagnostic(err, deadline, attempt)\n    return label, rows, fmt.Errorf(\"summary generation did not return within the %s safety deadline\", formatSummaryTimeout(deadline))\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Implement `timeoutDiagnostic`:\n\n```go\n// timeoutDiagnostic builds the label and supporting rows for a\n/