st of the path is unaffected.\n\nStdout is drained with `io.Copy(io.Discard, ...)` after the scanner stops, so a blocked pipe can't deadlock `cmd.Wait()`. Drain errors are logged at DEBUG (stdout is closing anyway).\n\nStream parsing types (`streamEvent`, `streamInnerEvent`, `streamDelta`, `streamMessage`) live in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/response.go`. Fixtures `testdata/stream_success.jsonl` and `testdata/stream_error_404.jsonl`.\n\nThe ClaudeCodeAgent struct gains `DeclaredCapabilities().StreamingTextGenerator = true`.\n\n## Wiring through `summarize`\n\n`summarize.GenerateFromTranscript` adds one parameter:\n\n```go\nfunc GenerateFromTranscript(\n    ctx context.Context,\n    transcriptBytes redact.RedactedBytes,\n    filesTouched []string,\n    agentType types.AgentType,\n    generator Generator,\n    progress agent.ProgressFn,  // new; may be nil\n) (*checkpoint.Summary, error)\n```\n\n`summarize.Generator.Generate` is not changed. The progress threading lives at one level up:\n\n`summarize.ClaudeGenerator.Generate(ctx, input)` is changed: it accesses its underlying agent via `AsStreamingTextGenerator`. If available, it calls `GenerateTextStreaming` and forwards the `ProgressFn` it received from `GenerateFromTranscript` (carried on a new field of `ClaudeGenerator` or via a closure — implementation plan picks the cleaner shape). If not available, falls back to current `GenerateText`.","numLines":35,"startLine":100,"totalLines":262}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0d9990e1-5dc7-4552-b138-01a79ebf2dc9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact-2","sessionId":"4944fa51-d7dd-4310-b62f-7802a196cd45","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"redact-2"}
