ignature if possible — wrap at the per-provider site.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4:** Update `summarize.Generator` callers to recognize and preserve `*TextGenerationFailure` (don't double-wrap with `fmt.Errorf`).\n\n- [ ] **Step 5:** Run `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/summarize ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/...`. Expected: PASS.","new_string":"### Task 7.1: Capture non-streaming subprocess output\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/text_generator_cli.go` — central place where the shared helper runs the subprocess and captures stderr; this is where the typed-error wrapping happens once.\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/summarize/types.go` (or create — verify with `ls cmd/entire/cli/summarize/`) — house the `TextGenerationFailure` type next to existing summarize types.\n- Modify (only if step 2 verification shows it's needed): each of the four per-provider generate.go files:\n  - `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/generate.go`\n  - `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/generate.go`\n  - `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/generate.go`\n  - `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/generate.go`\n- NOT modified: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/opencode/` and `cmd/entire/cli/agent/factoryaidroid/` — verified at plan-writing time (`ls cmd/entire/cli/agent/{opencode,factoryaidroid}/generate.go 2>&1`) that they do not have generate.go files. They do not implement TextGenerator and are not summary providers.\n- NOT modified: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/generate.go` — its error path already returns typed `*ClaudeError` (PR #963) which carries stderr-equivalent info in `ClaudeError.Message`. The diagnostic for Claude flows through stream-state, not `*TextGenerationFailure`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Define `TextGenerationFailure` in `cmd/entire/cli/summarize/types.go` (create if missing). Pick `summarize` over `agent` because the explain layer is the only consumer and `summarize` is already where `Generator` lives:\n\n```go\n// TextGenerationFailure carries captured subprocess output alongside a\n// TextGenerator's error so the explain layer can build a meaningful\n// timeout diagnostic (\"provider produced no output\" vs \"was generating\n// output when killed\"). Wraps the original error so errors.As against\n// the inner type (e.g. *ClaudeError) keeps working.\ntype TextGenerationFailure struct {\n\tErr         error\n\tStderr      string\n\tStdoutBytes int\n}\n\nfunc (e *TextGenerationFailure) Error() string { return e.Err.Error() }\nfunc (e *TextGenerationFailure) Unwrap() error { return e.Err }\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Check how the shared `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI` currently surfaces stderr. Run:\n\n```bash\ngrep -n \"stderr\\|Stderr\" cmd/entire/cli/agent/text_generator_cli.go\n```\n\nInspect the failure-return paths (non-zero exit, missing binary, ctx cancel). The shared helper already captures stderr internally (per spec). The change needed: on non-nil error, wrap into `*summarize.TextGenerationFailure` carrying the captured stderr and stdout byte count, then return.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Modify `cmd/entire/cli/agent/text_generator_cli.go` to wrap at the source. Find the error-return sites in `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI` and replace `return \"\", err` with:\n\n```go\nreturn \"\", &summarize.TextGenerationFailure{\n    Err:         err,\n    Stderr:      strings.TrimSpace(capturedStderr),\n    StdoutBytes: capturedStdoutBytes,\n}\n```\n\nThis introduces an import of `cmd/entire/cli/summarize` from `cmd/entire/cli/agent`. **Check for an import cycle**: run `go vet ./cmd/entire/cli/agent`. If it errors with `import cycle not allowed`, the wrapping needs to move to a layer that's downstream of both packages — concretely, do it in the per-provider files (Task 7.1 Step 4) instead, and skip this step. Document the choice (which layer wraps) in a one-line comment on the type.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4:** If step 3 introduced an import cycle, do the wrapping at each provider's site instead. Pattern for each of the four files (`codex/generate.go`, `cursor/generate.go`, `copilotcli/generate.go`, `g