{"parentUuid":"ff273745-9e4d-4c2f-af6c-599f30497537","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01YHFP7PUCR68tbYiww2Unaf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KxwwA57i2qF4F2ZY2nkFZ1","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-13-explain-summary-streaming-design.md","old_string":"Provider-display naming for the diagnostic copy uses a small lookup that maps `types.AgentName` to the CLI binary the user runs (e.g., `claude-code` → `claude`, `gemini-cli` → `gemini`, `copilot-cli` → `copilot`, `factoryai-droid` → `droid`, `codex` → `codex`, `cursor` → `agent`). Lookup helper lives in `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go` next to `timeoutDiagnostic`.","new_string":"Provider-display naming for the diagnostic copy uses a small lookup that maps `types.AgentName` to the CLI binary the user runs (e.g., `claude-code` → `claude`, `gemini-cli` → `gemini`, `copilot-cli` → `copilot`, `factoryai-droid` → `droid`, `codex` → `codex`, `cursor` → `agent`). Lookup helper lives in `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go` next to `timeoutDiagnostic`.\n\n### Stderr classifier for non-streaming providers\n\nStreaming providers get phase-based attribution (`PhaseConnecting` / `PhaseFirstToken` / `PhaseGenerating`) which cleanly distinguishes \"can't reach API\" from \"API slow.\" Non-streaming providers (Codex / Cursor / Copilot / Gemini) historically don't have that signal — they get only `stdoutByteCount` (zero vs non-zero) plus stderr text. To close the diagnostic-parity gap, a stderr classifier inspects captured stderr against known phrases and emits a category-tagged row.\n\nFunction `summarize.ClassifyStderr(stderr string) (FailureCategory, hint string)` lives in a new `cmd/entire/cli/summarize/classify.go`. Five categories plus an explicit unknown:\n\n| Category | Detection patterns (substring, case-insensitive) | Hint surfaced to user |\n|---|---|---|\n| `network` | `connection refused`, `could not resolve`, `no route to host`, `network unreachable`, `name or service not known`, `dial tcp` | \"couldn't reach provider API — check network/VPN\" |\n| `auth` | `unauthorized`, `401`, `not logged in`, `authentication failed`, `auth token` | \"provider rejected credentials — re-authenticate with the provider CLI\" |\n| `rate_limit` | `rate limit`, `429`, `quota exceeded`, `too many requests` | \"provider rate-limit — wait and retry\" |\n| `server_error` | `service unavailable`, `503`, `502`, `bad gateway`, `internal server error`, `500` | \"provider API degraded — try again shortly\" |\n| `model_not_found` | `model not found`, `invalid model`, `unknown model` | \"model rejected — check --model flag or settings\" |\n| (unknown) | — | (no extra row; raw stderr still shown) |\n\nConsumed in two places:\n\n1. **`timeoutDiagnostic`** (when non-streaming attempt has captured stderr): on classifier match, the `kind:` row and the classifier's `try:` hint REPLACE the generic `try: raise --summary-timeout-seconds` row. The raw stderr row remains so users can verify the classification.\n2. **`formatCheckpointSummaryError` default branch** (non-timeout failures with stderr): today's catch-all \"Failed to generate summary\" gains a `kind:` row when the classifier matches. Same false-positive insurance — raw stderr stays visible.\n\nWorst-case behavior: false-positive classification labels the failure wrong, but raw stderr is also shown so users can read the actual error themselves. The classifier never suppresses information; it only adds a labeled hint when patterns match.\n\nClaude is unaffected by this work — PR #963's typed `*ClaudeError` already produces equivalent or better classification for Claude failures via its `Kind` discriminator."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":113,"cache_read_input_tokens":