{"parentUuid":"54bf6cdd-2908-4c75-b9dd-7a54a3bd470d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"37f37d35-e1b4-4608-a223-c3017071f683","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015FtijDNog8LHu3dqx6fA4d","type":"tool_result","content":"1358\t\n1359\t## Chunk 6: Progress writer and live UI\n1360\t\n1361\t**Outcome:** TTY users see live progress events; non-TTY and `ACCESSIBLE=1` users get one-line-per-event output. Provider name is interpolated, no hardcoded vendor strings. One commit.\n1362\t\n1363\t### Task 6.1: Add the progress writer\n1364\t\n1365\t**Files:**\n1366\t- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go`\n1367\t\n1368\t- [ ] **Step 1:** Add helpers `formatMs`, `formatTokenCount` (if not already present from elsewhere), and `humanizeBytes`. Search first: `grep -n \"func formatMs\\|func humanizeBytes\\|func formatTokenCount\" cmd/entire/cli/`. If none, insert near the existing `formatSummaryTimeout` helper:\n1369\t\n1370\t```go\n1371\t// formatMs formats a millisecond count as \"1.5s\" / \"120ms\".\n1372\tfunc formatMs(ms int) string {\n1373\t\tif ms < 1000 {\n1374\t\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%dms\", ms)\n1375\t\t}\n1376\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%.1fs\", float64(ms)/1000.0)\n1377\t}\n1378\t\n1379\t// humanizeBytes formats a byte count as a short human-readable string\n1380\t// (e.g., 0 B, 500 B, 1.5 KB, 47 KB, 1.2 MB). Uses 1024-based units.\n1381\tfunc humanizeBytes(n int) string {\n1382\t\tconst unit = 1024\n1383\t\tif n < unit {\n1384\t\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%d B\", n)\n1385\t\t}\n1386\t\tdiv, exp := int64(unit), 0\n1387\t\tfor x := int64(n) / unit; x >= unit; x /= unit {\n1388\t\t\tdiv *= unit\n1389\t\t\texp++\n1390\t\t}\n1391\t\tsuffix := []string{\"KB\", \"MB\", \"GB\", \"TB\"}[exp]\n1392\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%.1f %s\", float64(n)/float64(div), suffix)\n1393\t}\n1394\t\n1395\t// formatTokenCount formats a token count compactly: 1234 -> \"1.2k\", 35892 -> \"35.9k\".\n1396\tfunc formatTokenCount(n int) string {\n1397\t\tif n < 1000 {\n1398\t\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%d\", n)\n1399\t\t}\n1400\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%.1fk\", float64(n)/1000.0)\n1401\t}\n1402\t```\n1403\t\n1404\t- [ ] **Step 2:** Add the `summaryAttempt` value type. This is the diagnostic state — separate from the UI writer — so chunk 7's `timeoutDiagnostic` can read it without depending on the writer struct. Place it near the existing style helpers in `explain.go`:\n1405\t\n1406\t```go\n1407\t// summaryAttempt accumulates observable state during a single --generate\n1408\t// summary call. The progress writer populates the streaming fields as\n1409\t// events fire; the non-streaming Generate path populates stderrCaptured /\n1410\t// stdoutByteCount via *summarize.TextGenerationFailure (chunk 7).\n1411\t// formatCheckpointSummaryError reads this struct at DeadlineExceeded to\n1412\t// build the timeout diagnostic message.\n1413\ttype summaryAttempt struct {\n1414\t\tstreaming       bool\n1415\t\tphasesReached   map[agent.ProgressPhase]bool\n1416\t\tstderrCaptured  string\n1417\t\tstdoutByteCount int\n1418\t\tdeadline        time.Duration\n1419\t\tprovider        types.AgentName\n1420\t}\n1421\t\n1422\tfunc newSummaryAttempt(provider types.AgentName, deadline time.Duration) *summaryAttempt {\n1423\t\treturn &summaryAttempt{\n1424\t\t\tphasesReached: make(map[agent.ProgressPhase]bool),\n1425\t\t\tdeadline:      deadline,\n1426\t\t\tprovider:      provider,\n1427\t\t}\n1428\t}\n1429\t```\n1430\t\n1431\t- [ ] **Step 3:** Add the `summaryProgressWriter` struct. It holds a `*summaryAttempt` and writes into it as a side effect of rendering progress. Place it directly below `summaryAttempt`:\n1432\t\n1433\t```go\n1434\t// summaryProgressWriter renders agent.GenerationProgress events to the\n1435\t// configured writer using existing statusStyles, and side-effectfully\n1436\t// updates the supplied *summaryAttempt so the timeout-diagnostic path\n1437\t// can attribute failure to a specific phase. On a TTY (and outside\n1438\t// ACCESSIBLE mode) it rew