{"parentUuid":"7ea0425f-347f-4520-9235-0d1d0bf9d636","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"37f37d35-e1b4-4608-a223-c3017071f683","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Co3XFdarmGPxgh8unqMjTv","type":"tool_result","content":"1758\t---\n1759\t\n1760\t## Chunk 7: Observable-state timeout diagnostic\n1761\t\n1762\t**Outcome:** When the user-set wall-clock cap fires, the error message reflects what the subprocess was actually doing. Non-streaming providers surface captured stderr. The three-cause shrug message goes away. One commit.\n1763\t\n1764\t### Task 7.1: Capture non-streaming subprocess output\n1765\t\n1766\t**Files:**\n1767\t- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/text_generator_cli.go` — central place where the shared helper runs the subprocess and captures stderr; this is where the typed-error wrapping happens once.\n1768\t- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/summarize/types.go` (or create — verify with `ls cmd/entire/cli/summarize/`) — house the `TextGenerationFailure` type next to existing summarize types.\n1769\t- Modify (only if step 2 verification shows it's needed): each of the four per-provider generate.go files:\n1770\t  - `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/generate.go`\n1771\t  - `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/generate.go`\n1772\t  - `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/generate.go`\n1773\t  - `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/generate.go`\n1774\t- NOT modified: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/opencode/` and `cmd/entire/cli/agent/factoryaidroid/` — verified at plan-writing time (`ls cmd/entire/cli/agent/{opencode,factoryaidroid}/generate.go 2>&1`) that they do not have generate.go files. They do not implement TextGenerator and are not summary providers.\n1775\t- NOT modified: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/generate.go` — its error path already returns typed `*ClaudeError` (PR #963) which carries stderr-equivalent info in `ClaudeError.Message`. The diagnostic for Claude flows through stream-state, not `*TextGenerationFailure`.\n1776\t\n1777\t- [ ] **Step 1:** Define `TextGenerationFailure` in `cmd/entire/cli/summarize/types.go` (create if missing). Pick `summarize` over `agent` because the explain layer is the only consumer and `summarize` is already where `Generator` lives:\n1778\t\n1779\t```go\n1780\t// TextGenerationFailure carries captured subprocess output alongside a\n1781\t// TextGenerator's error so the explain layer can build a meaningful\n1782\t// timeout diagnostic (\"provider produced no output\" vs \"was generating\n1783\t// output when killed\"). Wraps the original error so errors.As against\n1784\t// the inner type (e.g. *ClaudeError) keeps working.\n1785\ttype TextGenerationFailure struct {\n1786\t\tErr         error\n1787\t\tStderr      string\n1788\t\tStdoutBytes int\n1789\t}\n1790\t\n1791\tfunc (e *TextGenerationFailure) Error() string { return e.Err.Error() }\n1792\tfunc (e *TextGenerationFailure) Unwrap() error { return e.Err }\n1793\t```\n1794\t\n1795\t- [ ] **Step 2:** Check how the shared `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI` currently surfaces stderr. Run:\n1796\t\n1797\t```bash\n1798\tgrep -n \"stderr\\|Stderr\" cmd/entire/cli/agent/text_generator_cli.go\n1799\t```\n1800\t\n1801\tInspect the failure-return paths (non-zero exit, missing binary, ctx cancel). The shared helper already captures stderr internally (per spec). The change needed: on non-nil error, wrap into `*summarize.TextGenerationFailure` carrying the captured stderr and stdout byte count, then return.\n1802\t\n1803\t- [ ] **Step 3:** Modify `cmd/entire/cli/agent/text_generator_cli.go` to wrap at the source. Find the error-return sites in `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI` and replace `return \"\", err` with:\n1804\t\n1805\t```go\n1806\treturn \"\", &summarize.TextGenerationFailure{\n1807\t    Err:         err,\n1808\t    Stderr:      strings.TrimSpace(capturedStderr),\n1809\t    StdoutBytes: capturedStdoutBytes,\n1810\t}\n1811\t```\n1812\t\n1813\tThis introduces an import of `cmd/entire/cli/summarize` from `cmd/entire/cli/agent`. **Check for an import cycle**: run `go vet ./cmd/entire/cli/agent`. If it errors with `import cycle not allowed`, the wrapping needs to move to a layer that's downstream of both packages — concretely, do it in the per-provider files (Task 7.1 Step 4) instead, and skip this step. Document the choice (which layer wraps) in a one-line comment on the type.\n1814\t\n1815\t- [ ] **Step 4:** If step 3 introduced an import cycle, do the wrapping at each provider's site instead. Pattern for each of the four files (`codex/generate.go`, `cursor/generate.go`, `copilotcli/generate.go`, `geminicli/generate.go`):\n1816\t\n1817\t```go\n1818\t// Old (last 2 lines of GenerateText):\n1819\tresult, err := agent.RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI(ctx, c.CommandRunner, \"codex\", \"codex\", args, prompt)\n1820\treturn result, err\n1821\t\n1822\t// New:\n1823\tresult, err := agent.RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI(ctx, c.CommandRunner, \"codex\", \"codex\", args, prompt)\n1824\tif err != nil {\n1825\t    return \"\", &summarize.TextGenerationFailure{Err: err, Stderr: \"\", StdoutBytes: 0}\n1826\t}\n1827\treturn result, nil\n1828\t```\n1829\t\n1830\tIf you take the per-provider path, you'll need `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI` to expose the captured stderr and stdout-byte-count to callers — change its signature to `func ... (result, stderr string, stdoutBytes int, err error)` and update all four callers + the existing tests in `text_generator_cli_test.go`. This is more invasive than step 3; prefer step 3 if no import cycle exists.\n1831\t\n1832\t- [ ] **Step 5:** Update `summarize.ClaudeGenerator.Generate` (in `cmd/entire/cli/summarize/claude.go`) to NOT double-wrap. The existing code already has `//nolint:wrapcheck` on the `return nil, err` from `textGenerator.GenerateText` — that's the line that preserves the typed error. Verify it survives the change by running:\n1833\t\n1834\t```bash\n1835\tgrep -n \"nolint:wrapcheck\" cmd/entire/cli/summarize/claude.go\n1836\t```\n1837\t\n1838\tIf a new `fmt.Errorf(\"failed to generate 