xceeded):` branch (the one with the three-cause rows). Replace with state-aware classification reading from `*summaryAttempt` (NOT `*summaryProgressWriter` — error formatting must not depend on the UI struct):\n1876\t\n1877\t```go\n1878\tcase errors.Is(err, context.DeadlineExceeded):\n1879\t    label, rows := timeoutDiagnostic(err, attempt)\n1880\t    structured := errors.New(\"summary generation timed out\")\n1881\t    if attempt.deadline > 0 {\n1882\t        structured = fmt.Errorf(\"summary generation did not return within the %s safety deadline\", formatSummaryTimeout(attempt.deadline))\n1883\t    }\n1884\t    return label, rows, structured\n1885\t```\n1886\t\n1887\t- [ ] **Step 3:** Implement `timeoutDiagnostic`:\n1888\t\n1889\t```go\n1890\t// timeoutDiagnostic builds the label and supporting rows for a\n1891\t// context.DeadlineExceeded failure. The deadline can be: (a) the user's\n1892\t// --summary-timeout-seconds / summary_timeout_seconds, captured in\n1893\t// attempt.deadline; or (b) a parent-context deadline imposed externally,\n1894\t// in which case attempt.deadline is 0. We render the label without a\n1895\t// concrete duration when the latter is the only signal we have.\n1896\tfunc timeoutDiagnostic(err error, attempt *summaryAttempt) (string, []explainRow) {\n1897\t\t// Prefix the label: \"Timed out after Xs:\" when we know X; \"Timed out:\" otherwise.\n1898\t\tprefix := \"Timed out: \"\n1899\t\tif attempt.deadline > 0 {\n1900\t\t\tprefix = \"Timed out after \" + formatSummaryTimeout(attempt.deadline) + \": \"\n1901\t\t}\n1902\t\ttryRunCLI := \"run the provider CLI directly to confirm it works\"\n1903\t\tif cli := providerCLIName(attempt.provider); cli != \"\" {\n1904\t\t\ttryRunCLI = fmt.Sprintf(\"run `%s` directly to confirm it works\", cli)\n1905\t\t}\n1906\t\n1907\t\tif attempt.streaming {\n1908\t\t\tswitch {\n1909\t\t\tcase !attempt.phasesReached[agent.PhaseConnecting]:\n1910\t\t\t\treturn prefix + \"provider never sent its request\",\n1911\t\t