{"parentUuid":"ccb9f833-30c1-4342-84cc-c60959b40d67","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KZPvvrtXF1XPg3WzBr7Hqn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Code Review: PR #964 — `feat(explain): live progress and observable-state timeout diagnostic`\n\n**Commits reviewed:** `ea1617cff`, `4ccedd1ef`, `0b9993ee4` (HEAD)\n**Diff:** 22 files, +1,422 / −170. About half the additions are tests.\n**Verification:** `mise run check` green on HEAD; real end-to-end smoke tests pass (TTY happy path, timeout-during-generation, offline network failure, non-TTY, ACCESSIBLE).\n\n## Overview\n\nBuilds on PR #1204 by completing what draft PR #964 set out to deliver: live progress for `entire explain --generate` and a proper observable-state timeout diagnostic. Removes the 5-minute automatic deadline default that #1204 left in place — timeouts are now opt-in. The original idle-watchdog mechanic from the early #964 draft was dropped; the diagnostic instead uses captured subprocess state. A stderr substring classifier (was \"chunk 8\") was also dropped — raw stderr passthrough is preferred to speculative pattern matching.\n\n## Code quality and style\n\n### Strengths\n\n- **Clean decomposition.** Three commits with logical boundaries: mechanism, policy, UX. None requires the others to be useful in isolation (you could revert C and keep streaming infra + opt-in policy without breaking compilation).\n- **Symmetry with existing patterns.** `AsStreamingTextGenerator` is a pixel-perfect mirror of `AsTextGenerator`; `StreamingTextGenerator` interface embeds `Agent` exactly as `TextGenerator` does; the `DeclaredCaps` field is alphabetically/conceptually placed between `TextGenerator` and `HookResponseWriter`. New code reads like it belongs.\n- **Provider-neutral diagnostic copy.** No \"Anthropic\" / \"Claude\" hardcoded. The `providerCLIName` lookup makes diagnostic `try:` rows accurate per agent (`run \\`claude\\` directly` vs `run \\`codex\\` directly`).\n- **Subprocess lifecycle is correct.** `cmd.Start()` → scanner read → `io.Copy(io.Discard, stdout)` drain → `cmd.Wait()`. The drain is the meaningful detail — without it, a `bufio.ErrTooLong` would deadlock `Wait()` on a blocked pipe.\n- **Envelope-error precedence is documented and correct.** `if final != nil && final.IsError` runs before the `ctx.Err()` check, so a 404 envelope wins over `context.Canceled` — users get the actionable HTTP-status error instead of a generic \"canceled\" message.\n- **Stderr capture is consistent across non-streaming providers.** Codex, Cursor, Copilot, Gemini all use the same `*agent.TextGenerationError` wrap pattern at their `GenerateText` call sites. Easy to extend.\n\n### Issues / suggestions\n\n**`looksLikeUnrecognizedFlag` substring matching is broader than ideal**\n(`cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/generate_streaming.go:185-198`)\nChecks for `\"stream-json\"`, `\"verbose\"`, or `\"include-partial\"` in stderr to detect old CLIs. `\"verbose\"` is a very common word; an unrelated error message containing \"verbose\" could trigger the fallback. The AND-logic with a rejection phrase mitigates this, but `\"output-format\"` would be a tighter discriminator. Not blocking — current logic is correct in practice for known Claude CLI versions.\n\n**Redundant `cancel != nil` clause in DeadlineExceeded check**\n(`cmd/entire/cli/explain.go:1218`)\n```go\nif errors.Is(err, context.DeadlineExceeded) || (cancel != nil && errors.Is(runCtx.Err(), context.DeadlineExceeded)) {\n```\nWhen `cancel == nil`, `runCtx == ctx`, so `runCtx.Err()` == `err` propagation: the first clause already catches all cases the second could. Simplification: drop the second clause entirely.\n\n**Streaming switch lacks an explicit `default` case**\n(`cmd/entire/cli/explain.go:1340-1360`)\nWhen `attempt.streaming == true` AND all three phase flags are set (i.e., `PhaseDone` was reached), the switch falls through to the non-streaming code which renders \"provider produced no output\" — incorrect for that hypothetical state. Logically unreachable (`PhaseDone` only fires on success, and a successful generation returns before timeout classification), but a `default` case returning a generic \"timed out\" message would make the invariant explicit and survive future refactors.\n\n**`TextGenerationError.Stderr` has no size cap**\n(`cmd/entire/cli/agent/text_generator_cli.go:18-23`)\nA misbehaving CLI that dumps megabytes of stderr would have all of it captured and embedded in the error chain, then surfaced verbatim in the diagnostic `stderr:` row. Worth truncating to ~4 KB with an \"(N bytes truncated)\" suffix.\n\n**`outputTokensEstimate` arithmetic is unbounded**\n(`cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/generate_streaming.go:155`)\n`outputTokensEstimate += len(text) / 4` accumulates across the streaming call. `int` overflow is theoretically possible for extremely long generations (~1 billion characters), but unrealistic in practice. The 4-chars-per-token heuristic is also coarse; worth a comment that this is a UI counter, not an authoritative token count (the final value at `PhaseDone` comes from the API's actual `usage.output_tokens`).\n\n**`switch g := generator.(type)` assumes future generators won't need progress**\n(`cmd/entire/cli/summarize/summarize.go:66-71`)\nTwo cases today (`*ClaudeGenerator`, `*TextGeneratorAdapter`). A future external generator that needs progress would have to be added to this switch. Consider a `progressReceiver` interface as a follow-up if more generator types appear:\n```go\ntype progressReceiver interface { setProgress(agent.ProgressFn) }\n```\n\n## Test coverage\n\n### Strong\n\n- `streamClaudeResponse` (4 tests): success path, 404 envelope, malformed-line skip, no-result error\n- `GenerateTextStreaming` (3 tests): success, fallback on unrecognized flag, envelope-error surfaced\n- `summaryProgressWriter` (4 tests): non-TTY rendering, throttle rule, ACCESSIBLE mode, attempt-state population\n- `timeoutDiagnostic` (5 tests): all five state branches\n- `AsStreamingTextGenerator` (4 tests): mirrors `AsTextGenerator` pattern\n- `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI` tests updated for the 4-return signature\n\n### Gaps\n\n**Synthetic fixtures don't reflect real Claude output**\n`testdata/stream_success.jsonl` and `testdata/stream_error_404.jsonl` were hand-crafted to match the parser. The smoke test caught that the test fixtures *passed* but the real `claude --print --output-format stream-json` returned a different shape (missing `--include-partial-messages` produced `assistant` events instead of `stream_event`). Suggest capturing a real fixture by running the actual CLI and checking it in.\n\n**Per-provider error-wrap behavior is untested**\nCodex/Cursor/Copilot/Gemini's `GenerateText` wraps errors into `*TextGenerationError` — but no test asserts this wrap actually happens for each provider. A single per-provider test using a stub `CommandRunner` that returns a non-zero exit would lock in the contract.\n\n**`Flush()` is not directly tested**\n`summaryProgressWriter.Flush()` is exercised end-to-end via the failure path, but no unit test asserts that calling Flush after an inplace `updateLine` clears `lastLine` and emits `\\r\\033[2K`.\n\n**Streaming-switch fall-through state is untested**\nThe `timeoutDiagnostic` invariant that \"streaming=true + all phases reached\" never produces a `DeadlineExceeded` is documented but not tested.\n\n## Performance implications\n\n- **Streaming subprocess overhead.** Negligible. `bufio.Scanner` with 4 MiB max-line is comparable to the prior buffered read.\n- **Progress callback fire rate.** TTY mode short-circuits via `lastLine == line`; non-TTY throttles to 500ms OR 25% jump. Reasonable. Per-event work is constant-time (string format + `Fprintln`).\n- **Drain after scanner.** `io.Copy(io.Discard, stdout)` reads to EOF — bounded by what the subprocess writes, which terminates when it's killed/done.\n- **Stderr capture.** Bounded by subprocess output; see size-cap suggestion above.\n\n## Security considerations\n\n- **Subprocess isolation preserved.** `cmd.Dir = os.TempDir()`, `cmd.Env = agent.StripGitEnv(os.Environ())`, `--setting-sources \"\"` all carry over from the existing non-streaming path. No new attack surface.\n- **Prompt passed via stdin** (not flags). Avoids argument-injection risks.\n- **No new shell-out paths.** The `fakeStreamCmd` test helper uses `sh -c` to write fixture data, but only in test code. Production code uses `exec.CommandContext(\"claude\", ...)` directly with no shell.\n- **stderr-surfacing in diagnostic** could leak sensitive info if a misbehaving provider CLI prints credentials. Risk is low (providers shouldn't print secrets to stderr) but worth keeping in mind. Truncation would also help.\n- **Provider name injection.** `provider.Name` comes from settings (local user-controlled trust boundary), so embedding it in `\"... provider: %s\\n\"` is safe.\n\n## Following project conventions\n\n- ✅ `t.Parallel()` on all new tests except those with documented exceptions (`TestSummaryProgressWriter_Accessible` uses `t.Setenv`; `TestResolveSummaryTimeout_DefaultZero` uses `t.Chdir`).\n- ✅ `mise run check` green (per HEAD verification).\n- ✅ `golangci-lint` clean. `nolint:wrapcheck` directives are placed and justified.\n- ✅ No `t.Setenv` after `t.Parallel()` panics; no `os.Chdir` calls outside `t.Chdir`.\n- ✅ Errors flow through `errors.As` correctly; `*TextGenerationError.Unwrap()` preserves typed inner errors.\n- ✅ Constants extracted to satisfy `goconst` (e.g. `providerCLIBinaryClaude`, `streamEventTypeStreamEvent`).\n- ⚠️ One stale doc comment at `text_generator_cli.go:38` (or thereabouts) references `*summarize.TextGenerationError` but the type is in `agent`. Cosmetic.\n\n## Risk assessment\n\n**Low risk overall.** The streaming path has a fallback to non-streaming `GenerateText` for older Claude CLIs, so the worst case (Claude CLI changes its stream format again) is \"no live progress, summary still works.\" The deadline policy change is the most user-visible behavior shift — anyone relying on the 5-minute default cap from PR #1204 will now see uncapped runs until they set `summary_timeout_seconds`. The PR description notes this and provides the one-line remediation (`entire configure --summarize-timeout-seconds 300`).\n\n## Recommended actions before merge\n\n**Blockers:** None.\n\n**Should do (small, contained):**\n1. Truncate `TextGenerationError.Stderr` to ~4 KB to bound diagnostic payloads.\n2. Simplify the `cancel != nil` clause in the DeadlineExceeded check (drop the second clause).\n3. Fix the stale `*summarize.TextGenerationError` doc comment in `text_generator_cli.go`.\n\n**Could do (follow-up PR):**\n1. Capture real stream-json fixtures from a live Claude run, replace synthetic ones.\n2. Add a `default` arm in the `timeoutDiagnostic` streaming switch.\n3. Add a `progressReceiver` interface so future generators don't require a type-switch update.\n4. Per-provider tests for the `*TextGenerationError` wrap.\n5. Truncate `outputTokensEstimate` arithmetic with a comment about the heuristic.\n6. ACCESSIBLE mode propagation to the failure `✗` glyph (renders via `newStatusStyles` which doesn't currently check the env var).\n\n## Verdict\n\n**Approve.** Ship after addressing the three \"should do\" items above, or accept them as carry-forward and ship now with a tracked follow-up issue. The implementation faithfully delivers the design goals, has solid test coverage, and is structurally clean. The smoke-test fix that landed in the squash (`--include-partial-messages` + `TextGeneratorAdapter` streaming detection) is the most consequential addition over the prior review passes — it converts the feature from \"machinery exists\" to \"users actually see live progress.\""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3532,"cache_read_input_tokens":