e-per-event, throttle rule, accessible mode glyph swap, attempt-state population)\n- Deadline policy (0 default, flag override, setting override, negative-treated-as-unset)\n- 5 diagnostic state branches (streaming stuck before/during 3 phases, non-streaming with/without output)\n- Provider CLI name lookup (via `TestTimeoutDiagnostic_StreamingStuckBeforeConnecting` which asserts `\"claude\"` appears in the try-row)\n\n**E2E canary** (Vogon agent, the deterministic non-API fake): all 4 tests pass.\n\n## 2. Manual smoke tests (real Claude CLI, real subprocess, real money)\n\nYou ran these yourself; here are the results we observed:\n\n| # | Test | Command | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | List checkpoints | `$ENTIRE checkpoint list` | 56 checkpoints visible, picked `e3d911c520d2` (cats essay) |\n| 2 | Happy path, live progress on TTY | `$ENTIRE checkpoint explain --checkpoint e3d911c520d2 --generate --force` | All 4 phases rendered: Sending → Provider responded (TTFT 1.6s, 13k cached) → Writing summary (in-place updates) → ✓ Summary generated (7.6s, 420 output tokens, 9.8s total). No auto-timeout fired. |\n| 3 | Timeout diagnostic at 3s | `--summary-timeout-seconds 3` | After PhaseFirstToken fired but before PhaseDone: `✗ Timed out after 3s: model responded but did not finish` with cause + try hints. Exit code 1. |\n| 4 | **Network offline at 10s** (the most important diagnostic) | offline + `--summary-timeout-seconds 10` | After PhaseConnecting fired but PhaseFirstToken did not: `✗ Timed out after 10s: provider sent request but received no response` — correct phase-distinguished diagnostic (NOT \"never sent its request\" and NOT \"model responded but did not finish\"). |\n| 5 | Help text confirms no auto-deadline | `$ENTIRE checkpoint explain --help \\| grep summary-timeout` | `0 = use setting; if setting is also unset or 0, no automatic deadline applies.` |\n| 6 | Non-TTY pipe behavior | `... \\| cat` | Same content, each `→ Writing summary...` on its own line (no `\\r` in-place updates), no ANSI color escapes |\n| 7 | ACCESSIBLE mode | `env ACCESSIBLE=1 ...` with `--summary-timeout-seconds 3` | `->` arrows instead of `→`, no unicode in progress lines (failure `✗` glyph is a known carry-forward gap) |\n\nThe offline test (#4) is the headline validation: a real network failure produced the correct attribution. The pre-PR-#876 3-cause shrug (\"model slow / can't reach API / API degraded\") would have made you guess; now it tells you specifically.\n\n## 3. Lint and format\n\n- `mise run lint` — 0 issues. Verified independently against `origin/main` baseline (caught a `goconst` issue during development that the chunk-level review missed because golangci-lint's `--new` mode hides issues invisible against the previous commit).\n- `mise run fmt` — no diff.\n- `mise run check` (= fmt + lint + test:ci) — green on HEAD `0b9993ee4`.\n\n## 4. Reviewer agent passes (during development)\n\n| Pass | Reviewer | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Plan review (4 rounds) | spec/plan-document-reviewer | Approved after fixing 8+5+2 issues across rounds |\n| Per-chunk spec compliance (×8 chunks) | superpowers spec reviewer | Approved (some chunks needed fixes/reviews) |\n| Per-chunk code quality (×7 chunks) | superpowers code reviewer | Approved with carry-forward polish notes |\n| Final branch-level review | superpowers code reviewer | Approved with 1 important fix (stale flag help text — corrected) + minor notes |\n| `/review` on the final PR | review skill (Sonnet) | Approved with 3 \"should fix\" items deferred to follow-up + minor notes |\n| Cursor Bugbot | (you triggered) | Running on `0b9993ee4` per your earlier note — results visible in the PR |\n\n## 5. Caveats and gaps (transparency)\n\n- **Stream-event format coverage is parser-defined, not Claude-defined.** Tests use synthetic fixtures that match our parser's expectations. If Anthropic ships a stream format change that our parser silently doesn't handle, automated tests would pass while production drifts. The smoke test (#2 above) and the offline test (#4) cover this for the current Claude CLI version (`2.1.141`) but won't catch future drift.\n- **Test #4 requires manual offline state** — not in the automated suite.\n- **In-place TTY line updates** (test #2's `Writing summary... (~Nk tokens)` rewriting itself) can only be visually confirmed on a real terminal, not via test capture. You verified this manually.\n- **Per-provider error-wrap tests are absent.** Codex/Cursor/Copilot/Gemini's `GenerateText` wraps errors into `*agent.TextGenerationError` — the wrap mechanism is shared (in `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI`) and tested there, but the per-provider call sites don't have direct unit tests for the wrap. The final reviewer noted this as a follow-up.\n\n## What this gives confidence on\n\n✅ The streaming path fires correctly against real Claude (test #2 — observed live progress phases)\n✅ The diagnostic correctly distinguishes the three streaming failure modes (test #3 = \"did not finish\"; test #4 = \"received no response\"; would-be test for \"never sent its request\" requires a stalled `claude` binary which is harder to fake)\n✅ Opt-in deadline policy works (test #5 confirms help text; test #2 confirms no auto-timeout)\n✅ Non-TTY and ACCESSIBLE modes degrade correctly (tests #6, #7)\n✅ Lint, format, full test suite all green\n\nWant me to paste any of this into the PR description, or is it just for your own reference?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":414,"cache_read_input_tokens":751133,"output_tokens":4260,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":414,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":4260,"cache_read_input_tokens":751133,"cache_creation_input_tokens":414,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0