{"parentUuid":"45f4f41d-c319-4357-b8e8-6699cbcda09b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_017nq3o3zznXq1gKeu9L5YZM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Testing the smoke-test fix specifically\n\n## What the fix was\n\nTwo bugs found by manually running the binary, both invisible to the unit suite:\n\n**Bug 1:** `claudecode/generate_streaming.go` was missing the `--include-partial-messages` flag.\n**Bug 2:** `summarize/GenerateFromTranscript` only set the progress callback on `*ClaudeGenerator`, but production uses `*TextGeneratorAdapter`.\n\nBoth got folded into commit `ea1617cff` during the 8→3 squash.\n\n## How I verified bug 1 existed\n\nAfter implementing streaming, the smoke test showed:\n```\nGenerating checkpoint summary... (transcript: 40.7 KB, provider: claude-code)\n✓ Summary generated for e3d911c520d2\n```\n\nThe 4 progress phase events were missing. I ran the **real Claude CLI** directly with the flags the implementation was passing:\n\n```fish\necho \"hello world\" | claude --print --output-format stream-json --verbose --model haiku --setting-sources \"\"\n```\n\nOutput was:\n- `{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"init\",...}` ← we don't dispatch on this\n- `{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{...}}` ← we don't dispatch on this\n- `{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{...}}` ← same\n- `{\"type\":\"rate_limit_event\",...}` ← we don't dispatch on this\n- `{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",...}` ← captured but only fires PhaseDone\n\n**Zero `stream_event` types.** The parser's PhaseConnecting/FirstToken/Generating patterns never matched because they targeted `stream_event` envelopes which Claude wasn't emitting under those flags.\n\nThe fix discovery was `claude --print --help | grep -i partial`:\n```\n--include-partial-messages    Include partial message chunks as they arrive\n```\n\n## How I verified bug 1 was fixed\n\nRe-ran the same prompt WITH the new flag:\n\n```fish\necho \"hello\" | claude --print --output-format stream-json --include-partial-messages --verbose --model haiku --setting-sources \"\"\n```\n\nOutput now included:\n- `{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"status\",\"status\":\"requesting\",...}` ← matches PhaseConnecting pattern ✓\n- `{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"message_start\",\"message\":{\"usage\":{...}}},\"ttft_ms\":1238}` ← matches PhaseFirstToken ✓\n- `{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"delta\":{\"type\":\"thinking_delta\",\"thinking\":\"...\"}}}` (many) ← matches PhaseGenerating ✓\n- ... eventually `{\"type\":\"result\",...}` ← captured for PhaseDone ✓\n\nI compared event by event to the parser's `makeProgressDispatcher` switch cases. Every phase now has a matching event type in the real stream.\n\n## How I verified bug 2 existed\n\nAfter fixing bug 1, the smoke test **still** showed no progress events. I traced:\n\n1. Checked `.entire/logs/entire.log` for the `\"claude CLI rejected stream-json flags; falling back to non-streaming\"` warning — **not present**. So the fallback didn't fire; the streaming path was being attempted.\n2. Greped for `ClaudeGenerator` to find where it's instantiated in production: `grep -rn \"ClaudeGenerator{\" cmd/entire/cli/ --include=\"*.go\"`. Found only ONE callsite — `defaultTextGeneratorFactory` in `summarize/claude.go`, used as a fallback when `generator == nil`.\n3. Followed the real production path: `cmd/entire/cli/explain_summary_provider.go:buildCheckpointSummaryProvider` returns `&summarize.TextGeneratorAdapter{...}`, NOT `&summarize.ClaudeGenerator{...}`.\n4. Read `TextGeneratorAdapter.Generate` — it called `g.TextGenerator.GenerateText` directly (non-streaming), with no `AsStreamingTextGenerator` check.\n\nSo even though `ClaudeCodeAgent` *implemented* `StreamingTextGenerator`, the production summary pipeline never invoked it. The chunk-4 type assertion in `GenerateFromTranscript` was checking for the wrong type.\n\n## How I verified bug 2 was fixed\n\nThree changes made:\n1. Added streaming-capability detection to `TextGeneratorAdapter.Generate` (mirroring the same pattern as `ClaudeGenerator.Generate`).\n2. Changed the type assertion in `GenerateFromTranscript` from `if cg, ok := generator.(*ClaudeGenerator)` to a switch that handles both `*ClaudeGenerator` AND `*TextGeneratorAdapter`.\n3. Added unexported `progress agent.ProgressFn` field to `TextGeneratorAdapter`.\n\nRebuilt the binary, re-ran the smoke test:\n\n```\nGenerating checkpoint summary... (transcript: 40.7 KB, provider: claude-code)\n→ Sending request to provider...\n→ Provider responded (TTFT 1.8s, 20.2k cached input tokens) -- generating...\n→ Writing summary... (~4 tokens)\n→ Writing summary... (~31 tokens)\n→ Writing summary... (~57 tokens)\n→ Writing summary... (~75 tokens)\n→ Writing summary... (~101 tokens)\n→ Writing summary... (~156 tokens)\n→ Writing summary... (~209 tokens)\n→ Writing summary... (~261 tokens)\n→ Writing summary... (~324 tokens)\n→ Writing summary... (~365 tokens)\n✓ Summary generated (7.6s, 421 output tokens)\n✓ Summary generated for e3d911c520d2\n```\n\nLive progress events fired correctly. The token counter incremented through real generation. The final `PhaseDone` came from `cmd.Wait()` with real `duration_ms` and `usage.output_tokens` from the API.\n\n## On \"real responses instead of synthetic\"\n\nThe fix itself doesn't change the test fixtures — they're still synthetic JSONL files in `testdata/`. The reason we got away with this is:\n\n| Layer | What's tested | How |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Parser correctness** | `streamClaudeResponse` correctly decodes events of the right shape and dispatches phases | Synthetic JSONL fixtures matching the parser's expected event types |\n| **Subprocess wiring** | `GenerateTextStreaming` correctly invokes claude with the right flags, handles cmd lifecycle, falls back on old CLIs | Mocked `CommandRunner` returning canned stdout from synthetic fixtures |\n| **Production wiring** | `TextGeneratorAdapter.Generate` actually fires streaming when the underlying agent supports it | NOT directly unit-tested — caught by the smoke test |\n| **Real protocol agreement** | Claude's actual stream-json output shape matches what our parser expects | NOT in CI — only validated by manual smoke tests |\n\nThe bugs both lived in layers that the synthetic fixtures couldn't catch:\n- **Bug 1**: synthetic fixtures had the events we *wanted* to see. The CLI args used to generate those events were never validated against the real CLI.\n- **Bug 2**: synthetic fixtures tested the parser in isolation. The production path that *invokes* the parser (`TextGeneratorAdapter` → `AsStreamingTextGenerator` → streaming generator) is wired through several layers; the unit tests stub out the intermediate layers and never exercise the actual production wiring.\n\nThe thing that caught both bugs was the manual end-to-end run against a real `claude` binary against a real checkpoint. Specifically:\n\n1. **Ran the binary**, observed missing events\n2. **Ran `claude` directly** with the same flags, saw what events Claude actually emits\n3. **Read the help text** of `claude --print --help` to find the missing flag\n4. **Re-ran** with the flag, confirmed event shape\n5. **Re-ran the binary**, observed still no events\n6. **Read the logs** to confirm the fallback didn't fire\n7. **Grepped the production code** to find which generator was actually instantiated\n8. **Read `TextGeneratorAdapter`** and saw the missing streaming-capability check\n9. **Made the fix**, re-ran the binary, observed live events\n\nEach step was a check-then-act loop: form a hypothesis from observed behavior, run a targeted command to confirm or refute, then act on the confirmed signal. No bug was fixed without first reproducing it by exercise of the actual code path.\n\n## What this means for confidence\n\nThe fix is verified by **direct observation against the live system**, not by tests. The tests still pass (using synthetic fixtures) but didn't catch these bugs and wouldn't catch a similar future drift in Claude's protocol either. To improve this:\n\n- **Capture real fixtures** (which we drafted then reverted — your call, but the option's documented).\n- **Add an integration test** that runs the real `claude` binary if installed (gated behind a build tag or env var like `INTEGRATION_CLAUDE=1`) and asserts at least one progress event fires.\n- **Smoke-test docs** — add a manual-verification checklist to `e2e/README.md` or similar so future contributors know to run `entire explain --generate` against a real checkpoint before merging changes to the streaming path.\n\nNone of these are in this PR. Right now the testing story for these specific code paths is: \"synthetic unit tests + the human did smoke tests on commit `0b9993ee4`.\""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4297,"cache_read_input_tokens":751547,"output_tokens":4915,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4297,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":4915,"cache_read_input_tokens":751547,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4297,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4297},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cb4XKXEBawQJ5qQL38kaH","type":"assistant","uuid":"4f552a0a-b2f2-406e-ae7c-e3fbe7526b05","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:38:15.701Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact-2","sessionId":"4944fa51-d7dd-4310-b62f-7802a196cd45","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"redact-2"}
