{"parentUuid":"6cd3ff11-d40a-4d3f-b481-097e3c6a5409","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01S6qkiuc5op9TXK3tafxfEo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good question — the answer is **mostly yes, but with one important asterisk**.\n\n## What's real for which agent\n\n| Agent | Summary text (the markdown output) | Live progress UI | Timeout/error diagnostic |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **claude-code** | Real (always was; calls `claude` CLI) | **Real** — verified by smoke test #2/#3/#4 | Real, phase-attributed from stream state |\n| **codex** | Real (calls `codex` CLI) | Silent — no streaming support | Real stderr capture, but **NOT smoke-tested by me** |\n| **gemini-cli** | Real (calls `gemini` CLI) | Silent | Real stderr capture, **NOT smoke-tested** |\n| **copilot-cli** | Real (calls `copilot` CLI) | Silent | Real stderr capture, **NOT smoke-tested** |\n| **cursor** | Real (calls `agent` CLI) | Silent | Real stderr capture, **NOT smoke-tested** |\n\nSo the precise statement:\n\n1. **Summary text from each agent is the agent's actual model output.** This was already true before this PR — the production code path has always invoked the real CLI for each provider. We didn't change this.\n2. **Live progress phases are real Claude stream events.** Verified end-to-end via your smoke test runs.\n3. **Failure diagnostic for Claude uses real captured stream state.** Verified (tests #3 model-finishing, #4 network-down).\n4. **Failure diagnostic for the other four providers uses real captured stderr** from their `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI` invocation — but I haven't actually run any of them against their real CLIs in this session.\n\n## The asterisk\n\nFor codex/cursor/copilot/gemini, the **code path IS real** (no mocking in production). What's happening:\n\n- `TextGeneratorAdapter.Generate` calls `AsStreamingTextGenerator` → returns false (these agents don't implement it) → falls through to `g.TextGenerator.GenerateText` → calls the agent's `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI` which invokes the real binary subprocess\n- On non-zero exit or timeout, the per-provider wrapper at `cmd/entire/cli/agent/<provider>/generate.go` wraps the error into `*agent.TextGenerationError` carrying the real captured `Stderr` and `StdoutBytes`\n- That error propagates up to `formatCheckpointSummaryError` which surfaces the real stderr in the diagnostic `stderr:` row\n\nThe mechanism is real. But I haven't *exercised* it. Reasons:\n\n1. I don't have all four CLIs installed locally to test against\n2. Forcing each into a timeout scenario takes setup (each provider rejects timeouts differently)\n3. The diagnostic logic for the non-streaming path is unit-tested (`TestTimeoutDiagnostic_NonStreamingNoOutput`, `TestTimeoutDiagnostic_NonStreamingWithOutput`) — those tests construct synthetic `*summaryAttempt` values to exercise the diagnostic branches, but they don't validate that real codex/gemini/etc. actually populate those fields correctly in practice.\n\n## What you'd need to fully validate the other providers\n\nFor each of {codex, gemini, copilot, cursor}:\n\n```fish\n# Switch the configured summary provider\n$ENTIRE configure --summarize-provider codex --summarize-model gpt-5\n\n# Happy path (real generation; real stderr stays empty on success)\n$ENTIRE checkpoint explain --checkpoint <id> --generate --force\n\n# Timeout diagnostic — the headline test\n$ENTIRE checkpoint explain --checkpoint <id> --generate --force --summary-timeout-seconds 3\n# Expected: \"✗ Timed out after 3s: <provider> was generating output when killed\"\n# OR:       \"✗ Timed out after 3s: <provider> produced no output\"\n# with a `stderr:` row showing whatever each CLI emits\n\n# Network down + short timeout\n# Expected: \"✗ Timed out after 5s: <provider> produced no output\" with stderr like \"connection refused\" or \"dial tcp\"\n```\n\nIf any of those four return the **expected diagnostic shapes** with real stderr embedded, you've validated the path end-to-end for that provider. Without doing that, you're trusting that:\n- The `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI` stderr-capture signature change works (it has unit tests)\n- The per-provider wrap into `*TextGenerationError` works (no unit tests; reviewed by reading the diff)\n- The `errors.As` unwrap at `generateCheckpointAISummary` correctly extracts `Stderr` and `StdoutBytes` (covered by `TestTimeoutDiagnostic_NonStreaming*` tests using synthetic `*summaryAttempt`)\n\nSo: **the type system says it works for all 5 agents, Claude is observed to work end-to-end, the other 4 are observed to work in pieces but not as a whole**. Reasonable confidence, but not \"verified\" in the same way Claude is.\n\nWant me to do at least one non-Claude smoke test if you have any of those CLIs installed? `codex` would be the most likely candidate."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4958,"cache_read_input_tokens":755844,"output_tokens":2962,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4958,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":2962,"cache_read_input_tokens":755844,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4958,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4958},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cb4XamjEULvCvq5Vza6ZR","type":"assistant","uuid":"6e387903-fd64-442e-a76e-f615bf381b56","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:41:08.475Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact-2","sessionId":"4944fa51-d7dd-4310-b62f-7802a196cd45","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"redact-2"}
