{"parentUuid":"66785b97-1027-482c-97e0-4e3a8bc429f8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01HqHVDBwrVBQkj3ca8sqkyD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2890,"cache_read_input_tokens":770461,"output_tokens":2274,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2890,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":2274,"cache_read_input_tokens":770461,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2890,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2890},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cb4Zj76WnZKzufy8fBi7q","type":"assistant","uuid":"4a0e37c9-243c-4f37-9d9c-7686cd650448","timestamp":"2026-05-15T15:08:46.411Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact-2","sessionId":"4944fa51-d7dd-4310-b62f-7802a196cd45","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"redact-2"}
{"parentUuid":"4a0e37c9-243c-4f37-9d9c-7686cd650448","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01HqHVDBwrVBQkj3ca8sqkyD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Short answer: **no, the chain of custody only goes that deep for Claude.** Other agents have a real but much shorter chain.\n\nHere's the breakdown by agent:\n\n## What's real for each agent's summary generation\n\n| Aspect | Claude | Codex / Gemini / Copilot / Cursor |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Summary text** (the markdown the model produces) | Real — from `claude` CLI's `result.result` field | **Real** — captured directly from the agent's CLI stdout |\n| **Live progress lines** (`→ Sending request...`, `→ Provider responded (TTFT ...)`, `→ Writing summary...`) | Real, with TTFT + cached-tokens + token counter from actual stream events | **None at all.** No progress events. The UI is silent between \"Generating checkpoint summary...\" and the final confirmation line. |\n| **TTFT / cached input tokens display** | Real — from Claude's `message_start` event | Not displayed |\n| **Final duration & output tokens display** | Real — from Claude's `result.duration_ms` and `usage.output_tokens` | Not displayed (only the wallclock duration of the overall `entire` command, which is OUR measurement, not the API's) |\n| **Failure diagnostic stderr** | Real — but mostly via PR #963's typed `*ClaudeError` path | **Real** — captured from the subprocess stderr via `*agent.TextGenerationError` (this PR added that) |\n\n## Why the asymmetry\n\nEach provider CLI speaks its own dialect. Claude's `--output-format stream-json --include-partial-messages` emits per-token events we can parse. Codex / Gemini / Copilot / Cursor either don't have an equivalent streaming protocol, or have one with a different schema. This PR didn't add streaming support for them — it added the framework (the `StreamingTextGenerator` capability interface), but only `ClaudeCodeAgent` implements it.\n\nSo when you `entire configure --summarize-provider codex` and run `--generate`, the path is:\n\n1. `entire` invokes `codex` as a subprocess (real)\n2. `codex` reads the prompt on stdin, runs its own model, writes the response to stdout (real)\n3. `entire` waits for `codex` to exit, captures the stdout as the summary text (real)\n4. UI shows \"Generating checkpoint summary...\" → [silence] → \"✓ Summary generated for ...\"\n5. If `codex` exits with an error, `*agent.TextGenerationError` wraps the real captured stderr; diagnostic surfaces it\n\nWhat's missing for non-Claude agents:\n- No \"→ Sending request to provider...\" line\n- No TTFT display\n- No live token counter\n- No in-place progress updates\n\n## What that means for \"is what I see real\"\n\nIf you switch to a non-Claude provider and watch the UI, the **only line during generation** is the initial:\n```\nGenerating checkpoint summary... (transcript: 40.7 KB, provider: codex)\n```\nThe `40.7 KB` and `codex` are real (from `len(scopedTranscript)` and `provider.Name`). Then silence. Then the final summary content. That content is whatever Codex's model wrote to stdout. No synthesis.\n\nOn failure, you'd see `✗ Timed out after Xs: codex was generating output when killed` or `✗ Timed out after Xs: codex produced no output`, with a `stderr:` row containing real captured bytes from the `codex` subprocess. That stderr is whatever the codex CLI actually printed — not synthesized.\n\n## To get the same depth for other agents\n\nEach would need:\n1. A streaming output mode in its CLI (Codex has it via `codex exec --json`, Gemini has SSE, etc. — they all differ)\n2. A per-provider `GenerateTextStreaming` implementation that translates that CLI's events into our `agent.GenerationProgress` phases\n3. Tests against a captured fixture of that CLI's real output\n\nThat's straightforward but per-provider work. Not in this PR; could be follow-up PRs.\n\n## TL;DR\n\nFor all 5 agents, the **summary content** is real (and always was). For Claude specifically, the **live progress phases and the numbers in them** are also real (verified end-to-end). For the other four agents, there are no live progress phases at all — just silence during generation, then the real summary content. The diagnostic on failure captures real stderr for all of them."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2890,"cache_read_input_tokens":770461,"output_tokens":2274,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2890,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":2274,"cache_read_input_tokens":770461,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2890,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2890},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cb4Zj76WnZKzufy8fBi7q","type":"assistant","uuid":"e699f151-5ce1-485d-a154-92f00412a66a","timestamp":"2026-05-15T15:09:07.257Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact-2","sessionId":"4944fa51-d7dd-4310-b62f-7802a196cd45","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"redact-2"}
