{"parentUuid":"f90cad82-4420-4dce-97f1-57c79a78ba81","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01T6VM5ZSgPZHa6nCkP9d6qA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- **Every non-Claude CLI already has streaming support.** I just confirmed it. The framework we built in this PR (the `StreamingTextGenerator` interface + `AsStreamingTextGenerator` detector + `TextGeneratorAdapter` dispatch) was explicitly designed to be per-agent extensible — each agent opts in independently.\n- **Adding streaming for any agent is now a plug-in operation.** No changes needed to the progress writer, the diagnostic, the deadline policy, the interface itself, or the call sites. Just add one method on the agent struct.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n## Streaming support across all four non-Claude agents\n\n| Agent | Existing CLI flag | Format |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Codex** | `--json` | JSONL events to stdout |\n| **Gemini** | `--output-format stream-json` | Stream JSON |\n| **Cursor** | `--output-format stream-json --stream-partial-output` | Stream JSON with text deltas |\n| **Copilot** | `--output-format json --stream <mode>` | JSONL + explicit stream mode |\n\nEvery one of them can emit per-token events. We just don't consume them.\n\n## What the existing framework gives us \"for free\"\n\nWhen `TextGeneratorAdapter.Generate` runs (in `summarize/text_generator.go:40`), it does:\n\n```go\nif streamer, ok := agent.AsStreamingTextGenerator(g.TextGenerator); ok {\n    result, err := streamer.GenerateTextStreaming(ctx, prompt, g.Model, g.progress)\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nThe detector returns `true` *for any type that implements the interface*. So if `*CodexAgent` grows a `GenerateTextStreaming` method, this branch picks it up automatically — no other code changes needed.\n\nThe progress writer, the diagnostic state attribution, the deadline policy, the UI rendering — all of that already handles whatever events the streaming generator dispatches. Per-agent implementations only need to:\n\n1. Invoke their CLI with its streaming flag\n2. Parse the JSONL/SSE/whatever format\n3. Translate that protocol's events into our `agent.GenerationProgress` phases\n\n## Concrete shape of adding Codex streaming\n\nIt's basically a copy of what we did for Claude, swapping the CLI args and the event parser. Roughly 150-200 lines per agent (file + tests + fixture):\n\n```go\n// cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/generate_streaming.go (new file)\npackage codex\n\nfunc (c *CodexAgent) GenerateTextStreaming(\n    ctx context.Context, prompt, model string, progress agent.ProgressFn,\n) (string, error) {\n    args := []string{\"exec\", \"--skip-git-repo-check\", \"--json\"}\n    if model != \"\" { args = append(args, \"--model\", model) }\n    args = append(args, \"-\")\n\n    // ... cmd.Start(), pipe stdout, scanner loop, drain, Wait — same shape as claudecode ...\n    // Per-event translation: Codex's events → agent.GenerationProgress phases\n}\n```\n\nThe event-translation layer is the per-agent piece. Codex's events look different from Claude's (e.g., Codex uses `{\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"content\":\"...\"}` style instead of `stream_event,content_block_delta`). Each agent needs its own dispatcher.\n\n## What this means for fixing the non-Claude UX gap\n\nThis is a **purely additive** follow-up. No refactoring needed:\n\n- This PR (#964) ships the framework + Claude implementation\n- Follow-up PRs add per-agent streaming, one agent at a time\n- Each follow-up is small (~200 lines of code + tests + manual smoke test against the real CLI)\n- Each follow-up flips that agent from \"silent during generation\" to \"live progress\" without touching anything else\n\nOrder I'd suggest based on user prevalence:\n1. **Codex** — most commonly used non-Claude agent in your setup; `--json` is simple JSONL\n2. **Gemini** — `stream-json` format probably resembles Claude's enough to reuse parsing patterns\n3. **Cursor** — has explicit `--stream-partial-output` flag\n4. **Copilot** — most complex, has a separate `--stream <mode>` toggle\n\n## Scope question for you"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1155,"cache_read_input_tokens":778020,"output_tokens":3432,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1155,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3432,"cache_read_input_tokens":778020,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1155,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1155},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cb4ZvpLn73onH25JC4AVV","type":"assistant","uuid":"79975882-8164-4084-bac2-db6c97447fc5","timestamp":"2026-05-15T15:11:51.536Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact-2","sessionId":"4944fa51-d7dd-4310-b62f-7802a196cd45","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"redact-2"}
