ter `idle` elapses.\",\"line\":null,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/explain.go\"}\n{\"author\":\"Copilot\",\"body\":\"In ACCESSIBLE mode the progress output is intended to contain no ANSI escapes, but `newSummaryProgressWriter` still uses `newStatusStyles(w)`, which will enable lipgloss coloring whenever `w` is a TTY. Consider disabling `styles.colorEnabled` (or bypassing `styles.render`) when `IsAccessibleMode()` is true so arrows/checkmarks are always plain text.\\n```suggestion\\n\\tstyles := newStatusStyles(w)\\n\\tif IsAccessibleMode() {\\n\\t\\tstyles.colorEnabled = false\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\treturn \\u0026summaryProgressWriter{\\n\\t\\tw:       w,\",\"line\":null,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/explain.go\"}\n{\"author\":\"Copilot\",\"body\":\"This test is marked `t.Parallel()` but mutates the package-level `defaultTextGeneratorFactory`. That can race with other tests (and with other parallel tests that also override the factory), especially under `-race`. Consider removing `t.Parallel()` here or guarding the global override with a mutex/test-serial helper.\",\"line\":null,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/summarize/summarize_test.go\"}\n{\"author\":\"Copilot\",\"body\":\"The real Claude stream-json output (see added fixtures) includes `ttft_ms` at the top level of the NDJSON line, not nested under `event`. With the current struct tags, TTFT will decode as 0, so downstream progress reporting will be wrong. Consider adding a top-level `TTFTms` field on `StreamEvent` (and/or supporting both locations) and updating the dispatcher accordingly.\",\"line\":null,\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/response.go\"}\n{\"author\":\"Copilot\",\"body\":\"`makeProgressDispatcher` pulls TTFT from `ev.Event.TTFTms` and reports “cached input tokens” using `CacheReadInputTokens`. In the real stream fixtures, `ttft_ms` is a top-level field, and the “cached input tokens” shown in the output correspond to `cache_creation_input_tokens` (not `cache_read_input_tokens`, which is often 0). This will caus