{"parentUuid":"9c4fc67e-1bdc-4faf-a419-2eaa489f8030","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_017uERzbBqUdeWbakDQZJngT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Code Review: PR #964 (HEAD `252e320a5`)\n\n## Overview\n\nThis PR delivers the work originally scoped in draft #964: live progress UI for `entire explain --generate` and an observable-state timeout diagnostic that replaces the 3-cause shrug from PR #876. It builds on the timeout-configurability foundation from recently-merged PR #1204 and removes the 5-minute automatic deadline that #1204 left in place — timeouts are now opt-in only via `--summary-timeout-seconds` / `summary_timeout_seconds`.\n\n**Diff:** 23 files, +1,444 / −175. About half is tests + fixtures.\n**Commits:** 5. Three feat commits delivering the mechanism, policy, and UX; two fix commits (test date-rot fix, Cursor Bugbot response).\n**Verification:** `mise run check` green locally, manual smoke tests confirmed end-to-end (live progress phases, timeout diagnostic at 3s, network-offline diagnostic, ACCESSIBLE/non-TTY rendering).\n\n## Code quality and style\n\n### Strengths\n\n- **Clean abstraction boundary.** The new `agent.StreamingTextGenerator` capability interface mirrors the existing `TextGenerator` pattern exactly — same shape, same `As*` detector, same `DeclaredCaps` field. New agents can opt in without touching any of the surrounding infrastructure.\n- **Subprocess lifecycle is correct.** `cmd.Start()` → scanner → `io.Copy(io.Discard, stdout)` drain → `cmd.Wait()`. The drain prevents a `bufio.ErrTooLong` from deadlocking `Wait()` on a blocked pipe.\n- **Envelope errors win over ctx-cancel.** `if final != nil && final.IsError` is checked before `ctx.Err()` in `GenerateTextStreaming`. The recent fix in commit `252e320a5` extends this discipline upstream by removing the `cancel != nil && errors.Is(runCtx.Err(), DeadlineExceeded)` clause that could mask typed errors.\n- **Provider-neutral UI.** No \"Anthropic\" / \"Claude\" hardcoded in user-facing strings. The single source of truth for provider→CLI-binary mapping now lives in `agent.SummaryCLIBinaryName`.\n- **TTY / non-TTY / ACCESSIBLE rendering.** Three modes correctly handled: in-place `\\r` updates on TTY, one-line-per-event in CI, ASCII glyphs + no ANSI under `ACCESSIBLE=1`.\n- **The opt-in deadline policy is the right default.** Issue #1198's root cause was an auto-default that truncated legitimate generations; making the deadline opt-in eliminates that class of bug entirely. The diagnostic only ever explains a timeout the user explicitly requested.\n\n### Fixes since prior review\n\n**Commit `4be64e665`** — Date-rot in `cmd/entire/cli/review/manifest_test.go`. Three tests hardcoded `time.Date(2026, 5, 8, ...)` as the session anchor; `session.StateStore.Load` auto-deletes sessions older than 7 days, so the tests passed yesterday (6d after) and failed today (7d after). Switched to `time.Now().UTC().Add(-time.Hour)`. Unrelated to the streaming work but blocking CI; reasonable to fold here.\n\n**Commit `252e320a5`** — Two Cursor Bugbot findings:\n1. Dropped the `(cancel != nil && errors.Is(runCtx.Err(), DeadlineExceeded))` clause that could convert a typed `*ClaudeError` 404 into a generic \"timed out\" message when ctx fired concurrently.\n2. Unified `providerCLIName` (in explain.go) with `summaryProviderBinaries` (in agent/) via the new exported `agent.SummaryCLIBinaryName` helper. Eliminates the parallel-map drift risk.\n\nBoth fixes are correct and well-scoped.\n\n## Specific suggestions\n\nThese are minor — none blocking:\n\n### Code\n\n- **`text_generator_cli.go:30`** — `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI` now returns `(result, capturedStderr string, stdoutBytes int, err error)`. The `//nolint:unparam` comment on this function (\"capturedStderr (result 1) is used by sub-package callers ... even though intra-package tests blank it\") is technically wrong — `unparam` flags unused parameters/results, not always-zero ones. The comment should clarify it's about intra-package callers (the tests in this file pass `\"\"` and `0` because they don't construct `*TextGenerationError`), not about unused-ness. Minor.\n\n- **`claudecode/generate_streaming.go:185-198`** — `looksLikeUnrecognizedFlag` checks `\"verbose\"` as one of the streaming-flag substrings. `--verbose` is a common flag name across many CLIs; an unrelated `claude` error containing the word \"verbose\" could trigger the non-streaming fallback. The AND-logic with a rejection phrase mitigates this, but `\"output-format\"` would be tighter. Low risk in practice.\n\n- **`claudecode/generate_streaming.go:185-198`** — `\"include-partial\"` substring check is checked but `--include-partial-messages` IS now actually passed in the args (commit `ea1617cff`). So this check is no longer \"dead code\" — it'll correctly detect an old CLI that rejects this flag. Worth a one-line comment note that this was originally written before the flag was passed.\n\n- **`agent/text_generator_cli.go:18-23`** — `TextGenerationError.Stderr` has no size cap. A misbehaving provider CLI dumping megabytes of stderr would have all of it captured and surfaced verbatim in the diagnostic. Worth truncating to ~4 KB with an \"(N bytes truncated)\" suffix. Low risk; defensive.\n\n- **`explain.go:1407` (timeoutDiagnostic streaming switch)** — No `default` case. When `attempt.streaming == true` AND all three phases are reached, the switch falls through to the non-streaming branch which would render \"produced no output\" — incorrect for that state. Logically unreachable (PhaseDone fires only on success), but a `default` arm returning a generic message would make the invariant explicit.\n\n- **`explain.go:1568-1571`** — `Generating` phase emits `\"Writing summary... (~Nk tokens)\"` using a 4-chars-per-token estimate. The `~` flags it as approximate, which is right. Worth a one-line comment in the code making explicit that this is a UI heuristic and the final count at `PhaseDone` comes from the API's authoritative `usage.output_tokens`.\n\n### Tests\n\n- **Synthetic stream-json fixtures are still in use.** `testdata/stream_success.jsonl` and `testdata/stream_error_404.jsonl` are hand-crafted to match the parser's expected shape. They're functionally correct against the parser today, but tied to \"what the parser wants\" rather than \"what Claude emits.\" A future Claude format change would pass tests while breaking production. A captured-real-then-redacted fixture was attempted and reverted at user request earlier in the PR; tradeoffs were discussed and the synthetic fixture won. Acknowledged.\n\n- **Per-provider error-wrap tests are absent.** Codex / Cursor / Copilot / Gemini's `GenerateText` each wrap errors into `*agent.TextGenerationError` — this wrapping is shared mechanically via `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI`'s 4-return signature, but no test asserts that any specific provider's `GenerateText` returns the typed error. Would catch a future regression where someone \"simplifies\" a per-provider wrapper and accidentally drops the wrap.\n\n- **ACCESSIBLE-mode failure-glyph gap.** The progress writer correctly uses `->` and `*` in accessible mode, but `formatCheckpointSummaryError`'s failure renderer uses `✗` from `newStatusStyles(w).renderFailure(...)` which doesn't check `IsAccessibleMode()`. Verified manually during smoke test #7. Acceptable carry-forward; small follow-up.\n\n- **No test for the production wiring path.** `TextGeneratorAdapter.Generate` was the locus of the bug that the smoke test caught (streaming detection was on `ClaudeGenerator`, but production uses `TextGeneratorAdapter`). The fix is in commit `ea1617cff` — but there's no unit test that asserts \"given a streaming-capable agent, `TextGeneratorAdapter.Generate` fires the streaming path.\" Would be useful.\n\n## Performance implications\n\n- **Streaming subprocess overhead.** Negligible. `bufio.Scanner` with 4 MiB max-line is comparable to the prior buffered read. Per-event work is a constant-time switch dispatch + format + `Fprintln`.\n- **Progress callback fire rate.** TTY short-circuits via `lastLine == line`; non-TTY throttles to 500ms OR 25% jump. Reasonable.\n- **Drain after scanner.** Bounded by what the subprocess writes; terminates when subprocess exits.\n- **No new heavy allocations or goroutines** beyond the existing pattern.\n\n## Security considerations\n\n- **Subprocess isolation preserved.** `cmd.Dir = os.TempDir()`, `cmd.Env = agent.StripGitEnv(os.Environ())`, `--setting-sources \"\"` all carry over from the existing non-streaming path. No new attack surface.\n- **Prompt passed via stdin** (not as a CLI arg). Avoids argument-injection risk.\n- **No new shell-out paths in production.** The `fakeStreamCmd` test helper uses `sh -c`, but it's gated behind `_test.go` and not reachable from production.\n- **stderr surfacing in diagnostics.** Risk of leaking credentials if a misbehaving provider CLI prints secrets to stderr. Risk is low (providers shouldn't do this) but a size-cap (suggestion above) would also help bound disclosure.\n- **Provider name interpolation.** `provider.Name` comes from settings (local user-controlled trust boundary), so embedding it in `\"... provider: %s\\n\"` is safe.\n\n## Following project conventions\n\n- ✅ `t.Parallel()` on all new tests except those with `t.Chdir`/`t.Setenv` (documented).\n- ✅ `mise run check` green.\n- ✅ `golangci-lint` clean. `nolint` directives placed and justified.\n- ✅ `testutil.InitRepo` used (not raw `git init`).\n- ✅ Errors flow through `errors.As` correctly; `*TextGenerationError.Unwrap()` preserves typed inner errors.\n- ✅ Constants extracted to satisfy `goconst` (e.g., `streamEventTypeStreamEvent`).\n\n## Risks\n\n**Low risk overall.**\n\n- The streaming path has a fallback to non-streaming `GenerateText` for older Claude CLIs (`looksLikeUnrecognizedFlag`). Worst case: \"no live progress, summary still works.\"\n- The deadline policy change is the most user-visible behavior shift — anyone relying on the 5-minute default from #1204 will see uncapped runs until they explicitly set `summary_timeout_seconds`. PR description notes this with the one-line remediation.\n- The provider-binary unification (`SummaryCLIBinaryName` export) is purely refactoring; no behavior change.\n- The date-rot test fix in `manifest_test.go` is unrelated to the streaming work; folded into this PR pragmatically since it was blocking CI. Could be lifted into its own PR before merge if reviewers prefer.\n\n## Assessment\n\n**Approve.** The work is well-decomposed (3 feat commits + 2 fix commits, each with a clear scope), end-to-end verified by manual smoke tests against the real `claude` CLI (including the offline-network case), and the recent fixes correctly address the Cursor Bugbot findings. The minor suggestions above are polish items that don't block merge — they're better as a follow-up PR (alongside the four non-Claude-agent streaming implementations discussed earlier).\n\nSuggested before marking ready for human review:\n- Consider whether to lift the `manifest_test.go` date-rot fix (commit `4be64e665`) into its own PR for scope cleanliness. Optional.\n- Confirm CI passes on the latest push (was running when we left it)."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":865,"cache_read_input_tokens":845738,"output_tokens":4642,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":865,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":4642,"cache_read_input_tokens":845738,"cache_creation_input_tokens":865,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":865},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cb4dAkaJWjHY3yfL782zy","attributionSkill":