{"parentUuid":"e954784e-a487-4039-b040-1affb83d6bdc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01UyTQMws9kCNFUSz5BoB9X9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on what each CLI actually emits, here's what I found:\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- **Codex** emits `thread.started → turn.started → item.completed(agent_message) → turn.completed(usage: input/cached/output/reasoning tokens)`. For tool-using turns it also emits `item.started/completed(command_execution)` events. **No TTFT field.** Usage on `turn.completed` is comprehensive.\n- **Gemini** emits `init(session_id, model) → message(role: user) → message(role: assistant, delta:true, content)` chunks. Delta-based streaming. **No TTFT, no cached_tokens, no final usage event** in what I captured.\n- **Copilot** emits `session.mcp_servers_loaded → session.skills_loaded → session.tools_updated(model) → user.message → assistant.turn_start → assistant.message_delta(deltaContent)` chunks. Verbose, lots of session-loading prefix events. **No TTFT in captured sample; usage likely on a later event.**\n- **Cursor** needs `agent login` to test — I couldn't capture sample output. Per its `--help`: `stream-partial-output` flag with `stream-json` format, but the event schema is undocumented in my snapshot.\n- For SUMMARY generation specifically (no tools needed), each agent's stream collapses cleanly to our existing 4 phases: `Connecting (turn-start/session-init) → FirstToken (first assistant event) → Generating (deltas if any) → Done (turn-complete or stream-end)`.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n## Three approaches to consider\n\n### Approach 1 — Per-agent everything, unified UI shape (Recommended)\n\nEach agent gets its own `generate_streaming.go` + event struct + dispatcher in its own package. Each dispatcher translates that agent's events into our existing `agent.GenerationProgress` phases. The progress writer's render template stays universal but degrades gracefully (skips `TTFT` and `cached input tokens` when fields are zero).\n\n| Provider | What user sees |\n| --- | --- |\n| claude-code | `→ Provider responded (TTFT 1.6s, 13k cached input tokens) -- generating...` (unchanged) |\n| codex | `→ Provider responded (23.8k cached input tokens) -- generating...` (no TTFT field) |\n| gemini-cli | `→ Provider responded -- generating...` (no extras) |\n| copilot-cli | `→ Provider responded -- generating...` (deltas drive Generating updates) |\n| cursor | TBD when we capture real output |\n\nDone phase still shows duration + final tokens from each agent's terminal event (`turn.completed` for Codex, stream-end for Gemini, etc.).\n\n**Pros:** consistent UI vocabulary; users learn one mental model that works across providers; the diagnostic state attribution (PhaseConnecting → FirstToken → Done) keeps working; per-agent files are independent so a Codex protocol change doesn't risk Gemini.\n**Cons:** loses agent-specific richness — Codex's `item(command_execution)` events are dropped on the floor (not surfaced); Copilot's `session.skills_loaded` info is invisible.\n\n**Code shape:** ~150-200 lines per agent. No shared streaming helper. Test fixtures synthetic (per established pattern). Existing `summaryProgressWriter` and `timeoutDiagnostic` work as-is because the per-agent dispatcher emits the same `GenerationProgress` shape.\n\n### Approach 2 — Per-agent UI templates (\"native flavor\" per provider)\n\nEach agent's dispatcher emits per-agent strings into the progress writer. Codex shows `→ Codex running tool: <command>` lines, Copilot shows `→ Loading skill: <name>`, etc. The progress writer becomes pluggable per agent.\n\n**Pros:** users see what the agent is \"actually doing\" in its native idiom; richer feedback when tools/skills are in play.\n**Cons:** the diagnostic state attribution gets harder (phasesReached needs to map per-agent semantics); UI inconsistency across providers (users learn 5 different vocabularies); much more code; future agents need a third style.\n\n### Approach 3 — Pass through agent CLI stdout/stderr verbatim during streaming\n\nDon't parse the stream-json at all for non-Claude agents. Just let the agent's CLI write to the terminal directly while we capture stdout for the final summary. Lose the structured progress events; gain whatever the CLI naturally produces.\n\n**Pros:** zero parsing work per agent; trivially survives upstream protocol changes.\n**Cons:** loses ALL structured features — no in-place line updates, no diagnostic attribution on timeout, no consistent visual style, ANSI from the CLI's native TUI might conflict with our renderer. Effectively giving up on the unified explain UX for non-Claude.\n\n---\n\nI recommend **Approach 1**. The diagnostic attribution and consistent UI vocabulary are the actual value props from PR #964; throwing them away to gain \"Codex's command_execution events on screen\" feels like a poor trade. The richer per-agent events aren't relevant for summary generation anyway (no tools involved)."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1877,"cache_read_input_tokens":885446,"output_tokens":2184,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1877,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2184,"cache_read_input_tokens":885446,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1877,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1877},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cb4gPZu5DreaYdDVRMWCM","attributionSkill":"superpowers:brainstorming","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"3cb5fb85-c1d3-43f7-bc28-c0ebaf20049f","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:36:25.374Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"