{"parentUuid":"7cececcb-6e4b-437f-9042-5967c99420ec","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01YUaxREn6RLKxEjktD3y6aN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Design proposal — PR A (built-in non-Claude streaming)\n\nI'll present this in sections. Confirm each before I move on.\n\n### Section 1 — Architecture (shared template + per-agent parsers)\n\nAdd a new `StreamingGeneratorTemplate` to `cmd/entire/cli/agent/`, structurally parallel to `review/types/template.go`'s `ReviewerTemplate`:\n\n```go\n// cmd/entire/cli/agent/streaming_template.go (new)\ntype StreamingGeneratorTemplate struct {\n    AgentName   string\n    DisplayName string                                                            // for error wrapping (e.g., \"codex\")\n    BuildCmd    func(ctx context.Context, prompt, model string) *exec.Cmd        // per-agent argv + stdin\n    Parser      func(stdout io.Reader, progress ProgressFn) (result string, err error) // per-agent event→GenerationProgress translator\n\n    // Optional. Returns true when stderr indicates the CLI rejected a\n    // streaming flag (old version). Caller falls back to non-streaming\n    // GenerateText. nil means \"no fallback supported\".\n    LooksLikeUnrecognizedFlag func(stderr string) bool\n}\n\n// Generate runs cmd, scans stdout via Parser, drains and Waits. On\n// non-nil error, returns *TextGenerationError carrying stderr + stdout\n// bytes (same shape as RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI's error path).\nfunc (t *StreamingGeneratorTemplate) Generate(\n    ctx context.Context, prompt, model string, progress ProgressFn,\n) (string, error)\n```\n\nPer-agent files (4 new):\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/generate_streaming.go`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/generate_streaming.go`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/generate_streaming.go`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/generate_streaming.go`\n\nEach provides a `GenerateTextStreaming` method that constructs a `StreamingGeneratorTemplate` with that agent's `BuildCmd` + `Parser`, and delegates to `Generate`. Plus a per-agent stream-event struct that mirrors that CLI's JSONL schema.\n\n**`claudecode` stays as-is** (per your earlier choice). Two parallel patterns will exist for streaming until claudecode optionally migrates later.\n\n**Progress writer is unchanged.** It already handles the `agent.GenerationProgress` shape. Two formatter tweaks needed: when `TTFTms == 0`, omit the `TTFT X.Ys` clause; when `CachedInputTokens == 0`, omit the `Nk cached input tokens` clause. Result: same template renders cleanly across agents regardless of which fields they emit.\n\n### Section 2 — Per-agent event mapping\n\nFor each agent, the dispatcher maps native events to our 4 phases:\n\n| Agent | PhaseConnecting | PhaseFirstToken | PhaseGenerating | PhaseDone |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **codex** | `thread.started` (or `turn.started`) | first `item.completed` with `agent_message` | per-`item.completed` afterward | `turn.completed` (extract `usage.output_tokens`, no TTFT) |\n| **geminicli** | `init` | first `message` with `role:assistant, delta:true` | subsequent assistant deltas | stream EOF + final `message` (no separate Done event; compute duration in template, no usage available) |\n| **cursor** | TBD (need real capture during impl) | TBD | TBD | TBD |\n| **copilot-cli** | `assistant.turn_start` | first `assistant.message_delta` | subsequent `assistant.message_delta` events | turn-end event (TBD which one carries usage) |\n\nTool-use events (Codex's `command_execution`, Copilot's `session.skills_loaded`) are **ignored** — they don't apply to summary generation since the prompt doesn't authorize tools. If an agent emits them anyway (because the user authorized tools at a settings level), they're silently dropped from the UI.\n\nThe `Done` phase's final `OutputTokens` and `DurationMs` use whatever each agent's terminal event provides; agents without a final usage event get `OutputTokens = 0` and the template computes `DurationMs = time.Since(start)`.\n\n### Section 3 — Cursor authentication caveat\n\n`agent` (cursor's CLI) requires `agent login` or `CURSOR_API_KEY` to test. I couldn't capture its stream-json format during this brainstorm. The plan: during implementation, capture cursor's stream format once auth is set up (or use Anthropic-published docs if available); fall back to a \"best-effort dispatcher that fires Connecting at start, Done at EOF\" if the format proves opaque. This means cursor users might initially get a reduced UI (no FirstToken/Generating updates) until we get the format right. Worth flagging as a known gap.\n\n### Section 4 — Fallback semantics\n\nIf an agent's CLI doesn't support its streaming flag (older version), the template detects via `LooksLikeUnrecognizedFlag` and signals the per-agent method to fall back to `GenerateText` (the existing non-streaming path). No progress events fire in fallback. Mirrors claudecode's behavior.\n\n### Section 5 — Testing\n\nPer agent: synthetic stream-json fixtures (consistent with the existing claudecode pattern that we decided NOT to replace with captured ones). Each agent has:\n- A success fixture (`testdata/stream_success.jsonl`) — exercises all 4 phases\n- An error fixture (`testdata/stream_error_*.jsonl`) — verifies error envelope parsing for that agent's error shape\n- A parser unit test\n- A `GenerateTextStreaming` test with `fakeStreamCmd` (the helper from claudecode)\n\nTest helper `fakeStreamCmd` should be lifted from `claudecode/generate_streaming_test.go` to a shared test package (e.g., `cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil/streaming.go`) so all 4 new agents reuse it without duplication.\n\n### Section 6 — Scope\n\n| Component | Lines (est.) |\n| --- | --- |\n| `agent/streaming_template.go` | ~100 |\n| 4 × per-agent `generate_streaming.go` | ~120 each = ~480 |\n| 4 × per-agent stream-event types (extends each agent's `response.go` or new file) | ~30 each = ~120 |\n| 4 × per-agent fixtures (2 files each) | ~30 each = ~120 |\n| 4 × per-agent tests | ~120 each = ~480 |\n| Progress writer tweaks (graceful field omission) | ~20 |\n| Shared test helper extraction | ~70 |\n| **Total** | **~1,390 lines** |\n\nThis is a substantial PR. Could be split per-agent into 4 separate PRs (codex first, then gemini, then cursor, then copilot) if you want smaller review chunks. Or all together as one \"non-claude streaming\" PR.\n\n---\n\nConfirm Section 1 before I draft the spec? And let me know if you'd prefer one PR for all 4 agents or four separate PRs."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2584,"cache_read_input_tokens":896161,"output_tokens":2881,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2584,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2881,"cache_read_input_tokens":896161,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2584,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2584},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cb4hW1uYHwQvtgsxvyN2s","attributionSkill":"superpowers:brainstorming","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"286f4546-b945-480a-a86c-65f6305562f0","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:51:10.893Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact-2","sessionId":"4944fa51-d7dd-4310-b62f-7802a196cd45","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"redact-2"}
