{"parentUuid":"aecf4095-b902-4bdf-bebf-dd05f4505ece","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013LQhgZz23PEJYFmCxmsqah","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Kp3nXihtLVL73xWykURnpt","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-15-non-claude-streaming-summaries.md","content":"# Non-Claude streaming summaries — Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Add live progress UI for `entire explain --generate` when the configured summary provider is Codex, Gemini, Cursor, or Copilot — matching the experience already shipped for Claude in PR #964.\n\n**Architecture:** New shared `StreamingGeneratorTemplate` in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/` parallel to `review/types/template.go`'s `ReviewerTemplate` (established in PR #1192). The template owns the subprocess lifecycle (`cmd.Start → scanner → drain → cmd.Wait`); each agent owns its `BuildCmd` (CLI args) and `Parser` (per-agent stream-event schema → `agent.GenerationProgress`). The existing progress writer renders the unified `Connecting → FirstToken → Generating → Done` phases with graceful degradation when a field is zero (e.g., agents without TTFT). `claudecode` stays on its own `generate_streaming.go` from PR #964 — no migration in this PR.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26.x, `bufio.Scanner` for NDJSON, `exec.CommandContext` for subprocess, existing `agent.ProgressFn` callback contract.\n\n**Worktree:** Create a fresh worktree off `origin/main` via @superpowers:using-git-worktrees before starting Chunk 1.\n\n**Cost note:** Each per-agent smoke test step makes a real API call against that agent's provider. Budget ~$0.05-0.30 per smoke test × 4 agents × 2-3 tests each = ~$2-5 total. Cheaper if happy path uses a tiny prompt.\n\n---\n\n## File Structure\n\n**Create:**\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/streaming_template.go` — `StreamingGeneratorTemplate` struct + its `Generate` method (subprocess lifecycle).\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/streaming_template_test.go` — unit tests for the template using the shared `fakeStreamCmd`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil/streaming.go` — `FakeStreamCmd`, `BuildFakeShellScript` helpers extracted from `claudecode/generate_streaming_test.go`. Exported so all 4 new agents reuse them.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/generate_streaming.go` — Codex `GenerateTextStreaming` + per-event stream struct + parser.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/generate_streaming_test.go` — tests.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/testdata/stream_success.jsonl` — minimal synthetic happy-path fixture.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/testdata/stream_error.jsonl` — error envelope fixture.\n- Same trio (.go + 2 testdata) for `geminicli`, `cursor`, `copilotcli`.\n\n**Modify:**\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/codex.go` — declare `StreamingTextGenerator: true` in capabilities (if it's a `CapabilityDeclarer`, otherwise no-op — built-ins don't need to declare).\n- Same for the other 3 agent packages: confirm each has a `*Agent` receiver and `GenerateTextStreaming` will compile against it.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go` — adjust `summaryProgressWriter.handle` so `PhaseFirstToken` rendering omits zero fields:\n  - When `TTFTms == 0` AND `CachedInputTokens == 0` → `→ Provider responded -- generating...` (no parens block)\n  - When only `TTFTms == 0` → `→ Provider responded (Nk cached input tokens) -- generating...`\n  - When only `CachedInputTokens == 0` → `→ Provider responded (TTFT 1.6s) -- generating...`\n  - When both present → existing format unchanged.\n\n**Not modified:**\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/generate_streaming.go` — claudecode keeps its own streaming implementation. Per-user decision.\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 1: Shared infrastructure\n\n**Outcome:** New `StreamingGeneratorTemplate` and shared test helpers exist and are tested. No agent uses them yet. Progress writer degrades gracefully when phase fields are zero. One commit.\n\n### Task 1.1: Extract `fakeStreamCmd` helpers to a shared package\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil/streaming.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/generate_streaming_test.go` — update imports.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Verify the existing helpers in claudecode test:\n\n```bash\ngrep -n \"func fakeStreamCmd\\|func buildFakeShellScript\\|func itoa\" cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/generate_streaming_test.go\n```\n\nExpected: three matches.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Create `cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil/streaming.go` (new package `testutil` if not present; else add the file to existing package):\n\n```go\n// Package testutil holds shared test helpers for the agent package and\n// its sub-packages. Not for production use.\npackage testutil\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"strconv\"\n\t\"strings\"\n)\n\n// FakeStreamCmd returns a CommandRunner factory whose *exec.Cmd, when\n// Start()'d and Wait()'d, produces stdout/stderr/exit-code as configured.\n// Implementation uses `sh -c` to write fixture data; on Windows runners\n// we would need PowerShell, but the project's CI is Linux/macOS only.\nfunc FakeStreamCmd(stdout, stderr string, exitCode int) func(ctx context.Context, name string, args ...string) *exec.Cmd {\n\treturn func(ctx context.Context, _ string, _ ...string) *exec.Cmd {\n\t\tscript := BuildFakeShellScript(stdout, stderr, exitCode)\n\t\treturn exec.CommandContext(ctx, \"sh\", \"-c\", script)\n\t}\n}\n\n// BuildFakeShellScript renders a shell snippet that emits the given stdout,\n// stderr, and exit code. Exported so callers that need a customized fake\n// (e.g. multi-stage stdout) can compose against it.\nfunc BuildFakeShellScript(stdout, stderr string, exitCode int) string {\n\tvar sb strings.Builder\n\tif stdout != \"\" {\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"cat <<'__EOF__'\\n\")\n\t\tsb.WriteString(stdout)\n\t\tif !strings.HasSuffix(stdout, \"\\n\") {\n\t\t\tsb.WriteString(\"\\n\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"__EOF__\\n\")\n\t}\n\tif stderr != \"\" {\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"cat <<'__EOF__' 1>&2\\n\")\n\t\tsb.WriteString(stderr)\n\t\tif !strings.HasSuffix(stderr, \"\\n\") {\n\t\t\tsb.WriteString(\"\\n\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"__EOF__\\n\")\n\t}\n\tif exitCode != 0 {\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"exit \")\n\t\tsb.WriteString(strconv.Itoa(exitCode))\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"\\n\")\n\t}\n\treturn sb.String()\n}\n```\n\nNote: drops the `itoa` reinvention from claudecode (one of the carry-forward items from the PR #964 review).\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** In `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/generate_streaming_test.go`:\n  - Add import: `\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil\"`\n  - Replace local `fakeStreamCmd(...)` calls with `testutil.FakeStreamCmd(...)`\n  - Delete the local `fakeStreamCmd`, `buildFakeShellScript`, `itoa` function definitions.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4:** Run `mise run fmt && mise run lint`. Expected: clean.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5:** Run claudecode tests to confirm the migration:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode -run TestGenerateTextStreaming -v\n```\n\nExpected: all 3 tests PASS.\n\n### Task 1.2: Add `StreamingGeneratorTemplate`\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/streaming_template.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Write the template:\n\n```go\npackage agent\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"log/slog\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/logging\"\n)\n\n// StreamingGeneratorTemplate is the shared subprocess-lifecycle wrapper for\n// streaming text generators. Per-agent code provides BuildCmd (argv) and\n// Parser (stdout → progress events); the template handles Start, drain,\n// Wait, stderr capture, and error wrapping.\n//\n// Parallels review/types/template.ReviewerTemplate (established in PR #1192).\n//\n// Fields must be non-nil before Generate is called; nil values cause\n// Generate to return ErrTemplateMisconfigured.\ntype StreamingGeneratorTemplate struct {\n\t// AgentName is an identifier used in log entries (e.g., \"codex\").\n\tAgentName string\n\n\t// DisplayName is the user-facing CLI binary name used in *TextGenerationError\n\t// wrapping (e.g., \"codex\"). Often the same as AgentName but kept separate\n\t// for cases where they differ (e.g., Cursor's agent is named \"cursor\"\n\t// but its binary is \"agent\").\n\tDisplayName string\n\n\t// BuildCmd constructs the *exec.Cmd for one streaming call. Implementations\n\t// MUST set cmd.Stdin to the prompt and cmd.Args to the agent's\n\t// streaming-mode invocation. The template will set cmd.Dir = os.TempDir()\n\t// and cmd.Env = StripGitEnv(os.Environ()) before Start.\n\tBuildCmd func(ctx context.Context, prompt, model string) *exec.Cmd\n\n\t// Parser consumes the agent's stdout stream and dispatches progress\n\t// callbacks. Returns the final result text on success. Must read until\n\t// stdout EOF before returning so the template can call Wait cleanly.\n\t// progress may be nil; Parser must handle that.\n\tParser func(stdout io.Reader, progress ProgressFn) (result string, err error)\n\n\t// LooksLikeUnrecognizedFlag is optional. When non-nil and the subprocess\n\t// fails with stderr matching the predicate, the caller can fall back to\n\t// the agent's non-streaming GenerateText path. The template surfaces\n\t// this signal via ErrUnrecognizedStreamingFlag so the caller decides.\n\tLooksLikeUnrecognizedFlag func(stderr string) bool\n}\n\n// ErrTemplateMisconfigured is returned when required template fields are nil.\nvar ErrTemplateMisconfigured = errors.New(\"streaming template misconfigured\")\n\n// ErrUnrecognizedStreamingFlag is returned when LooksLikeUnrecognizedFlag\n// indicates the CLI rejected a streaming-specific flag. Callers that\n// implement a fallback should errors.Is this to detect.\nvar ErrUnrecognizedStreamingFlag = errors.New(\"CLI rejected streaming flag\")\n\n// Generate runs one streaming generation and returns the final result text.\n// On error, returns *TextGenerationError carrying captured stderr and the\n// stdout byte count, matching RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI's error shape.\nfunc (t *StreamingGeneratorTemplate) Generate(\n\tctx context.Context,\n\tprompt, model string,\n\tprogress ProgressFn,\n) (string, error) {\n\tif t.BuildCmd == nil || t.Parser == nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", ErrTemplateMisconfigured\n\t}\n\n\tcmd := t.BuildCmd(ctx, prompt, model)\n\tcmd.Dir = os.TempDir()\n\tcmd.Env = StripGitEnv(os.Environ())\n\n\tstdout, err := cmd.StdoutPipe()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%s stream stdout pipe: %w\", t.AgentName, err)\n\t}\n\tvar stderr bytes.Buffer\n\tcmd.Stderr = &stderr\n\n\tif err := cmd.Start(); err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%s stream start: %w\", t.AgentName, err)\n\t}\n\n\t// stdoutBytes counts what the subprocess actually produced — used by the\n\t// timeout-diagnostic path to distinguish \"produced no output\" from \"was\n\t// generating when killed\". The counting reader passes bytes through to\n\t// the parser unchanged.\n\tcounter := &countingReader{r: stdout}\n\tresult, parseErr := t.Parser(counter, progress)\n\n\t// Drain any unread stdout so the subprocess can exit cleanly even if\n\t// the parser aborted early. The discard isn't tracked because we don't\n\t// count post-parser bytes toward the diagnostic.\n\tif _, drainErr := io.Copy(io.Discard, stdout); drainErr != nil {\n\t\tlogging.Debug(ctx, \"draining stream stdout\",\n\t\t\tslog.String(\"agent\", t.AgentName),\n\t\t\tslog.String(\"error\", drainErr.Error()))\n\t}\n\twaitErr := cmd.Wait()\n\n\t// ctx cancellation takes precedence over parser/wait errors so callers\n\t// see context.DeadlineExceeded / Canceled cleanly when applicable.\n\tif ctx.Err() != nil {\n\t\tstderrStr := strings.TrimSpace(stderr.String())\n\t\treturn \"\", &TextGenerationError{\n\t\t\tErr:         ctx.Err(),\n\t\t\tStderr:      stderrStr,\n\t\t\tStdoutBytes: counter.n,\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tif parseErr == nil && waitErr == nil {\n\t\treturn result, nil\n\t}\n\n\t// Old-CLI fallback: only fires when the subprocess exited non-zero AND\n\t// stderr matches the per-agent fallback detector. Parser errors don't\n\t// trigger this; only the CLI's own rejection of streaming flags does.\n\tstderrStr := strings.TrimSpace(stderr.String())\n\tif waitErr != nil && t.LooksLikeUnrecognizedFlag != nil && t.LooksLikeUnrecognizedFlag(stderrStr) {\n\t\tlogging.Warn(ctx, \"CLI rejected streaming flags; caller should fall back to non-streaming\",\n\t\t\tslog.String(\"agent\", t.AgentName),\n\t\t\tslog.String(\"stderr\", stderrStr))\n\t\treturn \"\", ErrUnrecognizedStreamingFlag\n\t}\n\n\t// Compose the error: parser failure wins if waitErr is nil; otherwise\n\t// the wait error (which carries the exit code) wins. Both are wrapped\n\t// into *TextGenerationError so the explain layer's diagnostic can read\n\t// stderr.\n\twrappedErr := waitErr\n\tif wrappedErr == nil {\n\t\twrappedErr = parseErr\n\t}\n\treturn \"\", &TextGenerationError{\n\t\tErr:         fmt.Errorf(\"%s stream failed: %w\", t.AgentName, wrappedErr),\n\t\tStderr:      stderrStr,\n\t\tStdoutBytes: counter.n,\n\t}\n}\n\n// countingReader passes bytes through and counts them. Used by the template\n// so the diagnostic path can ask \"did the subprocess produce any output?\".\ntype countingReader struct {\n\tr io.Reader\n\tn int\n}\n\nfunc (c *countingReader) Read(p []byte) (int, error) {\n\tn, err := c.r.Read(p)\n\tc.n += n\n\treturn n, err\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Run `mise run fmt && mise run lint`. Expected: clean.\n\n### Task 1.3: Test `StreamingGeneratorTemplate`\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/streaming_template_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Write tests:\n\n```go\npackage agent_test\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil\"\n)\n\nfunc TestStreamingGeneratorTemplate_Generate_Success(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tparsed := false\n\ttmpl := &agent.StreamingGeneratorTemplate{\n\t\tAgentName:   \"fake\",\n\t\tDisplayName: \"fake\",\n\t\tBuildCmd: func(ctx context.Context, prompt, model string) *exec.Cmd {\n\t\t\treturn testutil.FakeStreamCmd(\"hello\\nworld\\n\", \"\", 0)(ctx, \"fake\", []string{}...)\n\t\t},\n\t\tParser: func(stdout io.Reader, progress agent.ProgressFn) (string, error) {\n\t\t\tb, err := io.ReadAll(stdout)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn \"\", err\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tparsed = true\n\t\t\treturn strings.TrimSpace(string(b)), nil\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\n\tresult, err := tmpl.Generate(context.Background(), \"prompt\", \"model\", nil)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif result != \"hello\\nworld\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"result = %q, want %q\", result, \"hello\\nworld\")\n\t}\n\tif !parsed {\n\t\tt.Error(\"expected parser to have been called\")\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestStreamingGeneratorTemplate_Generate_NilFieldsReturnError(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\ttmpl := &agent.StreamingGeneratorTemplate{}\n\t_, err := tmpl.Generate(context.Background(), \"prompt\", \"model\", nil)\n\tif !errors.Is(err, agent.ErrTemplateMisconfigured) {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"err = %v, want ErrTemplateMisconfigured\", err)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestStreamingGeneratorTemplate_Generate_UnrecognizedFlagFallback(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\ttmpl := &agent.StreamingGeneratorTemplate{\n\t\tAgentName:   \"fake\",\n\t\tDisplayName: \"fake\",\n\t\tBuildCmd: func(ctx context.Context, prompt, model string) *exec.Cmd {\n\t\t\treturn testutil.FakeStreamCmd(\"\", \"error: unknown flag: --stream-json\", 1)(ctx, \"fake\", []string{}...)\n\t\t},\n\t\tParser: func(stdout io.Reader, progress agent.ProgressFn) (string, error) {\n\t\t\t_, _ = io.Copy(io.Discard, stdout)\n\t\t\treturn \"\", nil\n\t\t},\n\t\tLooksLikeUnrecognizedFlag: func(stderr string) bool {\n\t\t\treturn strings.Contains(stderr, \"unknown flag\") && strings.Contains(stderr, \"stream-json\")\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\n\t_, err := tmpl.Generate(context.Background(), \"prompt\", \"model\", nil)\n\tif !errors.Is(err, agent.ErrUnrecognizedStreamingFlag) {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"err = %v, want ErrUnrecognizedStreamingFlag\", err)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestStreamingGeneratorTemplate_Generate_NonZeroExitWrapsError(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\ttmpl := &agent.StreamingGeneratorTemplate{\n\t\tAgentName:   \"fake\",\n\t\tDisplayName: \"fake\",\n\t\tBuildCmd: func(ctx context.Context, prompt, model string) *exec.Cmd {\n\t\t\treturn testutil.FakeStreamCmd(\"partial\\n\", \"boom\\n\", 1)(ctx, \"fake\", []string{}...)\n\t\t},\n\t\tParser: func(stdout io.Reader, progress agent.ProgressFn) (string, error) {\n\t\t\t_, _ = io.Copy(io.Discard, stdout)\n\t\t\treturn \"\", nil\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\n\t_, err := tmpl.Generate(context.Background(), \"prompt\", \"model\", nil)\n\tvar failure *agent.TextGenerationError\n\tif !errors.As(err, &failure) {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"err = %v, want *TextGenerationError\", err)\n\t}\n\tif !strings.Contains(failure.Stderr, \"boom\") {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"stderr captured = %q, want substring 'boom'\", failure.Stderr)\n\t}\n\tif failure.StdoutBytes == 0 {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"stdoutBytes = 0, want > 0 (subprocess emitted 'partial\\\\n')\")\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestStreamingGeneratorTemplate_Generate_ContextCancelled(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(context.Background())\n\tcancel()\n\n\ttmpl := &agent.StreamingGeneratorTemplate{\n\t\tAgentName:   \"fake\",\n\t\tDisplayName: \"fake\",\n\t\tBuildCmd: func(ctx context.Context, prompt, model string) *exec.Cmd {\n\t\t\treturn testutil.FakeStreamCmd(\"ok\\n\", \"\", 0)(ctx, \"fake\", []string{}...)\n\t\t},\n\t\tParser: func(stdout io.Reader, progress agent.ProgressFn) (string, error) {\n\t\t\t_, _ = io.Copy(io.Discard, stdout)\n\t\t\treturn \"\", nil\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\n\t_, err := tmpl.Generate(ctx, \"prompt\", \"model\", nil)\n\tvar failure *agent.TextGenerationError\n\tif !errors.As(err, &failure) {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"err = %v, want *TextGenerationError wrapping context error\", err)\n\t}\n\tif !errors.Is(failure.Err, context.Canceled) {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"inner err = %v, want context.Canceled\", failure.Err)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Run: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent -run TestStreamingGeneratorTemplate -v`. Expected: 5 PASS.\n\n### Task 1.4: Progress writer graceful degradation\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go` — `summaryProgressWriter.handle`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Find the `PhaseFirstToken` branch in `summaryProgressWriter.handle`:\n\n```bash\ngrep -n \"case agent.PhaseFirstToken\" cmd/entire/cli/explain.go\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Replace the existing branch with a graceful-degradation version:\n\n```go\ncase agent.PhaseFirstToken:\n    var clauses []string\n    if p.TTFTms > 0 {\n        clauses = append(clauses, fmt.Sprintf(\"TTFT %s\", formatMs(p.TTFTms)))\n    }\n    if p.CachedInputTokens > 0 {\n        clauses = append(clauses, fmt.Sprintf(\"%s cached input tokens\", formatTokenCount(p.CachedInputTokens)))\n    }\n    detail := \"\"\n    if len(clauses) > 0 {\n        detail = \" (\" + strings.Join(clauses, \", \") + \")\"\n    }\n    s.printLine(fmt.Sprintf(\n        \"%s Provider responded%s -- generating...\",\n        s.arrow, detail))\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Update existing tests in `cmd/entire/cli/explain_test.go` that match the FirstToken output. Look for tests asserting `\"Provider responded\"` — these may need to verify both the with-fields and without-fields shapes:\n\n```bash\ngrep -n \"Provider responded\" cmd/entire/cli/explain_test.go\n```\n\nUpdate assertions as needed so they still pass.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4:** Add a new test for the no-fields case:\n\n```go\nfunc TestSummaryProgressWriter_FirstTokenWithoutOptionalFields(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n\n    var buf bytes.Buffer\n    attempt := newSummaryAttempt(\"gemini-cli\", 0)\n    pw := newSummaryProgressWriter(&buf, attempt)\n\n    // PhaseFirstToken with TTFTms=0 and CachedInputTokens=0 (Gemini's\n    // shape — no TTFT or cached tokens fields). Output should omit the\n    // parenthesized detail block entirely.\n    pw.handle(agent.GenerationProgress{Phase: agent.PhaseFirstToken})\n\n    out := buf.String()\n    if !strings.Contains(out, \"Provider responded -- generating...\") {\n        t.Errorf(\"output = %q, want 'Provider responded -- generating...' (no parens)\", out)\n    }\n    if strings.Contains(out, \"(\") {\n        t.Errorf(\"output = %q, should not contain '(' when both fields are zero\", out)\n    }\n}\n\nfunc TestSummaryProgressWriter_FirstTokenWithOnlyCachedTokens(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n\n    var buf bytes.Buffer\n    attempt := newSummaryAttempt(\"codex\", 0)\n    pw := newSummaryProgressWriter(&buf, attempt)\n\n    pw.handle(agent.GenerationProgress{Phase: agent.PhaseFirstToken, CachedInputTokens: 23808})\n\n    out := buf.String()\n    if !strings.Contains(out, \"Provider responded (23.8k cached input tokens) -- generating...\") {\n        t.Errorf(\"output = %q, want '(23.8k cached input tokens)' clause\", out)\n    }\n    if strings.Contains(out, \"TTFT\") {\n        t.Errorf(\"output = %q, should not mention TTFT when TTFTms == 0\", out)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 5:** Run: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run TestSummaryProgressWriter -v`. Expected: all PASS.\n\n### Task 1.5: Verify and commit chunk 1\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Run `mise run fmt && mise run lint`. Expected: clean.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Run `mise run test:ci`. Expected: all green.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Commit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/agent/streaming_template.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/streaming_template_test.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil/streaming.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/generate_streaming_test.go cmd/entire/cli/explain.go cmd/entire/cli/explain_test.go\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfeat(agent): add StreamingGeneratorTemplate + progress-writer field degradation\n\nFoundation for non-Claude streaming summary generation. Mirrors the\nReviewerTemplate pattern (review/types/template.go, from PR #1192):\n\n- StreamingGeneratorTemplate owns subprocess lifecycle (Start, scanner,\n  drain, Wait, stderr capture, fallback detection, error wrapping into\n  *TextGenerationError). Per-agent code only provides BuildCmd (argv)\n  and Parser (stdout → progress events).\n\n- testutil.FakeStreamCmd extracted from claudecode/generate_streaming_test.go\n  so all 5 streaming agents (claudecode + 4 upcoming) reuse one fake.\n  Drops the in-line itoa reinvention (carry-forward from PR #964 review)\n  in favor of strconv.Itoa.\n\n- summaryProgressWriter renders PhaseFirstToken with graceful degradation:\n  omits the (TTFT, cached input tokens) clause when both fields are zero;\n  omits one or the other when only one is present. Lets non-Claude agents\n  (some of which emit neither field) render cleanly under the same template.\n\nNo agent uses the new template yet — wiring lands in subsequent commits\n(one per agent).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 2: Codex streaming\n\n**Outcome:** `entire explain --generate` with provider `codex` shows live progress. The `*CodexAgent` implements `StreamingTextGenerator`. Manually verified end-to-end against the real `codex` CLI. One commit.\n\n### Task 2.1: Capture real Codex stream format\n\nThis is a manual investigation step. Do NOT commit the captured file — it's reference material only.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Run codex with the same flags the implementation will use:\n\n```fish\ncd /tmp\necho \"say hi in 5 words\" | codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --json - > /tmp/codex-real.jsonl 2>&1\ncat /tmp/codex-real.jsonl\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Identify event shapes. Expected (from PR #964 plan-phase exploration):\n  - `{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"...\"}` — first event\n  - `{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}` — Connecting candidate\n  - `{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"...\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"...\"}}` — FirstToken AND result text\n  - More `item.completed` events possible (for tool calls — ignored for summary use case)\n  - `{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":N,\"cached_input_tokens\":N,\"output_tokens\":N,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":N}}` — Done with usage\n\nVerify the actual shape matches. If Codex's protocol has evolved or the prompt triggered tool calls that we should explicitly ignore, note the differences before proceeding.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Note any volatile fields to redact when writing the synthetic fixture: `thread_id`, `session_id`, timestamps. Result text is fine.\n\n### Task 2.2: Define Codex stream-event types\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/stream_response.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Write the file based on the captured shape from Task 2.1:\n\n```go\npackage codex\n\n// codexStreamEvent is one decoded line of `codex exec --json` output.\n// Fields are populated based on the event Type/Item.Type.\ntype codexStreamEvent struct {\n\tType     string          `json:\"type\"`\n\tThreadID string          `json:\"thread_id,omitempty\"`\n\tItem     *codexStreamItem `json:\"item,omitempty\"`\n\tUsage    *codexStreamUsage `json:\"usage,omitempty\"`\n}\n\n// codexStreamItem appears inside type=item.completed events. For summary\n// generation we care only about Type=\"agent_message\" items, which carry\n// the model's response in Text.\ntype codexStreamItem struct {\n\tID   string `json:\"id\"`\n\tType string `json:\"type\"` // \"agent_message\" | \"command_execution\" | ...\n\tText string `json:\"text\"` // populated for agent_message\n}\n\n// codexStreamUsage appears inside the terminal type=turn.completed event.\ntype codexStreamUsage struct {\n\tInputTokens          int `json:\"input_tokens,omitempty\"`\n\tCachedInputTokens    int `json:\"cached_input_tokens,omitempty\"`\n\tOutputTokens         int `json:\"output_tokens,omitempty\"`\n\tReasoningOutputTokens int `json:\"reasoning_output_tokens,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Run `mise run fmt`. Expected: clean.\n\n### Task 2.3: Write parser tests with synthetic fixtures\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/testdata/stream_success.jsonl`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/testdata/stream_error.jsonl`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/generate_streaming_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Create success fixture matching the shape observed in Task 2.1. Minimal version (one event per phase the parser dispatches on):\n\n```jsonl\n{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"test-thread\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Hello, world.\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":9,\"cached_input_tokens\":1234,\"output_tokens\":3,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":0}}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Create error fixture:\n\n```jsonl\n{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"test-thread\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"error\",\"message\":\"invalid_request_error: model not found\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.failed\",\"error\":{\"message\":\"model not found\"}}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Write the parser test (define the parser symbol now; implementation in Task 2.4):\n\n```go\npackage codex\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n)\n\nfunc TestParseCodexStream_Success(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"testdata\", \"stream_success.jsonl\"))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"read fixture: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tvar phases []agent.ProgressPhase\n\tresult, err := parseCodexStream(bytes.NewReader(data), func(p agent.GenerationProgress) {\n\t\tphases = append(phases, p.Phase)\n\t})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif result != \"Hello, world.\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"result = %q, want %q\", result, \"Hello, world.\")\n\t}\n\n\t// Expected dispatcher behavior for Codex:\n\t// - turn.started     → Connecting (1)\n\t// - first item.completed(agent_message) → FirstToken (1)\n\t// - turn.completed   → Done (1, with usage.output_tokens=3, cached_input_tokens=1234)\n\tcounts := map[agent.ProgressPhase]int{}\n\tfor _, p := range phases {\n\t\tcounts[p]++\n\t}\n\tif counts[agent.PhaseConnecting] != 1 {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"PhaseConnecting count = %d, want 1\", counts[agent.PhaseConnecting])\n\t}\n\tif counts[agent.PhaseFirstToken] != 1 {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"PhaseFirstToken count = %d, want 1\", counts[agent.PhaseFirstToken])\n\t}\n\tif counts[agent.PhaseDone] != 1 {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"PhaseDone count = %d, want 1\", counts[agent.PhaseDone])\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseCodexStream_ErrorEnvelope(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"testdata\", \"stream_error.jsonl\"))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"read fixture: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t_, err = parseCodexStream(bytes.NewReader(data), nil)\n\tif err == nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"expected error from error envelope\")\n\t}\n\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"model not found\") {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"error %q should mention 'model not found'\", err)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseCodexStream_MissingTurnCompleted(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tstream := `{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"t\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"i\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"partial\"}}\n`\n\t_, err := parseCodexStream(strings.NewReader(stream), nil)\n\tif err == nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"expected error when stream lacks turn.completed\")\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4:** Run: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex -run TestParseCodexStream -v`. Expected: FAIL with `parseCodexStream undefined`.\n\n### Task 2.4: Implement Codex parser\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/generate_streaming.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Write the parser and supporting functions:\n\n```go\npackage codex\n\nimport (\n\t\"bufio\"\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n)\n\n// streamBufferMax bounds a single NDJSON line. Codex envelopes can be large\n// (init events may carry the full tool list), so we lift the default scanner\n// limit substantially.\nconst streamBufferMax = 4 * 1024 * 1024 // 4 MiB\n\n// parseCodexStream consumes `codex exec --json` NDJSON output, dispatches\n// progress callbacks, and returns the final agent_message text. Returns\n// an error if the stream ends without a turn.completed event or if a\n// turn.failed event is observed.\nfunc parseCodexStream(stdout io.Reader, progress agent.ProgressFn) (string, error) {\n\tscanner := bufio.NewScanner(stdout)\n\tscanner.Buffer(make([]byte, 64*1024), streamBufferMax)\n\n\tvar (\n\t\tresultText      string\n\t\tfirstTokenFired bool\n\t\tsawTurnComplete bool\n\t\tusage           *codexStreamUsage\n\t\tmalformed       int\n\t)\n\n\tdispatch := func(p agent.GenerationProgress) {\n\t\tif progress != nil {\n\t\t\tprogress(p)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tfor scanner.Scan() {\n\t\tline := scanner.Bytes()\n\t\tif len(line) == 0 {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tvar ev codexStreamEvent\n\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(line, &ev); err != nil {\n\t\t\tmalformed++\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tswitch ev.Type {\n\t\tcase \"turn.started\":\n\t\t\tdispatch(agent.GenerationProgress{Phase: agent.PhaseConnecting})\n\n\t\tcase \"item.completed\":\n\t\t\tif ev.Item != nil && ev.Item.Type == \"agent_message\" {\n\t\t\t\tif !firstTokenFired {\n\t\t\t\t\tfirstTokenFired = true\n\t\t\t\t\tdispatch(agent.GenerationProgress{Phase: agent.PhaseFirstToken})\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t// Use the LAST agent_message as the final result. Codex emits\n\t\t\t\t// one per assistant turn; for a summary prompt there's typically\n\t\t\t\t// exactly one, but if the model produces multiple (e.g. it\n\t\t\t\t// explained then re-emitted) the last is what matches what\n\t\t\t\t// the user would see.\n\t\t\t\tresultText = ev.Item.Text\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\tcase \"turn.completed\":\n\t\t\tsawTurnComplete = true\n\t\t\tusage = ev.Usage\n\n\t\tcase \"turn.failed\", \"error\":\n\t\t\tdetail := \"unspecified error\"\n\t\t\tif len(line) > 0 {\n\t\t\t\tdetail = string(line)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"codex turn failed: %s\", detail)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif err := scanner.Err(); err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"reading codex stream: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tif !sawTurnComplete {\n\t\treturn \"\", errors.New(\"codex stream ended without a turn.completed event\")\n\t}\n\tif resultText == \"\" {\n\t\treturn \"\", errors.New(\"codex stream produced no agent_message\")\n\t}\n\tif progress != nil {\n\t\tdone := agent.GenerationProgress{Phase: agent.PhaseDone}\n\t\tif usage != nil {\n\t\t\tdone.OutputTokens = usage.OutputTokens\n\t\t\tdone.InputTokens = usage.InputTokens\n\t\t\tdone.CachedInputTokens = usage.CachedInputTokens\n\t\t}\n\t\tdispatch(done)\n\t}\n\t_ = malformed // malformed counter reserved for future logging if needed\n\treturn resultText, nil\n}\n\n// GenerateTextStreaming runs `codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --json -` and\n// dispatches progress events to the optional callback. Implements\n// agent.StreamingTextGenerator.\n//\n// If the codex CLI rejects the --json flag (older version), the template\n// signals ErrUnrecognizedStreamingFlag and the caller falls back to the\n// non-streaming GenerateText path.\nfunc (c *CodexAgent) GenerateTextStreaming(\n\tctx context.Context,\n\tprompt, model string,\n\tprogress agent.ProgressFn,\n) (string, error) {\n\ttmpl := &agent.StreamingGeneratorTemplate{\n\t\tAgentName:                 \"codex\",\n\t\tDisplayName:               \"codex\",\n\t\tBuildCmd:                  c.buildStreamCmd,\n\t\tParser:                    parseCodexStream,\n\t\tLooksLikeUnrecognizedFlag: looksLikeCodexUnrecognizedFlag,\n\t}\n\n\tresult, err := tmpl.Generate(ctx, prompt, model, progress)\n\tif errors.Is(err, agent.ErrUnrecognizedStreamingFlag) {\n\t\treturn c.GenerateText(ctx, prompt, model)\n\t}\n\treturn result, err\n}\n\nfunc (c *CodexAgent) buildStreamCmd(ctx context.Context, prompt, model string) *exec.Cmd {\n\tcommandRunner := c.CommandRunner\n\tif commandRunner == nil {\n\t\tcommandRunner = exec.CommandContext\n\t}\n\targs := []string{\"exec\", \"--skip-git-repo-check\", \"--json\"}\n\tif model != \"\" {\n\t\targs = append(args, \"--model\", model)\n\t}\n\targs = append(args, \"-\")\n\tcmd := commandRunner(ctx, \"codex\", args...)\n\tcmd.Stdin = strings.NewReader(prompt)\n\treturn cmd\n}\n\n// looksLikeCodexUnrecognizedFlag returns true if codex stderr indicates the\n// --json flag was rejected. Mirrors claudecode's pattern: AND-logic between\n// a rejection phrase and a streaming-flag name.\nfunc looksLikeCodexUnrecognizedFlag(stderr string) bool {\n\tlower := strings.ToLower(stderr)\n\thasRejectPhrase := strings.Contains(lower, \"unrecognized option\") ||\n\t\tstrings.Contains(lower, \"unknown flag\") ||\n\t\tstrings.Contains(lower, \"unknown option\") ||\n\t\tstrings.Contains(lower, \"invalid option\")\n\tif !hasRejectPhrase {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\treturn strings.Contains(lower, \"json\") || strings.Contains(lower, \"exec\")\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Run: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex -run TestParseCodexStream -v`. Expected: 3 PASS.\n\n### Task 2.5: Test `CodexAgent.GenerateTextStreaming`\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/generate_streaming_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Append integration tests using the shared `testutil.FakeStreamCmd`:\n\n```go\nfunc TestCodexGenerateTextStreaming_Success(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tfixture, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"testdata\"