rateTextStreaming -v`. Expected: 2 PASS.\n\n### Task 2.6: Smoke test against real Codex CLI\n\nThis is the critical end-to-end verification. Do NOT skip.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Switch the summary provider to Codex:\n\n```fish\n$ENTIRE configure --summarize-provider codex\n```\n\n(Where `$ENTIRE` is the binary built from the current branch — `go build -o entire ./cmd/entire` from the worktree.)\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Run on a real checkpoint:\n\n```fish\n$ENTIRE checkpoint explain --checkpoint <id> --generate --force\n```\n\nExpected:\n- `Generating checkpoint summary... (transcript: ..., provider: codex)`\n- `→ Sending request to provider...`\n- `→ Provider responded (23.8k cached input tokens) -- generating...` (or similar — Codex emits cached tokens but no TTFT)\n- `✓ Summary generated (Xs, Y output tokens)` (numbers from `turn.completed.usage`)\n- The summary content below.\n\nConfirm: no panics, no missing-event errors, the displayed token counts roughly match what codex naturally reports.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Smoke-test the timeout diagnostic:\n\n```fish\n$ENTIRE checkpoint explain --checkpoint <id> --generate --force --summary-timeout-seconds 3\n```\n\nExpected: `✗ Timed out after 3s: model responded but did not finish` (or \"...provider sent request but received no response\" if the 3s window expires before any agent_message arrives).\n\n- [ ] **Step 4:** Reset the provider back to claude-code (so subsequent chunk smoke tests start clean):\n\n```fish\n$ENTIRE configure --summarize-provider claude-code\n```\n\n### Task 2.7: Verify and commit chunk 2\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Run `mise run check`. Expected: green.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Commit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/stream_response.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/generate_streaming.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/generate_streaming_test.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/testdata/stream_success.jsonl cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/testdata/stream_error.jsonl\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfeat(codex): implement StreamingTextGenerator\n\nCodex now emits live progress events through the explain --generate UI.\nparseCodexStream consumes `codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --json -`\nNDJSON output and dispatches our 4 phases:\n\n- turn.started               → PhaseConnecting\n- first item.completed(agent_message) → PhaseFirstToken (no TTFT — Codex\n  doesn't emit one; progress writer omits the clause gracefully)\n- turn.completed             → PhaseDone (with usage.output_tokens,\n  usage.cached_input_tokens populated from the API)\n\nTool-call events (item.{started,completed} with type=command_execution)\nare intentionally ignored — summary generation doesn't authorize tools,\nso they shouldn't appear in this code path, but the parser skips them\nsilently if they do.\n\nVerified end-to-end against the real codex CLI on a 40 KB transcript.\n\nFalls back to non-streaming GenerateText if the CLI rejects --json (older\ncodex versions). Fallback path is unit-tested via the shared FakeStreamCmd.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 3: Gemini streaming\n\n**Outcome:** Same as Chunk 2 but for `gemini-cli`. One commit.\n\n### Task 3.1: Capture real Gemini stream format\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Capture:\n\n```fish\necho \"say hi in 5 words\" | gemini --output-format stream-json -p \" \" > /tmp/gemini-real.jsonl 2>&1\ncat /tmp/gemini-real.jsonl\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Observed shape (per pre-plan investigation):\n  - `{\"type\":\"init\",\"timestamp\":\"...\",\"session_id\":\"...\",\"model\":\"...\"}`\n  - `{\"type\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"...\",\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"...\"}` (echo of input)\n  - `{\"type\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"...\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"...\",\"delta\":true}` (chunked)\n  - ... more assistant deltas ...\n\nNote: Gemini doesn't appear to emit a terminal \"done\" event with usage. The stream just ends at EOF. The parser will compute duration via `time.Since(start)` and