re requesting human review.\n\n---\n\n## Carry-forward / known gaps\n\n- **claudecode is NOT migrated** to the new `StreamingGeneratorTemplate`. Per user decision, the parallel patterns coexist. Future cleanup PR can migrate it if drift becomes a problem.\n- **Cursor streaming may be missing** if auth couldn't be set up during implementation. Document in the PR description; ship the other 3 + Cursor as a follow-up PR.\n- **External-agent streaming** (PR B in the larger plan) is a separate brainstorm cycle. Requires extending the external-agent protocol with a `generate-text-streaming` subcommand and event schema. Not in this PR.\n- **Per-agent token-display variation:** Codex shows cached tokens but no TTFT; Gemini shows neither; Claude shows both. The progress writer's graceful-field-degradation handles this, but users will see different levels of detail depending on the provider. Acceptable; documented in the PR description.\n\n---\n\n## Out-of-scope (will NOT be done in this PR)\n\n- Streaming for `external-agent` plugins (those `entire-agent-*` binaries on PATH). See \"External-agent streaming\" in carry-forward.\n- Re-capturing claudecode's fixtures from real Claude (reverted earlier; not in scope here either).\n- ACCESSIBLE-mode failure-glyph gap (`✗` doesn't respect ACCESSIBLE in `formatCheckpointSummaryError`). Separate small follow-up.\n- Per-agent unit tests for the existing non-streaming error-wrap path (each provider's `GenerateText` wraps into `*TextGenerationError`; not tested directly, but covered by `RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI` tests). Acceptable carry-forward.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2356,"cache_read_input_tokens":904618,"output_tokens":20815,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2356,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"infe