{"parentUuid":"827a980e-2fe5-4ffa-8715-ac7a09a3dd10","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2ca4e545-954d-4dc1-a875-7d01362973cf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kp3nXihtLVL73xWykURnpt","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-15-non-claude-streaming-summaries.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"a03e6837-f24e-438c-ac1b-3c98b24766e7","timestamp":"2026-05-15T17:05:28.053Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-15-non-claude-streaming-summaries.md","content":"# Non-Claude streaming summaries — Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Add live progress UI for `entire explain --generate` when the configured summary provider is Codex, Gemini, Cursor, or Copilot — matching the experience already shipped for Claude in PR #964.\n\n**Architecture:** New shared `StreamingGeneratorTemplate` in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/` parallel to `review/types/template.go`'s `ReviewerTemplate` (established in PR #1192). The template owns the subprocess lifecycle (`cmd.Start → scanner → drain → cmd.Wait`); each agent owns its `BuildCmd` (CLI args) and `Parser` (per-agent stream-event schema → `agent.GenerationProgress`). The existing progress writer renders the unified `Connecting → FirstToken → Generating → Done` phases with graceful degradation when a field is zero (e.g., agents without TTFT). `claudecode` stays on its own `generate_streaming.go` from PR #964 — no migration in this PR.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26.x, `bufio.Scanner` for NDJSON, `exec.CommandContext` for subprocess, existing `agent.ProgressFn` callback contract.\n\n**Worktree:** Create a fresh worktree off `origin/main` via @superpowers:using-git-worktrees before starting Chunk 1.\n\n**Cost note:** Each per-agent smoke test step makes a real API call against that agent's provider. Budget ~$0.05-0.30 per smoke test × 4 agents × 2-3 tests each = ~$2-5 total. Cheaper if happy path uses a tiny prompt.\n\n---\n\n## File Structure\n\n**Create:**\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/streaming_template.go` — `StreamingGeneratorTemplate` struct + its `Generate` method (subprocess lifecycle).\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/streaming_template_test.go` — unit tests for the template using the shared `fakeStreamCmd`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil/streaming.go` — `FakeStreamCmd`, `BuildFakeShellScript` helpers extracted from `claudecode/generate_streaming_test.go`. Exported so all 4 new agents reuse them.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/generate_streaming.go` — Codex `GenerateTextStreaming` + per-event stream struct + parser.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/generate_streaming_test.go` — tests.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/testdata/stream_success.jsonl` — minimal synthetic happy-path fixture.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/testdata/stream_error.jsonl` — error envelope fixture.\n- Same trio (.go + 2 testdata) for `geminicli`, `cursor`, `copilotcli`.\n\n**Modify:**\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/codex.go` — declare `StreamingTextGenerator: true` in capabilities (if it's a `CapabilityDeclarer`, otherwise no-op — built-ins don't need to declare).\n- Same for the other 3 agent packages: confirm each has a `*Agent` receiver and `GenerateTextStreaming` will compile against it.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/explain.go` — adjust `summaryProgressWriter.handle` so `PhaseFirstToken` rendering omits zero fields:\n  - When `TTFTms == 0` AND `CachedInputTokens == 0` → `→ Provider responded -- generating...` (no parens block)\n  - When only `TTFTms == 0` → `→ Provider responded (Nk cached input tokens) -- generating...`\n  - When only `CachedInputTokens == 0` → `→ Provider responded (TTFT 1.6s) -- generating...`\n  - When both present → existing format unchanged.\n\n**Not modified:**\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/generate_streaming.go` — claudecode keeps its own streaming implementation. Per-user decision.\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 1: Shared infrastructure\n\n**Outcome:** New `StreamingGeneratorTemplate` and shared test helpers exist and are tested. No agent uses them yet. Progress writer degrades gracefully when phase fields are zero. One commit.\n\n### Task 1.1: Extract `fakeStreamCmd` helpers to a shared package\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil/streaming.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/generate_streaming_test.go` — update imports.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Verify the existing helpers in claudecode test:\n\n```bash\ngrep -n \"func fakeStreamCmd\\|func buildFakeShellScript\\|func itoa\" cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/generate_streaming_test.go\n```\n\nExpected: three matches.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Create `cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil/streaming.go` (new package `testutil` if not present; else add the file to existing package):\n\n```go\n// Package testutil holds shared test helpers for the agent package and\n// its sub-packages. Not for production use.\npackage testutil\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"strconv\"\n\t\"strings\"\n)\n\n// FakeStreamCmd returns a CommandRunner factory whose *exec.Cmd, when\n// Start()'d and Wait()'d, produces stdout/stderr/exit-code as configured.\n// Implementation uses `sh -c` to write fixture data; on Windows runners\n// we would need PowerShell, but the project's CI is Linux/macOS only.\nfunc FakeStreamCmd(stdout, stderr string, exitCode int) func(ctx context.Context, name string, args ...string) *exec.Cmd {\n\treturn func(ctx context.Context, _ string, _ ...string) *exec.Cmd {\n\t\tscript := BuildFakeShellScript(stdout, stderr, exitCode)\n\t\treturn exec.CommandContext(ctx, \"sh\", \"-c\", script)\n\t}\n}\n\n// BuildFakeShellScript renders a shell snippet that emits the given stdout,\n// stderr, and exit code. Exported so callers that need a customized fake\n// (e.g. multi-stage stdout) can compose against it.\nfunc BuildFakeShellScript(stdout, stderr string, exitCode int) string {\n\tvar sb strings.Builder\n\tif stdout != \"\" {\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"cat <<'__EOF__'\\n\")\n\t\tsb.WriteString(stdout)\n\t\tif !strings.HasSuffix(stdout, \"\\n\") {\n\t\t\tsb.WriteString(\"\\n\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"__EOF__\\n\")\n\t}\n\tif stderr != \"\" {\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"cat <<'__EOF__' 1>&2\\n\")\n\t\tsb.WriteString(stderr)\n\t\tif !strings.HasSuffix(stderr, \"\\n\") {\n\t\t\tsb.WriteString(\"\\n\")\n\t\t}\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"__EOF__\\n\")\n\t}\n\tif exitCode != 0 {\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"exit \")\n\t\tsb.WriteString(strconv.Itoa(exitCode))\n\t\tsb.WriteString(\"\\n\")\n\t}\n\treturn sb.String()\n}\n```\n\nNote: drops the `itoa` reinvention from claudecode (one of the carry-forward items from the PR #964 review).\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** In `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/generate_streaming_test.go`:\n  - Add import: `\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil\"`\n  - Replace local `fakeStreamCmd(...)` calls with `testutil.FakeStreamCmd(...)`\n  - Delete the local `fakeStreamCmd`, `buildFakeShellScript`, `itoa` function definitions.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4:** Run `mise run fmt && mise run lint`. Expected: clean.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5:** Run claudecode tests to confirm the migration:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode -run TestGenerateTextStreaming -v\n```\n\nExpected: all 3 tests PASS.\n\n### Task 1.2: Add `StreamingGeneratorTemplate`\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/streaming_template.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Write the template:\n\n```go\npackage agent\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"log/slog\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/logging\"\n)\n\n// StreamingGeneratorTemplate is the shared subprocess-lifecycle wrapper for\n// streaming text generators. Per-agent code provides BuildCmd (argv) and\n// Parser (stdout → progress events); the template handles Start, drain,\n// Wait, stderr capture, and error wrapping.\n//\n// Parallels review/types/template.ReviewerTemplate (established in PR #1192).\n//\n// Fields must be non-nil before Generate is called; nil values cause\n// Generate to return ErrTemplateMisconfigured.\ntype StreamingGeneratorTemplate struct {\n\t// AgentName is an identifier used in log entries (e.g., \"codex\").\n\tAgentName string\n\n\t// DisplayName is the user-facing CLI binary name used in *TextGenerationError\n\t// wrapping (e.g., \"codex\"). Often the same as AgentName but kept separate\n\t// for cases where they differ (e.g., Cursor's agent is named \"cursor\"\n\t// but its binary is \"agent\").\n\tDisplayName string\n\n\t// BuildCmd constructs the *exec.Cmd for one streaming call. Implementations\n\t// MUST set cmd.Stdin to the prompt and cmd.Args to the agent's\n\t// streaming-mode invocation. The template will set cmd.Dir = os.TempDir()\n\t// and cmd.Env = StripGitEnv(os.Environ()) before Start.\n\tBuildCmd func(ctx context.Context, prompt, model string) *exec.Cmd\n\n\t// Parser consumes the agent's stdout stream and dispatches progress\n\t// callbacks. Returns the final result text on success. Must read until\n\t// stdout EOF before returning so the template can call Wait cleanly.\n\t// progress may be nil; Parser must handle that.\n\tParser func(stdout io.Reader, progress ProgressFn) (result string, err error)\n\n\t// LooksLikeUnrecognizedFlag is optional. When non-nil and the subprocess\n\t// fails with stderr matching the predicate, the caller can fall back to\n\t// the agent's non-streaming GenerateText path. The template surfaces\n\t// this signal via ErrUnrecognizedStreamingFlag so the caller decides.\n\tLooksLikeUnrecognizedFlag func(stderr string) bool\n}\n\n// ErrTemplateMisconfigured is returned when required template fields are nil.\nvar ErrTemplateMisconfigured = errors.New(\"streaming template misconfigured\")\n\n// ErrUnrecognizedStreamingFlag is returned when LooksLikeUnrecognizedFlag\n// indicates the CLI rejected a streaming-specific flag. Callers that\n// implement a fallback should errors.Is this to detect.\nvar ErrUnrecognizedStreamingFlag = errors.New(\"CLI rejected streaming flag\")\n\n// Generate runs one streaming generation and returns the final result text.\n// On error, returns *TextGenerationError carrying captured stderr and the\n// stdout byte count, matching RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI's error shape.\nfunc (t *StreamingGeneratorTemplate) Generate(\n\tctx context.Context,\n\tprompt, model string,\n\tprogress ProgressFn,\n) (string, error) {\n\tif t.BuildCmd == nil || t.Parser == nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", ErrTemplateMisconfigured\n\t}\n\n\tcmd := t.BuildCmd(ctx, prompt, model)\n\tcmd.Dir = os.TempDir()\n\tcmd.Env = StripGitEnv(os.Environ())\n\n\tstdout, err := cmd.StdoutPipe()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%s stream stdout pipe: %w\", t.AgentName, err)\n\t}\n\tvar stderr bytes.Buffer\n\tcmd.Stderr = &stderr\n\n\tif err := cmd.Start(); err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%s stream start: %w\", t.AgentName, err)\n\t}\n\n\t// stdoutBytes counts what the subprocess actually produced — used by the\n\t// timeout-diagnostic path to distinguish \"produced no output\" from \"was\n\t// generating when killed\". The counting reader passes bytes through to\n\t// the parser unchanged.\n\tcounter := &countingReader{r: stdout}\n\tresult, parseErr := t.Parser(counter, progress)\n\n\t// Drain any unread stdout so the subprocess can exit cleanly even if\n\t// the parser aborted early. The discard isn't tracked because we don't\n\t// count post-parser bytes toward the diagnostic.\n\tif _, drainErr := io.Copy(io.Discard, stdout); drainErr != nil {\n\t\tlogging.Debug(ctx, \"draining stream stdout\",\n\t\t\tslog.String(\"agent\", t.AgentName),\n\t\t\tslog.String(\"error\", drainErr.Error()))\n\t}\n\twaitErr := cmd.Wait()\n\n\t// ctx cancellation takes precedence over parser/wait errors so callers\n\t// see context.DeadlineExceeded / Canceled cleanly when applicable.\n\tif ctx.Err() != nil {\n\t\tstderrStr := strings.TrimSpace(stderr.String())\n\t\treturn \"\", &TextGenerationError{\n\t\t\tErr:         ctx.Err(),\n\t\t\tStderr:      stderrStr,\n\t\t\tStdoutBytes: counter.n,\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tif parseErr == nil && waitErr == nil {\n\t\treturn result, nil\n\t}\n\n\t// Old-CLI fallback: only fires when the subprocess exited non-zero AND\n\t// stderr matches the per-agent fallback detector. Parser errors don't\n\t// trigger this; only the CLI's own rejection of streaming flags does.\n\tstderrStr := strings.TrimSpace(stderr.String())\n\tif waitErr != nil && t.LooksLikeUnrecognizedFlag != nil && t.LooksLikeUnrecognizedFlag(stderrStr) {\n\t\tlogging.Warn(ctx, \"CLI rejected streaming flags; caller should fall back to non-streaming\",\n\t\t\tslog.String(\"agent\", t.AgentName),\n\t\t\tslog.String(\"stderr\", stderrStr))\n\t\treturn \"\", ErrUnrecognizedStreamingFlag\n\t}\n\n\t// Compose the error: parser failure wins if waitErr is nil; otherwise\n\t// the wait error (which carries the exit code) wins. Both are wrapped\n\t// into *TextGenerationError so the explain layer's diagnostic can read\n\t// stderr.\n\twrappedErr := waitErr\n\tif wrappedErr == nil {\n\t\twrappedErr = parseErr\n\t}\n\treturn \"\", &TextGenerationError{\n\t\tErr:         fmt.Errorf(\"%s stream failed: %w\", t.AgentName, wrappedErr),\n\t\tStderr:      stderrStr,\n\t\tStdoutBytes: counter.n,\n\t}\n}\n\n// countingReader passes bytes through and counts them. Used by the template\n// so the diagnostic path can ask \"did the subprocess produce any output?\".\ntype countingReader struct {\n\tr io.Reader\n\tn int\n}\n\nfunc (c *countingReader) Read(p []byte) (int, error) {\n\tn, err := c.r.Read(p)\n\tc.n += n\n\treturn n, err\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Run `mise run fmt && mise run lint`. Expected: clean.\n\n### Task 1.3: Test `StreamingGeneratorTemplate`\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/streaming_template_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Write tests:\n\n```go\npackage agent_test\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil\"\n)\n\nfunc TestStreamingGeneratorTemplate_Generate_Success(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tparsed := false\n\ttmpl := &agent.StreamingGeneratorTemplate{\n\t\tAgentName:   \"fake\",\n\t\tDisplayName: \"fake\",\n\t\tBuildCmd: func(ctx context.Context, prompt, model string) *exec.Cmd {\n\t\t\treturn testutil.FakeStreamCmd(\"hello\\nworld\\n\", \"\", 0)(ctx, \"fake\", []string{}...)\n\t\t},\n\t\tParser: func(stdout io.Reader, progress agent.ProgressFn) (string, error) {\n\t\t\tb, err := io.ReadAll(stdout)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn \"\", err\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tparsed = true\n\t\t\treturn strings.TrimSpace(string(b)), nil\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\n\tresult, err := tmpl.Generate(context.Background(), \"prompt\", \"model\", nil)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unexpected error: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif result != \"hello\\nworld\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"result = %q, want %q\", result, \"hello\\nworld\")\n\t}\n\tif !parsed {\n\t\tt.Error(\"expected parser to have been called\")\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestStreamingGeneratorTemplate_Generate_NilFieldsReturnError(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\ttmpl := &agent.StreamingGeneratorTemplate{}\n\t_, err := tmpl.Generate(context.Background(), \"prompt\", \"model\", nil)\n\tif !errors.Is(err, agent.ErrTemplateMisconfigured) {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"err = %v, want ErrTemplateMisconfigured\", err)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestStreamingGeneratorTemplate_Generate_UnrecognizedFlagFallback(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\ttmpl := &agent.StreamingGeneratorTemplate{\n\t\tAgentName:   \"fake\",\n\t\tDisplayN