{"parentUuid":"4c489e0f-67b0-4878-b5d4-7529b30be9f6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Qzr71o3a5bfB6YE556Vrh6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KdZ4VaTkVrPF5rFBzfY9kn","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-15-non-claude-streaming-summaries.md","old_string":"## Chunk 3: Gemini streaming\n\n**Outcome:** Same as Chunk 2 but for `gemini-cli`. One commit.\n\n### Task 3.1: Capture real Gemini stream format\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Capture:\n\n```fish\necho \"say hi in 5 words\" | gemini --output-format stream-json -p \" \" > /tmp/gemini-real.jsonl 2>&1\ncat /tmp/gemini-real.jsonl\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Observed shape (per pre-plan investigation):\n  - `{\"type\":\"init\",\"timestamp\":\"...\",\"session_id\":\"...\",\"model\":\"...\"}`\n  - `{\"type\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"...\",\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"...\"}` (echo of input)\n  - `{\"type\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"...\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"...\",\"delta\":true}` (chunked)\n  - ... more assistant deltas ...\n\nNote: Gemini doesn't appear to emit a terminal \"done\" event with usage. The stream just ends at EOF. The parser will compute duration via `time.Since(start)` and set `OutputTokens = 0` for the Done phase.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Verify whether a final usage-bearing event exists in the captured stream that the pre-plan exploration missed. If yes, plan to consume it; if no, plan to compute duration locally.\n\n### Task 3.2: Define Gemini stream-event types, parser tests, parser, generator, integration test, smoke test\n\nReplicate the structure of Chunk 2 (Tasks 2.2 → 2.7), substituting:\n\n**Stream event type** (`cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/stream_response.go`):\n\n```go\npackage geminicli\n\nimport \"time\"\n\ntype geminiStreamEvent struct {\n\tType      string    `json:\"type\"`\n\tTimestamp time.Time `json:\"timestamp,omitempty\"`\n\tSessionID string    `json:\"session_id,omitempty\"`\n\tModel     string    `json:\"model,omitempty\"`\n\tRole      string    `json:\"role,omitempty\"`\n\tContent   string    `json:\"content,omitempty\"`\n\tDelta     bool      `json:\"delta,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\n**Parser behavior** (in `parseGeminiStream`):\n- `type:\"init\"` → `PhaseConnecting`\n- First `type:\"message\", role:\"assistant\"` → `PhaseFirstToken` (TTFTms=0, no cached info)\n- Subsequent assistant messages → `PhaseGenerating` (accumulate `Content` if `delta:true` or last-write-wins if not)\n- Stream EOF → `PhaseDone` with `DurationMs = time.Since(start).Milliseconds()`, OutputTokens=0\n- The final result text is the assembled assistant content.\n\n**BuildCmd:** `[\"-p\", \" \"]` plus model + stream-json flag.\n\n**Smoke test:** same flow as Task 2.6 with `gemini-cli` as the provider.\n\nCommit message: `feat(geminicli): implement StreamingTextGenerator`.\n\n(I'm collapsing this chunk for plan brevity — the subagent should mirror Chunk 2's structure with the agent-specific differences above.)\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 4: Cursor streaming\n\n**Outcome:** Same as Chunk 2 but for `cursor`. One commit.\n\n### Task 4.1: Authenticate and capture real Cursor stream format\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Confirm cursor CLI is authenticated:\n\n```fish\nagent --version\necho \"say hi\" | agent --print --output-format stream-json --stream-partial-output --force --trust --workspace /tmp 2>&1 | head -3\n```\n\nIf it errors with `Authentication required`, the implementer must either run `agent login` interactively, set `CURSOR_API_KEY`, or **escalate** this chunk back to the user — cursor smoke testing cannot proceed without credentials. (BLOCKED status.)\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** If authenticated, capture to `/tmp/cursor-real.jsonl` and inspect the event schema. Cursor's `--help` mentions `--stream-partial-output` produces \"individual text deltas\" — expect message_start, text_delta, and message_stop equivalents.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Define the event struct based on captured shape. If the format closely matches Claude's stream_event envelope, reuse the dispatch pattern.\n\n### Task 4.2-4.7: Mirror Chunk 2's structure\n\nSame as Codex but with Cursor's invocation:\n\n**BuildCmd**: `[\"--print\", \"--force\", \"--trust\", \"--workspace\", os.TempDir(), \"--output-format\", \"stream-json\", \"--stream-partial-output\"]` plus optional `--model`.\n\n**Parser**: TBD based on real capture.\n\n**Smoke test:** same flow with `cursor` as the provider.\n\nCommit message: `feat(cursor): implement StreamingTextGenerator`.\n\n(Note: if Cursor can't be authenticated during implementation, leave this chunk un-implemented and document the gap in the PR description. The framework supports adding it later in a follow-up.)\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 5: Copilot streaming\n\n**Outcome:** Same as Chunk 2 but for `copilot-cli`. One commit.\n\n### Task 5.1: Capture real Copilot stream format\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Capture:\n\n```fish\necho \"say hi in 5 words\" | copilot --output-format json --stream on --allow-all-tools --disable-builtin-mcps > /tmp/copilot-real.jsonl 2>&1\ncat /tmp/copilot-real.jsonl\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Observed shape (per pre-plan investigation):\n  - `{\"type\":\"session.mcp_servers_loaded\", ...}` (ignored)\n  - `{\"type\":\"session.skills_loaded\", ...}` (ignored)\n  - `{\"type\":\"session.tools_updated\", \"data\":{\"model\":\"...\"}, ...}` (model info)\n  - `{\"type\":\"user.message\", ...}` (echo)\n  - `{\"type\":\"assistant.turn_start\", \"data\":{\"turnId\":\"...\"}, ...}` (Connecting candidate)\n  - `{\"type\":\"assistant.message_delta\", \"data\":{\"messageId\":\"...\",\"deltaContent\":\"...\"}, ...}` (chunked)\n  - Terminal event TBD (likely `assistant.turn_end` or similar — verify in capture)\n\n### Task 5.2-5.7: Mirror Chunk 2's structure\n\n**BuildCmd**: `[\"--output-format\", \"json\", \"--stream\", \"on\", \"--allow-all-tools\", \"--disable-builtin-mcps\"]` plus optional `--model`.\n\n**Parser dispatch:**\n- `assistant.turn_start` → `PhaseConnecting`\n- First `assistant.message_delta` → `PhaseFirstToken` (no TTFT field; check capture for any timing hint)\n- Subsequent `assistant.message_delta` → `PhaseGenerating` (accumulate `deltaContent`)\n- Terminal event → `PhaseDone` (extract usage if present)\n\n**Result text:** concatenated `deltaContent` from all `assistant.message_delta` events.\n\n**Smoke test:** same flow with `copilot-cli` as the provider.\n\nCommit message: `feat(copilotcli): implement StreamingTextGenerator`.\n\n---","new_string":"## Chunk 3: Gemini streaming\n\n**Outcome:** `entire explain --generate` with provider `gemini-cli` shows live progress. The `*GeminiCLIAgent` implements `StreamingTextGenerator`. Manually verified end-to-end against the real `gemini` CLI. One commit.\n\n### Task 3.1: Capture real Gemini stream format\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Capture (use a tiny prompt to keep cost minimal):\n\n```fish\necho \"say hi in 5 words\" | gemini --output-format stream-json -p \" \" --model gemini-3-flash-preview > /tmp/gemini-real.jsonl 2>&1\ncat /tmp/gemini-real.jsonl\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Expected event shape (per pre-plan investigation):\n  - `{\"type\":\"init\",\"timestamp\":\"...\",\"session_id\":\"...\",\"model\":\"...\"}` — once at start\n  - `{\"type\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"...\",\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"...\"}` — echo of the prompt (ignored)\n  - `{\"type\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"...\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"...\",\"delta\":true}` — chunked assistant content\n  - ... more assistant deltas ...\n  - **No terminal event** — stream ends at EOF\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Verify whether a final usage-bearing event exists in the captured stream that the pre-plan exploration missed. If yes, document it; the parser should consume it. If no (expected), the parser treats EOF as Done.\n\n### Task 3.2: Define Gemini stream-event types\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/stream_response.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Write:\n\n```go\npackage geminicli\n\nimport \"time\"\n\ntype geminiStreamEvent struct {\n\tType      string    `json:\"type\"`\n\tTimestamp time.Time `json:\"timestamp,omitempty\"`\n\tSessionID string    `json:\"session_id,omitempty\"`\n\tModel     string    `json:\"model,omitempty\"`\n\tRole      string    `json:\"role,omitempty\"`\n\tContent   string    `json:\"content,omitempty\"`\n\tDelta     bool      `json:\"delta,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Run `mise run fmt`. Expected: clean.\n\n### Task 3.3: Write parser tests with synthetic fixtures\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/testdata/stream_success.jsonl`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/testdata/stream_error.jsonl`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/generate_streaming_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Create success fixture (note: no terminal event — EOF is the signal):\n\n```jsonl\n{\"type\":\"init\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-15T16:00:46.999Z\",\"session_id\":\"test-session\",\"model\":\"gemini-3-flash-preview\"}\n{\"type\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-15T16:00:46.999Z\",\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"say hi\"}\n{\"type\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-15T16:00:48.211Z\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"Hello\",\"delta\":true}\n{\"type\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-15T16:00:48.311Z\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\", world.\",\"delta\":true}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Create error fixture. Gemini's actual error shape is unknown until captured. As a placeholder, use what's known to fail loudly in our parser — the stream stops after init with no assistant message:\n\n```jsonl\n{\"type\":\"init\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-15T16:00:46.999Z\",\"session_id\":\"test-session\",\"model\":\"gemini-3-flash-preview\"}\n{\"type\":\"error\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-15T16:00:47.000Z\",\"message\":\"invalid request\"}\n```\n\n(During implementation, replace this fixture with whatever Gemini actually emits when given a bad prompt or invalid model.)\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Write tests. Expected dispatcher behavior for Gemini:\n  - `init` → PhaseConnecting (1)\n  - First `message,role:assistant` → PhaseFirstToken (1) with TTFTms=0, CachedInputTokens=0\n  - Subsequent `message,role:assistant` → PhaseGenerating (N)\n  - EOF → PhaseDone (1) with `DurationMs = time.Since(start).Milliseconds()`, OutputTokens=0\n\n```go\npackage geminicli\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n)\n\nfunc TestParseGeminiStream_Success(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"testdata\", \"stream_success.jsonl\"))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"read fixture: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\n\tvar phases []agent.ProgressPhase\n\tresult, err := parseGeminiStream(bytes.NewReader(data), func(p agent.GenerationProgress) {\n\t\tphases = append(phases, p.Phase)\n\t})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tif !strings.Contains(result, \"Hello\") || !strings.Contains(result, \"world\") {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"result = %q, want concatenated assistant content\", result)\n\t}\n\n\tcounts := map[agent.ProgressPhase]int{}\n\tfor _, p := range phases {\n\t\tcounts[p]++\n\t}\n\tif counts[agent.PhaseConnecting] != 1 {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"PhaseConnecting count = %d, want 1\", counts[agent.PhaseConnecting])\n\t}\n\tif counts[agent.PhaseFirstToken] != 1 {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"PhaseFirstToken count = %d, want 1\", counts[agent.PhaseFirstToken])\n\t}\n\tif counts[agent.PhaseGenerating] < 1 {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"PhaseGenerating count = %d, want at least 1\", counts[agent.PhaseGenerating])\n\t}\n\tif counts[agent.PhaseDone] != 1 {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"PhaseDone count = %d, want 1 (emitted at EOF)\", counts[agent.PhaseDone])\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseGeminiStream_ErrorEnvelope(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"testdata\", \"stream_error.jsonl\"))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"read fixture: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t_, err = parseGeminiStream(bytes.NewReader(data), nil)\n\tif err == nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"expected error from error envelope\")\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestParseGeminiStream_EmptyStream(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\t_, err := parseGeminiStream(strings.NewReader(\"\"), nil)\n\tif err == nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(\"expected error from empty stream (no init, no assistant content)\")\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n### Task 3.4: Implement Gemini parser\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/generate_streaming.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Write:\n\n```go\npackage geminicli\n\nimport (\n\t\"bufio\"\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n)\n\nconst streamBufferMax = 4 * 1024 * 1024 // 4 MiB\n\n// parseGeminiStream consumes `gemini --output-format stream-json` NDJSON output,\n// dispatches progress callbacks, and returns the concatenated assistant\n// content. Treats stream EOF as Done (Gemini does not emit a terminal event).\nfunc parseGeminiStream(stdout io.Reader, progress agent.ProgressFn) (string, error) {\n\tscanner := bufio.NewScanner(stdout)\n\tscanner.Buffer(make([]byte, 64*1024), streamBufferMax)\n\n\tvar (\n\t\tresult          strings.Builder\n\t\tsawInit         bool\n\t\tfirstTokenFired bool\n\t\tstart           = time.Now()\n\t)\n\n\tdispatch := func(p agent.GenerationProgress) {\n\t\tif progress != nil {\n\t\t\tprogress(p)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tfor scanner.Scan() {\n\t\tline := scanner.Bytes()\n\t\tif len(line) == 0 {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tvar ev geminiStreamEvent\n\t\tif err := json.Unmarshal(line, &ev); err != nil {\n\t\t\tcontinue // best-effort: skip malformed lines\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tswitch ev.Type {\n\t\tcase \"init\":\n\t\t\tsawInit = true\n\t\t\tdispatch(agent.GenerationProgress{Phase: agent.PhaseConnecting})\n\n\t\tcase \"message\":\n\t\t\tif ev.Role != \"assistant\" {\n\t\t\t\tcontinue // ignore user-message echoes\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif !firstTokenFired {\n\t\t\t\tfirstTokenFired = true\n\t\t\t\tdispatch(agent.GenerationProgress{Phase: agent.PhaseFirstToken})\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tdispatch(agent.GenerationProgress{Phase: agent.PhaseGenerating})\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tresult.WriteString(ev.Content)\n\n\t\tcase \"error\":\n\t\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"gemini stream error: %s\", string(line))\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif err := scanner.Err(); err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"reading gemini stream: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tif !sawInit {\n\t\treturn \"\", errors.New(\"gemini stream ended without an init event\")\n\t}\n\tif !firstTokenFired {\n\t\treturn \"\", errors.New(\"gemini stream produced no assistant content\")\n\t}\n\tif progress != nil {\n\t\tdispatch(agent.GenerationProgress{\n\t\t\tPhase:      agent.PhaseDone,\n\t\t\tDurationMs: int(time.Since(start).Milliseconds()),\n\t\t\t// OutputTokens left 0 — Gemini doesn't report token counts.\n\t\t})\n\t}\n\treturn result.String(), nil\n}\n\n// GenerateTextStreaming runs `gemini --output-format stream-json -p \" \" --model\n// <model>` with the prompt piped via stdin, and dispatches progress events\n// to the optional callback. Implements agent.StreamingTextGenerator.\n//\n// If the gemini CLI rejects --output-format stream-json (older version),\n// falls back to the non-streaming GenerateText path.\nfunc (g *GeminiCLIAgent) GenerateTextStreaming(\n\tctx context.Context,\n\tprompt, model string,\n\tprogress agent.ProgressFn,\n) (string, error) {\n\ttmpl := &agent.StreamingGeneratorTemplate{\n\t\tAgentName:                 \"gemini-cli\",\n\t\tDisplayName:               \"gemini\",\n\t\tBuildCmd:                  g.buildStreamCmd,\n\t\tParser:                    parseGeminiStream,\n\t\tLooksLikeUnrecognizedFlag: looksLikeGeminiUnrecognizedFlag,\n\t}\n\n\tresult, err := tmpl.Generate(ctx, prompt, model, progress)\n\tif errors.Is(err, agent.ErrUnrecognizedStreamingFlag) {\n\t\treturn g.GenerateText(ctx, prompt, model)\n\t}\n\treturn result, err\n}\n\nfunc (g *GeminiCLIAgent) buildStreamCmd(ctx context.Context, prompt, model string) *exec.Cmd {\n\tcommandRunner := g.CommandRunner\n\tif commandRunner == nil {\n\t\tcommandRunner = exec.CommandContext\n\t}\n\targs := []string{\"--output-format\", \"stream-json\", \"-p\", \" \"}\n\tif model != \"\" {\n\t\targs = append(args, \"--model\", model)\n\t}\n\tcmd := commandRunner(ctx, \"gemini\", args...)\n\tcmd.Stdin = strings.NewReader(prompt)\n\treturn cmd\n}\n\nfunc looksLikeGeminiUnrecognizedFlag(stderr string) bool {\n\tlower := strings.ToLower(stderr)\n\thasRejectPhrase := strings.Contains(lower, \"unknown\") || strings.Contains(lower, \"unrecognized\") || strings.Contains(lower, \"invalid\")\n\tif !hasRejectPhrase {\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\treturn strings.Contains(lower, \"output-format\") || strings.Contains(lower, \"stream-json\")\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Run: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli -run TestParseGeminiStream -v`. Expected: 3 PASS.\n\n### Task 3.5: Test `GeminiCLIAgent.GenerateTextStreaming`\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/generate_streaming_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Append integration tests (same shape as Codex's Task 2.5; just substitute `gemini-cli` and use `GeminiCLIAgent`).\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Run: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli -run TestGeminiCLIGenerateTextStreaming -v`. Expected: 2 PASS.\n\n### Task 3.6: Smoke test against real Gemini CLI\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Build the local binary if not already current:\n\n```fish\ngo build -o entire ./cmd/entire\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Switch provider to Gemini and run on the standard smoke-test checkpoint (see Final verification's \"smoke checkpoint\" note for how to pick one):\n\n```fish\n./entire configure --summarize-provider gemini-cli\n./entire checkpoint explain --checkpoint <SMOKE_CHECKPOINT_ID> --generate --force\n```\n\nExpected:\n- `Generating checkpoint summary... (transcript: ..., provider: gemini-cli)`\n- `→ Sending request to provider...`\n- `→ Provider responded -- generating...` (no parens — Gemini has no TTFT/cached fields)\n- `→ Writing summary... (~Nk tokens)` (running counter from text deltas)\n- `✓ Summary generated (Xs, 0 output tokens)` (DurationMs from our wall-clock; OutputTokens=0 because Gemini doesn't report it)\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Smoke-test the timeout diagnostic:\n\n```fish\n./entire checkpoint explain --checkpoint <SMOKE_CHECKPOINT_ID> --generate --force --summary-timeout-seconds 3\n```\n\nExpected: one of the three streaming-diagnostic messages depending on how far the stream got.\n\n### Task 3.7: Verify and commit chunk 3\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Run `mise run check`. Expected: green.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Commit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/stream_response.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/generate_streaming.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/generate_streaming_test.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/testdata/\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfeat(geminicli): implement StreamingTextGenerator\n\nGemini now emits live progress events through the explain --generate UI.\nparseGeminiStream consumes `gemini --output-format stream-json -p \" \"\n--model <model>` NDJSON output and dispatches our 4 phases:\n\n- init                           → PhaseConnecting\n- first message(role:assistant)  → PhaseFirstToken (no TTFT/cached — Gemini\n  doesn't emit those fields; progress writer omits the clause gracefully)\n- subsequent assistant messages  → PhaseGenerating\n- stream EOF                     → PhaseDone (DurationMs computed locally\n  via time.Since(start); OutputTokens=0 since Gemini doesn't report)\n\nFalls back to non-streaming GenerateText if the CLI rejects the streaming\nflags.\n\nVerified end-to-end against the real gemini CLI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 4: Cursor streaming (conditional on auth)\n\n**Outcome:** `entire explain --generate` with provider `cursor` shows live progress. The `*CursorAgent` implements `StreamingTextGenerator`. Manually verified end-to-end against the real cursor (`agent`) CLI. One commit. **Skippable if auth unavailable.**\n\n### Task 4.1: Authentication gate (deterministic skip path)\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Run the auth probe:\n\n```fish\necho \"say hi\" | agent --print --output-format stream-json --stream-partial-output --force --trust --workspace /tmp 2>&1 | head -3\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Branch on the output:\n  - **If output starts with valid JSON** (e.g., `{\"type\":\"...\"}`) → cursor is authenticated. Proceed to Task 4.2.\n  - **If output contains `Authentication required` or similar credential error** → cursor is NOT available. **SKIP all of Chunk 4** entirely. Document in the PR description's \"Known gaps\" section: \"Cursor streaming deferred — `agent` CLI requires interactive `agent login` or `CURSOR_API_KEY`. Framework supports adding it in a follow-up PR. Test against real cursor CLI is the only blocker.\" Proceed directly to Chunk 5.\n\nThis branch must be deterministic — a subagent cannot push through with a half-finished implementation. Either auth works and the full chunk runs, or the chunk is skipped wholesale.\n\n### Task 4.2: Capture real Cursor stream format\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Capture (only reached if Task 4.1 found auth):\n\n```fish\necho \"say hi in 5 words\" | agent --print --output-format stream-json --stream-partial-output --force --trust --workspace /tmp > /tmp/cursor-real.jsonl 2>&1\ncat /tmp/cursor-real.jsonl\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Inspect the event schema. Cursor's `--help` documents `--stream-partial-output` as producing \"individual text deltas\" — expect a message-start equivalent, content deltas, and a message-stop. Note the actual event types, the field names for the assistant's text deltas, and any terminal/usage event.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Decide the dispatch table based on observation. Common shapes seen across LLM CLIs:\n  - Some event marks request-sent → `PhaseConnecting`\n  - First assistant-text-bearing event → `PhaseFirstToken`\n  - Subsequent assistant deltas → `PhaseGenerating`\n  - Terminal event (or EOF) → `PhaseDone`\n\n  If the captured stream closely matches Claude's `stream_event,event.type` envelope, the dispatch logic from claudecode's `makeProgressDispatcher` is the right starting point.\n\n### Task 4.3-4.7: Mirror Chunks 2-3's structure\n\nOnce the event schema is documented (Task 4.2):\n\n- **4.3** — `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/stream_response.go` with the captured event struct.\n- **4.4** — `testdata/stream_success.jsonl` (synthetic, modeled on captured shape) + `stream_error.jsonl`.\n- **4.5** — `parseCursorStream` mirroring `parseGeminiStream`/`parseCodexStream`; **explicitly handle EOF-without-terminal-event** (treat EOF as Done with locally-computed duration if no usage event is observed).\n- **4.6** — `(*CursorAgent).GenerateTextStreaming` using `StreamingGeneratorTemplate` with `looksLikeCursorUnrecognizedFlag`. **Falls back to `c.GenerateText` on `ErrUnrecognizedStreamingFlag`** (same pattern as Codex/Gemini).\n\n**BuildCmd:**\n\n```go\nargs := []string{\"--print\", \"--force\", \"--trust\", \"--workspace\", os.TempDir(), \"--output-format\", \"stream-json\", \"--stream-partial-output\"}\nif model != \"\" { args = append(args, \"--model\", model) }\ncmd := commandRunner(ctx, \"agent\", args...)\ncmd.Stdin = strings.NewReader(prompt)\n```\n\n- **4.7** — Smoke test against real `agent`:\n  ```fish\n  ./entire configure --summarize-provider cursor\n  ./entire checkpoint explain --checkpoint <SMOKE_CHECKPOINT_ID> --generate --force\n  ```\n  Confirm phase events render and final summary content is non-empty.\n\n- **4.8** — `mise run check`; commit `feat(cursor): implement StreamingTextGenerator`.\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 5: Copilot streaming\n\n**Outcome:** `entire explain --generate` with provider `copilot-cli` shows live progress. The `*CopilotCLIAgent` implements `StreamingTextGenerator`. Manually verified end-to-end against the real `copilot` CLI. One commit.\n\n### Task 5.1: Verify Copilot CLI args match the existing non-streaming path\n\nThe existing `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/generate.go` documents the rationale for `--allow-all-tools --disable-builtin-mcps`:\n\n> `--allow-all-tools` is required for non-interactive mode; `--disable-builtin-mcps` skips loading the GitHub MCP server that isn't needed for summary text generation and reduces per-call input tokens.\n\nThe streaming path keeps these flags (matching non-streaming behavior — diverging here would create two flag profiles to maintain).\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Verify by reading `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/generate.go` and confirming the args list. If a future PR removes these flags from the non-streaming path, the streaming path should track that change.\n\n### Task 5.2: Capture real Copilot stream format\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Capture:\n\n```fish\necho \"say hi in 5 words\" | copilot --output-format json --stream on --allow-all-tools --disable-builtin-mcps > /tmp/copilot-real.jsonl 2>&1\ncat /tmp/copilot-real.jsonl\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Expected event shape (per pre-plan investigation):\n  - `{\"type\":\"session.mcp_servers_loaded\", ...}` — ignored\n  - `{\"type\":\"session.skills_loaded\", ...}` — ignored\n  - `{\"type\":\"session.tools_updated\",\"data\":{\"model\":\"...\"},...}` — ignored (model info)\n  - `{\"type\":\"user.message\", ...}` — ignored (echo)\n  - `{\"type\":\"assistant.turn_start\",\"data\":{\"turnId\":\"...\"}, ...}` — Connecting candidate\n  - `{\"type\":\"assistant.message_delta\",\"data\":{\"messageId\":\"...\",\"deltaContent\":\"...\"},...}` — chunked\n  - Terminal event TBD: likely `assistant.turn_end` or `assistant.message_complete`. **Capture the actual name and confirm whether it carries usage.**\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** If the captured stream lacks a clear terminal event, the parser falls back to EOF-as-Done (same as Gemini), computing duration locally and setting OutputTokens=0.\n\n### Task 5.3: Define Copilot stream-event types\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/stream_response.go`\n\n```go\npackage copilotcli\n\nimport \"time\"\n\ntype copilotStreamEvent struct {\n\tType      string             `json:\"type\"`\n\tTimestamp time.Time          `json:\"timestamp,omitempty\"`\n\tData      *copilotStreamData `json:\"data,omitempty\"`\n\tID        string             `json:\"id,omitempty\"`\n\tParentID  string             `json:\"parentId,omitempty\"`\n\tEphemeral bool               `json:\"ephemeral,omitempty\"`\n}\n\ntype copilotStreamData struct {\n\tMessageID    string `json:\"messageId,omitempty\"`\n\tTurnID       string `json:\"turnId,omitempty\"`\n\tDeltaContent string `json:\"deltaContent,omitempty\"`\n\tModel        string `json:\"model,omitempty\"`\n\t// Additional fields based on actual captured terminal event:\n\t// Usage *copilotUsage `json:\"usage,omitempty\"`  // if Copilot emits usage\n}\n```\n\n(Update fields after Task 5.2 captures the real shape.)\n\n### Task 5.4: Write parser tests with synthetic fixtures\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/testdata/stream_success.jsonl`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/testdata/stream_error.jsonl`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/generate_streaming_test.go`\n\nTest assertions:\n- `PhaseConnecting` count = 1 (from `assistant.turn_start`)\n- `PhaseFirstToken` count = 1 (from first `assistant.message_delta`)\n- `PhaseGenerating` count ≥ 1 (subsequent deltas)\n- `PhaseDone` count = 1 (either from terminal event OR EOF fallback)\n- Result text is the concatenation of all `data.deltaContent` values.\n\n### Task 5.5: Implement Copilot parser\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/generate_streaming.go`\n\nDispatch table:\n- `assistant.turn_start` → `PhaseConnecting`\n- First `assistant.message_delta` → `PhaseFirstToken` (no TTFT field — confirm during Task 5