{"parentUuid":"6637c74e-83b1-4c44-8c3a-1525a5d550f2","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/peytonmontei/.claude/projects/-Users-peytonmontei-Documents-entire-devenv-entireio-cli/memory/feedback_few_commits_per_pr.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/peytonmontei/.claude/projects/-Users-peytonmontei-Documents-entire-devenv-entireio-cli/memory/feedback_few_commits_per_pr.md","content":"---\nname: Limit commits per PR — group work into logical commits\ndescription: User cares about avoiding *unnecessary* commits proposed in a plan (TDD-step-per-commit clutter), NOT a hard cap on commit count. Real work added during execution stays as its own commit.\ntype: feedback\noriginSessionId: e3d7584b-083c-4342-8757-bc0dd5816063\n---\nThe rule is **about plans, not absolute count**. Don't propose unnecessary commits in a plan (e.g., one per TDD step). Group plan tasks into logical commits at meaningful boundaries (helpers, surface rewrites, error paths, test sweep). But **commits added during execution for real distinct work — review-response fixes, CI-failure fixes, smoke-test bug fixes, scope additions — stay as their own commits**. Don't pre-emptively suggest squashing those.\n\n**Why:** Originally observed 2026-04-30: \"limit the number of commits for this plan, we don't need a bunch to clutter pr.\" Reconfirmed 2026-05-15 on PR #964: \"leave as 5 commits i don't really care about final number of commits only when there are unnecessary ones proposed in a plan.\" The first comment was about planning, not execution. The user values clear commit boundaries — each commit should represent one logical unit of work the reviewer can understand independently. Adding a 4th, 5th, 6th commit during execution is fine when it represents real distinct work.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- When writing plans (superpowers:writing-plans): collapse per-TDD-step commit lines into logical-boundary commits. Authoring as \"test → implement → commit per task\" is fine for the implementer's mental model, but the commit step should fire at chunk boundaries, not per task.\n- During execution (subagent-driven-development): tell the implementer to skip per-task commits. The controller stages multiple completed tasks and commits at logical breakpoints.\n- Don't pre-emptively squash commits added during a PR's life cycle (smoke-test fixes, review-response fixes, CI-failure fixes). Each is its own logical unit.\n- Don't propose final squash plans without being asked. If asked, group at the logical-unit level.\n- Bisectability is still a goal — keep each commit independently buildable and testable.\n","numLines":17,"startLine":1,"totalLines":17}},"displayPath":"../../../../../../../.claude/projects/-Users-peytonmontei-Documents-entire-devenv-entireio-cli/memory/feedback_few_commits_per_pr.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ecddf5a5-d510-420d-81df-dec6a7217fe3","timestamp":"2026-05-15T17:55:57.267Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact-2","sessionId":"4944fa51-d7dd-4310-b62f-7802a196cd45","version":"2.1.140","gitBranch":"redact-2","slug":"functional-forging-tiger"}
