n/main`.\n12\t\n13\t**Before starting,** check whether PR #964 has merged to main:\n14\t\n15\t```fish\n16\tgit fetch origin main\n17\tgit log --oneline origin/main | grep -F \"explain): live progress and observable-state timeout diagnostic\" | head -3\n18\t```\n19\t\n20\t- **If PR #964 IS merged** to main (the commit message appears in `origin/main`'s history): branch the new worktree off `origin/main` as usual.\n21\t- **If PR #964 is NOT yet merged**: branch off the PR's tip ref instead, via @superpowers:using-git-worktrees with a custom base:\n22\t\n23\t```fish\n24\tgit fetch origin feat/explain-stream-progress\n25\tgit worktree add .worktrees/non-claude-streaming -b feat/non-claude-streaming origin/feat/explain-stream-progress\n26\t```\n27\t\n28\tThen `cd .worktrees/non-claude-streaming` and proceed. Once PR #964 lands on main, a `git rebase origin/main` will cleanly pick up any conflict-free changes; the new commits sit on top.\n29\t\n30\t**Cost note:** Each per-agent smoke test step makes a real API call against that agent's provider.\n31\t\n32\tTo bound cost, pick **one specific small checkpoint** before starting Chunk 2 and reuse it across all per-agent smoke tests. Use `entire checkpoint list` to find a small committed checkpoint with a short transcript (under 50 KB if possible); record its 12-char ID and refer to it as `<SMOKE_CHECKPOINT_ID>` throughout the plan. A small checkpoint × 4 agents × 2 tests each ≈ $0.50–$2.00 total. Without this discipline the cost can balloon if the implementer picks different (large) checkpoints per agent.\n33\t\n34\t---\n35\t\n36\t## File Structure\n37\t\n38\t**Create:**\n39\t- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/streaming_template.go` — `StreamingGeneratorTemplate` struct + its `Generate` method (subprocess lifecycle).\n40\t- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/streaming_template_test.go` — unit tests for the template using the shared `fakeStreamCmd`.\n41\t- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil/streaming.go` — `FakeStreamCmd`, `BuildFakeShellScript` helpers 