out pipe: %w\", t.AgentName, err)\n240\t\t}\n241\t\tvar stderr bytes.Buffer\n242\t\tcmd.Stderr = &stderr\n243\t\n244\t\tif err := cmd.Start(); err != nil {\n245\t\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"%s stream start: %w\", t.AgentName, err)\n246\t\t}\n247\t\n248\t\t// stdoutBytes counts what the subprocess actually produced — used by the\n249\t\t// timeout-diagnostic path to distinguish \"produced no output\" from \"was\n250\t\t// generating when killed\". The counting reader passes bytes through to\n251\t\t// the parser unchanged.\n252\t\tcounter := &countingReader{r: stdout}\n253\t\tresult, parseErr := t.Parser(counter, progress)\n254\t\n255\t\t// Drain any unread stdout so the subprocess can exit cleanly even if\n256\t\t// the parser aborted early. The discard isn't tracked because we don't\n257\t\t// count post-parser bytes toward the diagnostic.\n258\t\tif _, drainErr := io.Copy(io.Discard, stdout); drainErr != nil {\n259\t\t\tlogging.Debug(ctx, \"draining stream stdout\",\n260\t\t\t\tslog.String(\"agent\", t.AgentName),\n261\t\t\t\tslog.String(\"error\", drainErr.Error()))\n262\t\t}\n263\t\twaitErr := cmd.Wait()\n264\t\n265\t\t// ctx cancellation takes precedence over parser/wait errors so callers\n266\t\t// see context.DeadlineExceeded / Canceled cleanly when applicable.\n267\t\tif ctx.Err() != nil {\n268\t\t\tstderrStr := strings.TrimSpace(stderr.String())\n269\t\t\treturn \"\", &TextGenerationError{\n270\t\t\t\tErr:         ctx.Err(),\n271\t\t\t\tStderr:      stderrStr,\n272\t\t\t\tStdoutBytes: counter.n,\n273\t\t\t}\n274\t\t}\n275\t\n276\t\tif parseErr == nil && waitErr == nil {\n277\t\t\treturn result, nil\n278\t\t}\n279\t\n280\t\t// Old-CLI fallback: only fires when the subprocess exited non-zero AND\n281\t\t// stderr matches the per-agent fallback detector. Parser errors don't\n282\t\t// trigger this; only the CLI's own rejection of streaming flags does.\n283\t\tstderrStr := strings.TrimSpace(stderr.String())\n284\t\tif waitErr != nil && t.LooksLikeUnrecognizedFlag != nil && t.LooksLikeUnrecognizedFlag(stderrStr) {\n285\t\t\tlogging.Warn(ctx, \"CLI rejected streaming flags; caller should fall back to non-streaming\",\n286\t\t\t\tslog.String(\"agent\", t.AgentName),\n287\t\t\t\tslog.String(\"stderr\", stderrStr))\n288\t\t\treturn \"\", ErrUnrecognizedStreamingFlag\n289\t\t}\n290\t\n291\t\t// Compose the error: parser failure wins if waitErr is nil; otherwise\n292\t\t// the wait error (which carries the exit code) wins. Both are wrapped\n293\t\t// into *TextGenerationError so the explain layer's diagnostic can read\n294\t\t// stderr.\n295\t\twrappedErr := waitErr\n296\t\tif wrappedErr == nil {\n297\t\t\twrappedErr = parseErr\n298\t\t}\n299\t\treturn \"\", &TextGenerationError{\n300\t\t\tErr:         fmt.Errorf(\"%s stream failed: %w\", t.AgentName, wrappedErr),\n301\t\t\tStderr:      stderrStr,\n302\t\t\tStdoutBytes: counter.n,\n303\t\t}\n304\t}\n305\t\n306\t// countingReader passes bytes through and counts them. Used by the template\n307\t// so the diagnostic path can ask \"did the subprocess produce any output?\".\n308\ttype countingReader struct {\n309\t\tr io.Reader\n310\t\tn int\n311\t}\n312\t\n313\tfunc (c *countingReader) Read(p []byte) (int, error) {\n314\t\tn, err := c.r.Read(p)\n315\t\tc.n += n\n316\t\treturn n, err\n317\t}\n318\t```\n319\t\n320\t- [ ] **Step 2:** Run `mise run fmt && mise run lint`. Expected: clean.\n321\t\n322\t### Task 1.3: Test `StreamingGeneratorTemplate`\n323\t\n324\t**Files:**\n325\t- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/streaming_template_test.go`\n326\t\n327\t- [ ] **Step 1:** Write tests:\n328\t\n329\t```go\n330\tpackage agent_test\n331\t\n332\timport (\n333\t\t\"context\"\n334\t\t\"errors\"\n335\t\t\"io\"\n336\t\t\"os/exec\"\n337\t\t\"strings\"\n338\t\t\"testing\"\n339\t\n340\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n341\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/testutil\"\n342\t)\n343\t\n344\tfunc TestStreamingGeneratorTemplate_Generate_Success(t *testing.T) {\n345\t\tt.Par